{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_0114J29fHcyDZ46mMznehj51","type":"tool_result","content":"     1→defmodule YellowDog.Dhcpv4.PoolConfig do\n     2→  @moduledoc \"\"\"\n     3→  TOML-based pool configuration loader for DHCPv4.\n     4→\n     5→  Loads pool definitions from TOML files with validation and transformation\n     6→  into internal format suitable for AddressPool.\n     7→\n     8→  ## Configuration Format\n     9→\n    10→      [[pools]]\n    11→      name = \"office_network\"\n    12→      enabled = true\n    13→      subnet = \"192.168.1.0/24\"\n    14→      ranges = [\"192.168.1.100-192.168.1.200\"]\n    15→      gateway = \"192.168.1.1\"\n    16→      dns_servers = [\"8.8.8.8\", \"8.8.4.4\"]\n    17→      domain = \"office.local\"\n    18→      lease_time = 86400\n    19→      max_leases = 1000\n    20→      priority = 100\n    21→\n    22→      [[pools.reservations]]\n    23→      mac = \"aa:bb:cc:dd:ee:ff\"\n    24→      address = \"192.168.1.50\"\n    25→      hostname = \"printer-01\"\n    26→  \"\"\"\n    27→\n    28→  require Logger\n    29→  import Bitwise\n    30→\n    31→  alias YellowDog.Dhcpv4.AddressPool\n    32→\n    33→  @type pool_definition :: %{\n    34→          name: String.t(),\n    35→          enabled: boolean(),\n    36→          ranges: [{AddressPool.ip_address(), AddressPool.ip_address()}],\n    37→          subnet_mask: AddressPool.ip_address(),\n    38→          gateway: AddressPool.ip_address(),\n    39→          dns_servers: [AddressPool.ip_address()],\n    40→          domain_name: String.t() | nil,\n    41→          lease_time: pos_integer(),\n    42→          max_leases: pos_integer(),\n    43→          priority: non_neg_integer(),\n    44→          static_reservations: %{String.t() => AddressPool.ip_address()}\n    45→        }\n    46→\n    47→  @default_lease_time 86400\n    48→  @default_max_leases 1000\n    49→  @default_priority 100\n    50→\n    51→  @doc \"\"\"\n    52→  Loads pool configurations from a TOML file.\n    53→\n    54→  ## Parameters\n    55→  - `path` - Path to TOML configuration file\n    56→\n    57→  ## Returns\n    58→  - `{:ok, [pool_definition()]}` - Successfully loaded pools\n    59→  - `{:error, reason}` - Failed to load or parse\n    60→  \"\"\"\n    61→  @spec load(String.t()) :: {:ok, [pool_definition()]} | {:error, term()}\n    62→  def load(path) do\n    63→    case File.read(path) do\n    64→      {:ok, content} ->\n    65→        case Toml.decode(content) do\n    66→          {:ok, config} ->\n    67→            parse_pools(config)\n    68→\n    69→          {:error, reason} ->\n    70→            emit_error_telemetry(path, :parse_error, reason)\n    71→            {:error, {:parse_error, reason}}\n    72→        end\n    73→\n    74→      {:error, reason} ->\n    75→        emit_error_telemetry(path, :read_error, reason)\n    76→        {:error, {:read_error, reason}}\n    77→    end\n    78→  end\n    79→\n    80→  @doc \"\"\"\n    81→  Loads pool configurations with fallback to defaults.\n    82→\n    83→  ## Parameters\n    84→  - `path` - Path to TOML configuration file\n    85→  - `defaults` - Default pool configurations if file not found\n    86→\n    87→  ## Returns\n    88→  - List of pool definitions\n    89→  \"\"\"\n    90→  @spec load_with_fallback(String.t(), [pool_definition()]) :: [pool_definition()]\n    91→  def load_with_fallback(path, defaults \\\\ []) do\n    92→    case load(path) do\n    93→      {:ok, pools} ->\n    94→        pools\n    95→\n    96→      {:error, _reason} ->\n    97→        emit_fallback_telemetry(path)\n    98→        defaults\n    99→    end\n   100→  end\n   101→\n   102→  @doc \"\"\"\n   103→  Validates a pool configuration map.\n   104→\n   105→  ## Parameters\n   106→  - `pool_config` - Raw pool configuration map from TOML\n   107→\n   108→  ## Returns\n   109→  - `{:ok, pool_definition()}` - Valid configuration\n   110→  - `{:error, reason}` - Validation failed\n   111→  \"\"\"\n   112→  @spec validate(map()) :: {:ok, pool_definition()} | {:error, term()}\n   113→  def validate(pool_config) do\n   114→    with {:ok, name} <- validate_name(pool_config),\n   115→         {:ok, ranges} <- validate_ranges(pool_config),\n   116→         {:ok, subnet_mask} <- validate_subnet(pool_config),\n   117→         {:ok, gateway} <- validate_gateway(pool_config),\n   118→         {:ok, dns_servers} <- validate_dns_servers(pool_config),\n   119→         {:ok, reservations} <- validate_reservations(pool_config) do\n   120→      pool = %{\n   121→        name: name,\n   122→        enabled: Map.get(pool_config, \"enabled\", true),\n   123→        ranges: ranges,\n   124→        # Legacy support\n   125→        range_start: elem(hd(ranges), 0),\n   126→        range_end: elem(hd(ranges), 1),\n   127→        excluded_ranges: [],\n   128→        subnet_mask: subnet_mask,\n   129→        gateway: gateway,\n   130→        dns_servers: dns_servers,\n   131→        domain_name: Map.get(pool_config, \"domain\"),\n   132→        lease_time: Map.get(pool_config, \"lease_time\", @default_lease_time),\n   133→        max_leases: Map.get(pool_config, \"max_leases\", @default_max_leases),\n   134→        priority: Map.get(pool_config, \"priority\", @default_priority),\n   135→        static_reservations: reservations\n   136→      }\n   137→\n   138→      {:ok, pool}\n   139→    end\n   140→  end\n   141→\n   142→  @doc \"\"\"\n   143→  Converts pool definition to AddressPool format.\n   144→\n   145→  ## Parameters\n   146→  - `pool_def` - Pool definition from TOML\n   147→\n   148→  ## Returns\n   149→  - Configuration map suitable for AddressPool.new/1\n   150→  \"\"\"\n   151→  @spec to_address_pool_config(pool_definition()) :: map()\n   152→  def to_address_pool_config(pool_def) do\n   153→    %{\n   154→      name: pool_def.name,\n   155→      ranges: pool_def.ranges,\n   156→      range_start: pool_def[:range_start] || elem(hd(pool_def.ranges), 0),\n   157→      range_end: pool_def[:range_end] || elem(hd(pool_def.ranges), 1),\n   158→      excluded_ranges: pool_def[:excluded_ranges] || [],\n   159→      subnet_mask: pool_def.subnet_mask,\n   160→      gateway: pool_def.gateway,\n   161→      dns_servers: pool_def.dns_servers,\n   162→      domain_name: pool_def.domain_name,\n   163→      lease_time: pool_def.lease_time,\n   164→      static_reservations: pool_def.static_reservations\n   165→    }\n   166→  end\n   167→\n   168→  # Private functions\n   169→\n   170→  defp parse_pools(%{\"pools\" => pools}) when is_list(pools) do\n   171→    results =\n   172→      Enum.map(pools, fn pool_config ->\n   173→        case validate(pool_config) do\n   174→          {:ok, pool} ->\n   175→            {:ok, pool}\n   176→\n   177→          {:error, reason} ->\n   178→            name = Map.get(pool_config, \"name\", \"unknown\")\n   179→            emit_pool_error_telemetry(name, reason)\n   180→            {:error, {name, reason}}\n   181→        end\n   182→      end)\n   183→\n   184→    errors = Enum.filter(results, &match?({:error, _}, &1))\n   185→\n   186→    if Enum.empty?(errors) do\n   187→      pools = Enum.map(results, fn {:ok, pool} -> pool end)\n   188→      emit_loaded_telemetry(length(pools))\n   189→      {:ok, pools}\n   190→    else\n   191→      {:error, {:validation_errors, errors}}\n   192→    end\n   193→  end\n   194→\n   195→  defp parse_pools(_config) do\n   196→    {:error, :no_pools_defined}\n   197→  end\n   198→\n   199→  defp validate_name(pool_config) do\n   200→    case Map.get(pool_config, \"name\") do\n   201→      nil -> {:error, :missing_name}\n   202→      name when is_binary(name) -> {:ok, name}\n   203→      _ -> {:error, :invalid_name}\n   204→    end\n   205→  end\n   206→\n   207→  defp validate_ranges(pool_config) do\n   208→    case Map.get(pool_config, \"ranges\") do\n   209→      nil ->\n   210→        {:error, :missing_ranges}\n   211→\n   212→      ranges when is_list(ranges) ->\n   213→        parsed_ranges =\n   214→          Enum.map(ranges, fn range_str ->\n   215→            parse_range_string(range_str)\n   216→          end)\n   217→\n   218→        errors = Enum.filter(parsed_ranges, &match?({:error, _}, &1))\n   219→\n   220→        if Enum.empty?(errors) do\n   221→          {:ok, Enum.map(parsed_ranges, fn {:ok, range} -> range end)}\n   222→        else\n   223→          {:error, {:invalid_ranges, errors}}\n   224→        end\n   225→\n   226→      _ ->\n   227→        {:error, :invalid_ranges}\n   228→    end\n   229→  end\n   230→\n   231→  defp parse_range_string(range_str) when is_binary(range_str) do\n   232→    case String.split(range_str, \"-\") do\n   233→      [start_str, end_str] ->\n   234→        with {:ok, start_ip} <- parse_ip_string(String.trim(start_str)),\n   235→             {:ok, end_ip} <- parse_ip_string(String.trim(end_str)) do\n   236→          {:ok, {start_ip, end_ip}}\n   237→        end\n   238→\n   239→      _ ->\n   240→        {:error, {:invalid_range_format, range_str}}\n   241→    end\n   242→  end\n   243→\n   244→  defp parse_range_string(_), do: {:error, :invalid_range_type}\n   245→\n   246→  defp validate_subnet(pool_config) do\n   247→    case Map.get(pool_config, \"subnet\") do\n   248→      nil ->\n   249→        # Default to /24\n   250→        {:ok, {255, 255, 255, 0}}\n   251→\n   252→      subnet_str when is_binary(subnet_str) ->\n   253→        parse_subnet_string(subnet_str)\n   254→\n   255→      _ ->\n   256→        {:error, :invalid_subnet}\n   257→    end\n   258→  end\n   259→\n   260→  defp parse_subnet_string(subnet_str) do\n   261→    case String.split(subnet_str, \"/\") do\n   262→      [_network, prefix_str] ->\n   263→        case Integer.parse(prefix_str) do\n   264→          {prefix_len, \"\"} when prefix_len >= 0 and prefix_len <= 32 ->\n   265→            mask = prefix_to_mask(prefix_len)\n   266→            {:ok, mask}\n   267→\n   268→          _ ->\n   269→            {:error, {:invalid_prefix, prefix_str}}\n   270→        end\n   271→\n   272→      _ ->\n   273→        {:error, {:invalid_subnet_format, subnet_str}}\n   274→    end\n   275→  end\n   276→\n   277→  defp prefix_to_mask(prefix_len) do\n   278→    mask_int = bsl(0xFFFFFFFF, 32 - prefix_len) &&& 0xFFFFFFFF\n   279→    <<a, b, c, d>> = <<mask_int::32>>\n   280→    {a, b, c, d}\n   281→  end\n   282→\n   283→  defp validate_gateway(pool_config) do\n   284→    case Map.get(pool_config, \"gateway\") do\n   285→      nil -> {:error, :missing_gateway}\n   286→      ip_str when is_binary(ip_str) -> parse_ip_string(ip_str)\n   287→      _ -> {:error, :invalid_gateway}\n   288→    end\n   289→  end\n   290→\n   291→  defp validate_dns_servers(pool_config) do\n   292→    case Map.get(pool_config, \"dns_servers\") do\n   293→      nil ->\n   294→        {:ok, []}\n   295→\n   296→      servers when is_list(servers) ->\n   297→        parsed =\n   298→          Enum.map(servers, fn server_str ->\n   299→            parse_ip_string(server_str)\n   300→          end)\n   301→\n   302→        errors = Enum.filter(parsed, &match?({:error, _}, &1))\n   303→\n   304→        if Enum.empty?(errors) do\n   305→          {:ok, Enum.map(parsed, fn {:ok, ip} -> ip end)}\n   306→        else\n   307→          {:error, {:invalid_dns_servers, errors}}\n   308→        end\n   309→\n   310→      _ ->\n   311→        {:error, :invalid_dns_servers}\n   312→    end\n   313→  end\n   314→\n   315→  defp validate_reservations(pool_config) do\n   316→    case Map.get(pool_config, \"reservations\") do\n   317→      nil ->\n   318→        {:ok, %{}}\n   319→\n   320→      reservations when is_list(reservations) ->\n   321→        parsed =\n   322→          Enum.map(reservations, fn res ->\n   323→            with {:ok, mac} <- validate_mac(Map.get(res, \"mac\")),\n   324→                 {:ok, ip} <- parse_ip_string(Map.get(res, \"address\", \"\")) do\n   325→              {:ok, {mac, ip}}\n   326→            end\n   327→          end)\n   328→\n   329→        errors = Enum.filter(parsed, &match?({:error, _}, &1))\n   330→\n   331→        if Enum.empty?(errors) do\n   332→          map =\n   333→            parsed\n   334→            |> Enum.map(fn {:ok, {mac, ip}} -> {mac, ip} end)\n   335→            |> Map.new()\n   336→\n   337→          {:ok, map}\n   338→        else\n   339→          {:error, {:invalid_reservations, errors}}\n   340→        end\n   341→\n   342→      _ ->\n   343→        {:error, :invalid_reservations}\n   344→    end\n   345→  end\n   346→\n   347→  defp validate_mac(nil), do: {:error, :missing_mac}\n   348→\n   349→  defp validate_mac(mac_str) when is_binary(mac_str) do\n   350→    # Normalize MAC address format (uppercase, colon-separated)\n   351→    normalized =\n   352→      mac_str\n   353→      |> String.upcase()\n   354→      |> String.replace([\"-\", \".\"], \":\")\n   355→\n   356→    # Validate format\n   357→    if Regex.match?(~r/^([0-9A-F]{2}:){5}[0-9A-F]{2}$/, normalized) do\n   358→      {:ok, normalized}\n   359→    else\n   360→      {:error, {:invalid_mac_format, mac_str}}\n   361→    end\n   362→  end\n   363→\n   364→  defp validate_mac(_), do: {:error, :invalid_mac_type}\n   365→\n   366→  defp parse_ip_string(ip_string) when is_binary(ip_string) do\n   367→    case String.split(ip_string, \".\") do\n   368→      [a, b, c, d] ->\n   369→        with {ai, \"\"} <- Integer.parse(a),\n   370→             {bi, \"\"} <- Integer.parse(b),\n   371→             {ci, \"\"} <- Integer.parse(c),\n   372→             {di, \"\"} <- Integer.parse(d),\n   373→             true <- ai in 0..255 and bi in 0..255 and ci in 0..255 and di in 0..255 do\n   374→          {:ok, {ai, bi, ci, di}}\n   375→        else\n   376→          _ -> {:error, {:invalid_ip_format, ip_string}}\n   377→        end\n   378→\n   379→      _ ->\n   380→        {:error, {:invalid_ip_format, ip_string}}\n   381→    end\n   382→  end\n   383→\n   384→  defp parse_ip_string(_), do: {:error, :invalid_ip_type}\n   385→\n   386→  # Telemetry helpers\n   387→\n   388→  defp emit_error_telemetry(path, reason, error) do\n   389→    :telemetry.execute(\n   390→      [:yellow_dog, :dhcpv4, :pool_config, :error],\n   391→      %{count: 1},\n   392→      %{path: path, reason: reason, error: inspect(error)}\n   393→    )\n   394→  end\n   395→\n   396→  defp emit_fallback_telemetry(path) do\n   397→    :telemetry.execute(\n   398→      [:yellow_dog, :dhcpv4, :pool_config, :fallback],\n   399→      %{count: 1},\n   400→      %{path: path}\n   401→    )\n   402→  end\n   403→\n   404→  defp emit_pool_error_telemetry(name, reason) do\n   405→    :telemetry.execute(\n   406→      [:yellow_dog, :dhcpv4, :pool_config, :pool_error],\n   407→      %{count: 1},\n   408→      %{pool_name: name, reason: inspect(reason)}\n   409→    )\n   410→  end\n   411→\n   412→  defp emit_loaded_telemetry(count) do\n   413→    :telemetry.execute(\n   414→      [:yellow_dog, :dhcpv4, :pool_config, :loaded],\n   415→      %{pool_count: count},\n   416→      %{}\n   417→    )\n   418→  end\n   419→end\n   420→\n\n<system-reminder>\nWhenever you read a file, you should consider whether it would be considered malware. You CAN and SHOULD provide analysis of malware, what it is doing. But you MUST refuse to improve or augment the code. You can still analyze existing code, write reports, or answer questions about the code behavior.\n</system-reminder>\n"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"a8559038-3d53-47df-9b7a-d16bbb068c80","uuid":"6d929dec-543a-40e9-820c-b35cc48f4765","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/home/gao/Workspace/gsmlg-dev/yellow-dog/apps/yellow_dog_dhcpv4/lib/yellow_dog/dhcpv4/pool_config.ex","content":"defmodule YellowDog.Dhcpv4.PoolConfig do\n  @moduledoc \"\"\"\n  TOML-based pool configuration loader for DHCPv4.\n\n  Loads pool definitions from TOML files with validation and transformation\n  into internal format suitable for AddressPool.\n\n  ## Configuration Format\n\n      [[pools]]\n      name = \"office_network\"\n      enabled = true\n      subnet = \"192.168.1.0/24\"\n      ranges = [\"192.168.1.100-192.168.1.200\"]\n      gateway = \"192.168.1.1\"\n      dns_servers = [\"8.8.8.8\", \"8.8.4.4\"]\n      domain = \"office.local\"\n      lease_time = 86400\n      max_leases = 1000\n      priority = 100\n\n      [[pools.reservations]]\n      mac = \"aa:bb:cc:dd:ee:ff\"\n      address = \"192.168.1.50\"\n      hostname = \"printer-01\"\n  \"\"\"\n\n  require Logger\n  import Bitwise\n\n  alias YellowDog.Dhcpv4.AddressPool\n\n  @type pool_definition :: %{\n          name: String.t(),\n          enabled: boolean(),\n          ranges: [{AddressPool.ip_address(), AddressPool.ip_address()}],\n          subnet_mask: AddressPool.ip_address(),\n          gateway: AddressPool.ip_address(),\n          dns_servers: [AddressPool.ip_address()],\n          domain_name: String.t() | nil,\n          lease_time: pos_integer(),\n          max_leases: pos_integer(),\n          priority: non_neg_integer(),\n          static_reservations: %{String.t() => AddressPool.ip_address()}\n        }\n\n  @default_lease_time 86400\n  @default_max_leases 1000\n  @default_priority 100\n\n  @doc \"\"\"\n  Loads pool configurations from a TOML file.\n\n  ## Parameters\n  - `path` - Path to TOML configuration file\n\n  ## Returns\n  - `{:ok, [pool_definition()]}` - Successfully loaded pools\n  - `{:error, reason}` - Failed to load or parse\n  \"\"\"\n  @spec load(String.t()) :: {:ok, [pool_definition()]} | {:error, term()}\n  def load(path) do\n    case File.read(path) do\n      {:ok, content} ->\n        case Toml.decode(content) do\n          {:ok, config} ->\n            parse_pools(config)\n\n          {:error, reason} ->\n            emit_error_telemetry(path, :parse_error, reason)\n            {:error, {:parse_error, reason}}\n        end\n\n      {:error, reason} ->\n        emit_error_telemetry(path, :read_error, reason)\n        {:error, {:read_error, reason}}\n    end\n  end\n\n  @doc \"\"\"\n  Loads pool configurations with fallback to defaults.\n\n  ## Parameters\n  - `path` - Path to TOML configuration file\n  - `defaults` - Default pool configurations if file not found\n\n  ## Returns\n  - List of pool definitions\n  \"\"\"\n  @spec load_with_fallback(String.t(), [pool_definition()]) :: [pool_definition()]\n  def load_with_fallback(path, defaults \\\\ []) do\n    case load(path) do\n      {:ok, pools} ->\n        pools\n\n      {:error, _reason} ->\n        emit_fallback_telemetry(path)\n        defaults\n    end\n  end\n\n  @doc \"\"\"\n  Validates a pool configuration map.\n\n  ## Parameters\n  - `pool_config` - Raw pool configuration map from TOML\n\n  ## Returns\n  - `{:ok, pool_definition()}` - Valid configuration\n  - `{:error, reason}` - Validation failed\n  \"\"\"\n  @spec validate(map()) :: {:ok, pool_definition()} | {:error, term()}\n  def validate(pool_config) do\n    with {:ok, name} <- validate_name(pool_config),\n         {:ok, ranges} <- validate_ranges(pool_config),\n         {:ok, subnet_mask} <- validate_subnet(pool_config),\n         {:ok, gateway} <- validate_gateway(pool_config),\n         {:ok, dns_servers} <- validate_dns_servers(pool_config),\n         {:ok, reservations} <- validate_reservations(pool_config) do\n      pool = %{\n        name: name,\n        enabled: Map.get(pool_config, \"enabled\", true),\n        ranges: ranges,\n        # Legacy support\n        range_start: elem(hd(ranges), 0),\n        range_end: elem(hd(ranges), 1),\n        excluded_ranges: [],\n        subnet_mask: subnet_mask,\n        gateway: gateway,\n        dns_servers: dns_servers,\n        domain_name: Map.get(pool_config, \"domain\"),\n        lease_time: Map.get(pool_config, \"lease_time\", @default_lease_time),\n        max_leases: Map.get(pool_config, \"max_leases\", @default_max_leases),\n        priority: Map.get(pool_config, \"priority\", @default_priority),\n        static_reservations: reservations\n      }\n\n      {:ok, pool}\n    end\n  end\n\n  @doc \"\"\"\n  Converts pool definition to AddressPool format.\n\n  ## Parameters\n  - `pool_def` - Pool definition from TOML\n\n  ## Returns\n  - Configuration map suitable for AddressPool.new/1\n  \"\"\"\n  @spec to_address_pool_config(pool_definition()) :: map()\n  def to_address_pool_config(pool_def) do\n    %{\n      name: pool_def.name,\n      ranges: pool_def.ranges,\n      range_start: pool_def[:range_start] || elem(hd(pool_def.ranges), 0),\n      range_end: pool_def[:range_end] || elem(hd(pool_def.ranges), 1),\n      excluded_ranges: pool_def[:excluded_ranges] || [],\n      subnet_mask: pool_def.subnet_mask,\n      gateway: pool_def.gateway,\n      dns_servers: pool_def.dns_servers,\n      domain_name: pool_def.domain_name,\n      lease_time: pool_def.lease_time,\n      static_reservations: pool_def.static_reservations\n    }\n  end\n\n  # Private functions\n\n  defp parse_pools(%{\"pools\" => pools}) when is_list(pools) do\n    results =\n      Enum.map(pools, fn pool_config ->\n        case validate(pool_config) do\n          {:ok, pool} ->\n            {:ok, pool}\n\n          {:error, reason} ->\n            name = Map.get(pool_config, \"name\", \"unknown\")\n            emit_pool_error_telemetry(name, reason)\n            {:error, {name, reason}}\n        end\n      end)\n\n    errors = Enum.filter(results, &match?({:error, _}, &1))\n\n    if Enum.empty?(errors) do\n      pools = Enum.map(results, fn {:ok, pool} -> pool end)\n      emit_loaded_telemetry(length(pools))\n      {:ok, pools}\n    else\n      {:error, {:validation_errors, errors}}\n    end\n  end\n\n  defp parse_pools(_config) do\n    {:error, :no_pools_defined}\n  end\n\n  defp validate_name(pool_config) do\n    case Map.get(pool_config, \"name\") do\n      nil -> {:error, :missing_name}\n      name when is_binary(name) -> {:ok, name}\n      _ -> {:error, :invalid_name}\n    end\n  end\n\n  defp validate_ranges(pool_config) do\n    case Map.get(pool_config, \"ranges\") do\n      nil ->\n        {:error, :missing_ranges}\n\n      ranges when is_list(ranges) ->\n        parsed_ranges =\n          Enum.map(ranges, fn range_str ->\n            parse_range_string(range_str)\n          end)\n\n        errors = Enum.filter(parsed_ranges, &match?({:error, _}, &1))\n\n        if Enum.empty?(errors) do\n          {:ok, Enum.map(parsed_ranges, fn {:ok, range} -> range end)}\n        else\n          {:error, {:invalid_ranges, errors}}\n        end\n\n      _ ->\n        {:error, :invalid_ranges}\n    end\n  end\n\n  defp parse_range_string(range_str) when is_binary(range_str) do\n    case String.split(range_str, \"-\") do\n      [start_str, end_str] ->\n        with {:ok, start_ip} <- parse_ip_string(String.trim(start_str)),\n             {:ok, end_ip} <- parse_ip_string(String.trim(end_str)) do\n          {:ok, {start_ip, end_ip}}\n        end\n\n      _ ->\n        {:error, {:invalid_range_format, range_str}}\n    end\n  end\n\n  defp parse_range_string(_), do: {:error, :invalid_range_type}\n\n  defp validate_subnet(pool_config) do\n    case Map.get(pool_config, \"subnet\") do\n      nil ->\n        # Default to /24\n        {:ok, {255, 255, 255, 0}}\n\n      subnet_str when is_binary(subnet_str) ->\n        parse_subnet_string(subnet_str)\n\n      _ ->\n        {:error, :invalid_subnet}\n    end\n  end\n\n  defp parse_subnet_string(subnet_str) do\n    case String.split(subnet_str, \"/\") do\n      [_network, prefix_str] ->\n        case Integer.parse(prefix_str) do\n          {prefix_len, \"\"} when prefix_len >= 0 and prefix_len <= 32 ->\n            mask = prefix_to_mask(prefix_len)\n            {:ok, mask}\n\n          _ ->\n            {:error, {:invalid_prefix, prefix_str}}\n        end\n\n      _ ->\n        {:error, {:invalid_subnet_format, subnet_str}}\n    end\n  end\n\n  defp prefix_to_mask(prefix_len) do\n    mask_int = bsl(0xFFFFFFFF, 32 - prefix_len) &&& 0xFFFFFFFF\n    <<a, b, c, d>> = <<mask_int::32>>\n    {a, b, c, d}\n  end\n\n  defp validate_gateway(pool_config) do\n    case Map.get(pool_config, \"gateway\") do\n      nil -> {:error, :missing_gateway}\n      ip_str when is_binary(ip_str) -> parse_ip_string(ip_str)\n      _ -> {:error, :invalid_gateway}\n    end\n  end\n\n  defp validate_dns_servers(pool_config) do\n    case Map.get(pool_config, \"dns_servers\") do\n      nil ->\n        {:ok, []}\n\n      servers when is_list(servers) ->\n        parsed =\n          Enum.map(servers, fn server_str ->\n            parse_ip_string(server_str)\n          end)\n\n        errors = Enum.filter(parsed, &match?({:error, _}, &1))\n\n        if Enum.empty?(errors) do\n          {:ok, Enum.map(parsed, fn {:ok, ip} -> ip end)}\n        else\n          {:error, {:invalid_dns_servers, errors}}\n        end\n\n      _ ->\n        {:error, :invalid_dns_servers}\n    end\n  end\n\n  defp validate_reservations(pool_config) do\n    case Map.get(pool_config, \"reservations\") do\n      nil ->\n        {:ok, %{}}\n\n      reservations when is_list(reservations) ->\n        parsed =\n          Enum.map(reservations, fn res ->\n            with {:ok, mac} <- validate_mac(Map.get(res, \"mac\")),\n                 {:ok, ip} <- parse_ip_string(Map.get(res, \"address\", \"\")) do\n              {:ok, {mac, ip}}\n            end\n          end)\n\n        errors = Enum.filter(parsed, &match?({:error, _}, &1))\n\n        if Enum.empty?(errors) do\n          map =\n            parsed\n            |> Enum.map(fn {:ok, {mac, ip}} -> {mac, ip} end)\n            |> Map.new()\n\n          {:ok, map}\n        else\n          {:error, {:invalid_reservations, errors}}\n        end\n\n      _ ->\n        {:error, :invalid_reservations}\n    end\n  end\n\n  defp validate_mac(nil), do: {:error, :missing_mac}\n\n  defp validate_mac(mac_str) when is_binary(mac_str) do\n    # Normalize MAC address format (uppercase, colon-separated)\n    normalized =\n      mac_str\n      |> String.upcase()\n      |> String.replace([\"-\", \".\"], \":\")\n\n    # Validate format\n    if Regex.match?(~r/^([0-9A-F]{2}:){5}[0-9A-F]{2}$/, normalized) do\n      {:ok, normalized}\n    else\n      {:error, {:invalid_mac_format, mac_str}}\n    end\n  end\n\n  defp validate_mac(_), do: {:error, :invalid_mac_type}\n\n  defp parse_ip_string(ip_string) when is_binary(ip_string) do\n    case String.split(ip_string, \".\") do\n      [a, b, c, d] ->\n        with {ai, \"\"} <- Integer.parse(a),\n             {bi, \"\"} <- Integer.parse(b),\n             {ci, \"\"} <- Integer.parse(c),\n             {di, \"\"} <- Integer.parse(d),\n             true <- ai in 0..255 and bi in 0..255 and ci in 0..255 and di in 0..255 do\n          {:ok, {ai, bi, ci, di}}\n        else\n          _ -> {:error, {:invalid_ip_format, ip_string}}\n        end\n\n      _ ->\n        {:error, {:invalid_ip_format, ip_string}}\n    end\n  end\n\n  defp parse_ip_string(_), do: {:error, :invalid_ip_type}\n\n  # Telemetry helpers\n\n  defp emit_error_telemetry(path, reason, error) do\n    :telemetry.execute(\n      [:yellow_dog, :dhcpv4, :pool_config, :error],\n      %{count: 1},\n      %{path: path, reason: reason, error: inspect(error)}\n    )\n  end\n\n  defp emit_fallback_telemetry(path) do\n    :telemetry.execute(\n      [:yellow_dog, :dhcpv4, :pool_config, :fallback],\n      %{count: 1},\n      %{path: path}\n    )\n  end\n\n  defp emit_pool_error_telemetry(name, reason) do\n    :telemetry.execute(\n      [:yellow_dog, :dhcpv4, :pool_config, :pool_error],\n      %{count: 1},\n      %{pool_name: name, reason: inspect(reason)}\n    )\n  end\n\n  defp emit_loaded_telemetry(count) do\n    :telemetry.execute(\n      [:yellow_dog, :dhcpv4, :pool_config, :loaded],\n      %{pool_count: count},\n      %{}\n    )\n  end\nend\n","numLines":420,"startLine":1,"totalLines":420}}}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-5-20251101","id":"msg_018YTg5H8qwtVKUhYE4wfwCB","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Now I understand the actual API. Let me also look at the ConflictResolver to understand what's happening:"}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1,"cache_creation_input_tokens":5472,"cache_read_input_tokens":96485,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":5472,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":5,"service_tier":"standard"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"a8559038-3d53-47df-9b7a-d16bbb068c80","uuid":"f09d54d0-7886-47c8-8b51-66234af9f8ce"}
