{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"text","text":"This session is being continued from a previous conversation that ran out of context. The summary below covers the earlier portion of the conversation.\n\nAnalysis:\nLet me analyze the conversation chronologically:\n\n1. **Initial Context (from compacted summary)**: \n   - User activated \"Loki Mode\" - an autonomous development mode with a PRD at ./prd.md\n   - PRD describes DHCP Service Data Persistence layer with:\n     - TOML-based pool configuration loading (FR1)\n     - Lease lifecycle management with conflict resolution (FR2)\n     - ACL enforcement (FR3)\n     - Custom options with template variables (FR4)\n     - Max lease limits per pool (default 1000) (FR1.6)\n   - Previous work already completed: PoolConfig, ACL, ConflictResolver, CustomOptions modules were created\n   - Tests were passing at the end of the previous session\n\n2. **Current Session Work**:\n   - Continued from compacted context\n   - Ran compilation - all modules compiled successfully\n   - Ran test suite - all tests passed initially (573 tests across apps)\n   - Created new unit tests for PRD modules:\n     - ACL test (acl_test.exs)\n     - CustomOptions test (custom_options_test.exs)\n     - ConflictResolver test (conflict_resolver_test.exs)\n     - PoolConfig test (pool_config_test.exs)\n\n3. **Test Failures and Fixes**:\n   - PoolConfig tests failed - the actual module API was different from test expectations\n     - Fixed: Rewrote tests to match actual API (e.g., `subnet_mask` vs `subnet`, gateway is required, MAC stored as string)\n   \n   - ConflictResolver tests failed - depends on LeaseManager which wasn't running\n     - Fixed: Added LeaseManager to test setup with proper pool_config including `static_reservations`\n   \n   - LeaseManager Bug 1: `get_pool_config` used `Map.get(state.pools, pool_name)` but `state.pools` is a list, not a map\n     - Fixed: Changed to `Enum.find(state.pools, fn pool -> pool.name == pool_name end)`\n   \n   - LeaseManager Bug 2: `get_pool_config` returned a simplified config map without `static_reservations`\n     - Fixed: Added `static_reservations: pool.static_reservations` to the returned config\n   \n   - LeaseManager Bug 3: `get_pool_config` still missing `ranges` field needed by `AddressPool.get_available_ip`\n     - Fixed: Changed to return the full pool struct instead of a partial config\n   \n   - LeaseManager Bug 4: `get_static_reservations` also used `Map.get(state.pools, pool_name)` instead of `Enum.find`\n     - Fixed: Same fix as Bug 1\n\n4. **Final Test Results**:\n   - All 103 DHCPv4 tests pass (0 failures, 7 excluded)\n   - All project tests pass across all apps\n\n5. **Files Created/Modified**:\n   - Created: acl_test.exs, custom_options_test.exs, conflict_resolver_test.exs, pool_config_test.exs\n   - Modified: lease_manager.ex (multiple bug fixes)\n\n6. **User Messages**: Only the system-generated continuation message from compaction - no direct user messages in this session.\n\n7. **Pending Tasks**:\n   - Update CONTINUITY.md with progress (in_progress)\n   - Commit all PRD implementation changes (pending)\n\nSummary:\n1. Primary Request and Intent:\n   The user activated \"Loki Mode\" - an autonomous development mode with a PRD at ./prd.md for implementing a DHCP Service Data Persistence layer. The PRD specifies:\n   - TOML-based pool configuration loading (FR1)\n   - Lease lifecycle management with conflict resolution (FR2)\n   - ACL enforcement (FR3)\n   - Custom options with template variables (FR4)\n   - Max lease limits per pool (default 1000) (FR1.6)\n   \n   The mode requires working perpetually, finding improvements, running tests, and committing changes atomically.\n\n2. Key Technical Concepts:\n   - Elixir umbrella project with 11 apps\n   - DHCP protocol (v4 and v6)\n   - Mnesia for persistent lease storage\n   - TOML configuration parsing\n   - GenServer patterns for lease management\n   - Telemetry for observability\n   - ACL pattern matching with glob support\n   - Template variable substitution\n   - IP address pool management with conflict quarantine\n   - ExUnit testing with supervised process setup\n\n3. Files and Code Sections:\n\n   - **apps/yellow_dog_dhcpv4/lib/yellow_dog/dhcpv4/lease_manager.ex** (MODIFIED)\n     - Critical bug fixes discovered through testing\n     - Fix 1: `get_pool_config` handler - state.pools is a list, not a map\n     ```elixir\n     @impl true\n     def handle_call({:get_pool_config, pool_name}, _from, state) do\n       case Enum.find(state.pools, fn pool -> pool.name == pool_name end) do\n         nil ->\n           {:reply, {:error, :pool_not_found}, state}\n\n         pool ->\n           # Return the full pool struct for use with AddressPool functions\n           {:reply, {:ok, pool}, state}\n       end\n     end\n     ```\n     - Fix 2: `get_static_reservations` handler - same issue\n     ```elixir\n     @impl true\n     def handle_call({:get_static_reservations, pool_name}, _from, state) do\n       case Enum.find(state.pools, fn pool -> pool.name == pool_name end) do\n         nil ->\n           {:reply, [], state}\n\n         pool ->\n     ```\n\n   - **apps/yellow_dog_dhcpv4/test/yellow_dog/dhcpv4/acl_test.exs** (CREATED)\n     - Tests ACL rule validation, evaluation, priority ordering\n     - 25+ tests covering allow/deny/custom_options actions\n\n   - **apps/yellow_dog_dhcpv4/test/yellow_dog/dhcpv4/custom_options_test.exs** (CREATED)\n     - Tests option validation, template substitution, encoding\n     - Covers string, ip, ip_list, uint8, uint16, uint32, hex types\n\n   - **apps/yellow_dog_dhcpv4/test/yellow_dog/dhcpv4/conflict_resolver_test.exs** (CREATED)\n     - Tests quarantine management, stats, conflict handling\n     - Required setup with LeaseManager and LeaseStorage:\n     ```elixir\n     setup do\n       LeaseStorage.init()\n\n       pool_config = %{\n         name: \"default\",\n         range_start: {192, 168, 1, 100},\n         range_end: {192, 168, 1, 200},\n         subnet_mask: {255, 255, 255, 0},\n         gateway: {192, 168, 1, 1},\n         dns_servers: [{192, 168, 1, 1}],\n         domain_name: \"test.local\",\n         lease_time: 86400,\n         static_reservations: %{}\n       }\n\n       {:ok, _lease_mgr} = start_supervised({LeaseManager, pools: [pool_config]})\n       {:ok, _resolver} = start_supervised(ConflictResolver)\n\n       :ok\n     end\n     ```\n\n   - **apps/yellow_dog_dhcpv4/test/yellow_dog/dhcpv4/pool_config_test.exs** (CREATED)\n     - Tests TOML pool configuration validation and conversion\n     - Tests subnet mask calculation for /8, /16, /24 prefixes\n\n4. Errors and fixes:\n   - **PoolConfig test failures** (tests expected different API):\n     - Tests expected `pool.subnet` but actual API uses `pool.subnet_mask`\n     - Tests expected optional gateway but it's required\n     - Tests expected MAC as binary but it's stored as uppercase string\n     - Fix: Rewrote tests to match actual PoolConfig module API\n   \n   - **ConflictResolver tests crash** (LeaseManager not running):\n     - `handle_conflict` calls `LeaseManager.decline_ip/2` which requires LeaseManager\n     - Fix: Added LeaseManager to test setup with proper pool_config\n   \n   - **LeaseManager BadMapError** (`Map.get` on list):\n     - `state.pools` is stored as a list but `handle_call({:get_pool_config, ...})` used `Map.get`\n     - Fix: Changed to `Enum.find(state.pools, fn pool -> pool.name == pool_name end)`\n   \n   - **KeyError :static_reservations not found**:\n     - `get_pool_config` created a new map without `static_reservations` field\n     - Fix: Initially added the field, then simplified to return full pool struct\n   \n   - **KeyError :ranges not found**:\n     - AddressPool.get_available_ip expects full pool struct with `ranges` field\n     - Fix: Changed `get_pool_config` to return `{:reply, {:ok, pool}, state}` (full struct)\n\n5. Problem Solving:\n   - Discovered and fixed 4 bugs in LeaseManager through comprehensive testing\n   - Successfully wrote tests that validate the full integration path: LeaseStorage → LeaseManager → ConflictResolver\n   - All 103 DHCPv4 tests now pass (0 failures, 7 excluded)\n   - Full project test suite passes across all apps\n\n6. All user messages:\n   - Only the system-generated continuation message from compaction was present - no direct user messages in this session. The original Loki Mode activation prompt from the previous session specified autonomous development with the PRD.\n\n7. Pending Tasks:\n   - Update CONTINUITY.md with progress (in_progress per todo list)\n   - Commit all PRD implementation changes (pending per todo list)\n\n8. Current Work:\n   Immediately before this summary, I had just:\n   - Fixed all LeaseManager bugs discovered through testing\n   - Verified all 103 DHCPv4 tests pass\n   - Verified full project test suite passes\n   - Updated todo list marking \"Add unit tests for new PRD functionality\" as completed\n   - Added new todo item \"Fix LeaseManager bugs discovered via tests\" as completed\n   - Set \"Update CONTINUITY.md with progress\" as in_progress\n\n9. Optional Next Step:\n   Based on the Loki Mode instructions and current todo list status, the next step is to:\n   1. Update CONTINUITY.md with the PRD implementation progress\n   2. Commit all the changes atomically with a descriptive message\n\n   The most recent work involved updating the todo list:\n   ```\n   {\"content\": \"Update CONTINUITY.md with progress\", \"status\": \"in_progress\", \"activeForm\": \"Updating continuity\"}\n   {\"content\": \"Commit all PRD implementation changes\", \"status\": \"pending\", \"activeForm\": \"Committing changes\"}\n   ```\n\nIf you need specific details from before compaction (like exact code snippets, error messages, or content you generated), read the full transcript at: /home/gao/.claude/projects/-home-gao-Workspace-gsmlg-dev-yellow-dog/a8559038-3d53-47df-