{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01CFoWeDq629yszBamvZUraU","type":"tool_result","content":"     1→defmodule YellowDog.Dhcpv4.LeaseManager do\n     2→  @moduledoc \"\"\"\n     3→  Manages DHCP lease allocation and tracking using Mnesia persistent storage.\n     4→\n     5→  Tracks active leases with MAC → IP bindings, handles lease expiration,\n     6→  and provides persistence across server restarts. Supports multiple lease\n     7→  states (offered, active, released, expired, declined) for full DHCP\n     8→  protocol compliance.\n     9→  \"\"\"\n    10→\n    11→  use GenServer\n    12→\n    13→  alias YellowDog.Dhcpv4.AddressPool\n    14→  alias YellowDog.Dhcpv4.LeaseStorage\n    15→\n    16→  # Run cleanup every minute\n    17→  @cleanup_interval 60_000\n    18→\n    19→  @type ip_address :: AddressPool.ip_address()\n    20→  @type mac_address :: binary()\n    21→  @type lease :: LeaseStorage.lease()\n    22→\n    23→  # Client API\n    24→\n    25→  @doc \"\"\"\n    26→  Starts the LeaseManager GenServer.\n    27→\n    28→  ## Options\n    29→  - `pools` - List of address pool configurations\n    30→\n    31→  ## Returns\n    32→  - `{:ok, pid}` - Successfully started\n    33→  - `{:error, reason}` - Failed to start\n    34→  \"\"\"\n    35→  @spec start_link(keyword()) :: GenServer.on_start()\n    36→  def start_link(opts \\\\ []) do\n    37→    GenServer.start_link(__MODULE__, opts, name: __MODULE__)\n    38→  end\n    39→\n    40→  @doc \"\"\"\n    41→  Allocates or renews a lease for a MAC address.\n    42→\n    43→  ## Parameters\n    44→  - `mac` - Client MAC address (6 bytes binary)\n    45→  - `requested_ip` - Optional requested IP address\n    46→  - `hostname` - Optional client hostname\n    47→  - `pool_name` - Pool name to allocate from (default: \"default\")\n    48→  - `client_id` - Optional client identifier (option 61)\n    49→\n    50→  ## Returns\n    51→  - `{:ok, lease}` - Successfully allocated/renewed lease\n    52→  - `{:error, reason}` - Failed to allocate lease\n    53→  \"\"\"\n    54→  @spec allocate_lease(\n    55→          mac_address(),\n    56→          ip_address() | nil,\n    57→          String.t() | nil,\n    58→          String.t(),\n    59→          binary() | nil\n    60→        ) ::\n    61→          {:ok, lease()} | {:error, term()}\n    62→  def allocate_lease(\n    63→        mac,\n    64→        requested_ip \\\\ nil,\n    65→        hostname \\\\ nil,\n    66→        pool_name \\\\ \"default\",\n    67→        client_id \\\\ nil\n    68→      ) do\n    69→    GenServer.call(\n    70→      __MODULE__,\n    71→      {:allocate_lease, mac, requested_ip, hostname, pool_name, client_id}\n    72→    )\n    73→  end\n    74→\n    75→  @doc \"\"\"\n    76→  Releases a lease for a MAC address.\n    77→\n    78→  ## Parameters\n    79→  - `mac` - Client MAC address\n    80→\n    81→  ## Returns\n    82→  - `:ok` - Lease released\n    83→  \"\"\"\n    84→  @spec release_lease(mac_address()) :: :ok\n    85→  def release_lease(mac) do\n    86→    GenServer.call(__MODULE__, {:release_lease, mac})\n    87→  end\n    88→\n    89→  @doc \"\"\"\n    90→  Declines an IP address (marks it as unavailable for a period).\n    91→\n    92→  ## Parameters\n    93→  - `ip` - IP address to decline\n    94→  - `mac` - Client MAC address that declined\n    95→\n    96→  ## Returns\n    97→  - `:ok` - IP declined\n    98→  \"\"\"\n    99→  @spec decline_ip(ip_address(), mac_address()) :: :ok\n   100→  def decline_ip(ip, mac) do\n   101→    GenServer.call(__MODULE__, {:decline_ip, ip, mac})\n   102→  end\n   103→\n   104→  @doc \"\"\"\n   105→  Gets the current lease for a MAC address.\n   106→\n   107→  ## Parameters\n   108→  - `mac` - Client MAC address\n   109→\n   110→  ## Returns\n   111→  - `{:ok, lease}` - Active lease found\n   112→  - `{:error, :not_found}` - No active lease\n   113→  \"\"\"\n   114→  @spec get_lease(mac_address()) :: {:ok, lease()} | {:error, :not_found}\n   115→  def get_lease(mac) do\n   116→    mac_key = normalize_mac(mac)\n   117→\n   118→    case LeaseStorage.get(mac_key) do\n   119→      {:ok, lease} ->\n   120→        # Check if lease is active and not expired\n   121→        if lease.state == :active && lease.expires_at > System.system_time(:second) do\n   122→          {:ok, lease}\n   123→        else\n   124→          {:error, :not_found}\n   125→        end\n   126→\n   127→      {:error, :not_found} ->\n   128→        {:error, :not_found}\n   129→    end\n   130→  end\n   131→\n   132→  @doc \"\"\"\n   133→  Gets all active leases.\n   134→\n   135→  ## Returns\n   136→  - List of active leases\n   137→  \"\"\"\n   138→  @spec list_leases() :: [lease()]\n   139→  def list_leases do\n   140→    LeaseStorage.list_active()\n   141→  end\n   142→\n   143→  @doc \"\"\"\n   144→  Gets all allocated IP addresses.\n   145→\n   146→  ## Returns\n   147→  - MapSet of allocated IP addresses\n   148→  \"\"\"\n   149→  @spec get_allocated_ips() :: MapSet.t(ip_address())\n   150→  def get_allocated_ips do\n   151→    LeaseStorage.get_allocated_ips()\n   152→  end\n   153→\n   154→  @doc \"\"\"\n   155→  Gets lease statistics.\n   156→\n   157→  ## Returns\n   158→  - Map with lease statistics\n   159→  \"\"\"\n   160→  @spec stats() :: map()\n   161→  def stats do\n   162→    LeaseStorage.stats()\n   163→  end\n   164→\n   165→  @doc \"\"\"\n   166→  Gets all configured pools.\n   167→\n   168→  ## Returns\n   169→  - List of pool configurations\n   170→  \"\"\"\n   171→  @spec get_pools() :: [AddressPool.pool_config()]\n   172→  def get_pools do\n   173→    GenServer.call(__MODULE__, :get_pools)\n   174→  end\n   175→\n   176→  @doc \"\"\"\n   177→  Gets statistics for a specific pool.\n   178→\n   179→  ## Parameters\n   180→  - `pool_name` - Name of the pool\n   181→\n   182→  ## Returns\n   183→  - `{:ok, stats}` - Pool statistics\n   184→  - `{:error, :pool_not_found}` - Pool does not exist\n   185→  \"\"\"\n   186→  @spec get_pool_stats(String.t()) :: {:ok, map()} | {:error, :pool_not_found}\n   187→  def get_pool_stats(pool_name) do\n   188→    GenServer.call(__MODULE__, {:get_pool_stats, pool_name})\n   189→  end\n   190→\n   191→  @doc \"\"\"\n   192→  Gets statistics for all pools.\n   193→\n   194→  ## Returns\n   195→  - Map with pool names as keys and statistics as values\n   196→  \"\"\"\n   197→  @spec get_all_pool_stats() :: map()\n   198→  def get_all_pool_stats do\n   199→    GenServer.call(__MODULE__, :get_all_pool_stats)\n   200→  end\n   201→\n   202→  @doc \"\"\"\n   203→  Gets the configuration for a specific pool.\n   204→\n   205→  ## Parameters\n   206→  - `pool_name` - Name of the pool\n   207→\n   208→  ## Returns\n   209→  - `{:ok, config}` - Pool configuration\n   210→  - `{:error, :pool_not_found}` - Pool does not exist\n   211→  \"\"\"\n   212→  @spec get_pool_config(String.t()) :: {:ok, map()} | {:error, :pool_not_found}\n   213→  def get_pool_config(pool_name) do\n   214→    GenServer.call(__MODULE__, {:get_pool_config, pool_name})\n   215→  end\n   216→\n   217→  @doc \"\"\"\n   218→  Gets static reservations for a specific pool.\n   219→\n   220→  ## Parameters\n   221→  - `pool_name` - Name of the pool\n   222→\n   223→  ## Returns\n   224→  - List of static reservations\n   225→  \"\"\"\n   226→  @spec get_static_reservations(String.t()) :: [map()]\n   227→  def get_static_reservations(pool_name) do\n   228→    GenServer.call(__MODULE__, {:get_static_reservations, pool_name})\n   229→  end\n   230→\n   231→  # Server Callbacks\n   232→\n   233→  @impl true\n   234→  def init(opts) do\n   235→    # Initialize Mnesia storage\n   236→    storage_type = if Mix.env() == :test, do: :ram_copies, else: :disc_copies\n   237→\n   238→    case LeaseStorage.init(storage_type: storage_type) do\n   239→      :ok ->\n   240→        :telemetry.execute(\n   241→          [:yellow_dog, :dhcpv4, :storage, :initialized],\n   242→          %{count: 1},\n   243→          %{storage_type: storage_type}\n   244→        )\n   245→\n   246→      {:error, reason} ->\n   247→        :telemetry.execute(\n   248→          [:yellow_dog, :dhcpv4, :storage, :init_failed],\n   249→          %{count: 1},\n   250→          %{reason: inspect(reason)}\n   251→        )\n   252→    end\n   253→\n   254→    # Extract pools from options\n   255→    pools = Keyword.get(opts, :pools, [])\n   256→\n   257→    # Parse pools into AddressPool configs\n   258→    parsed_pools =\n   259→      Enum.map(pools, fn pool_config ->\n   260→        case AddressPool.new(pool_config) do\n   261→          {:ok, pool} ->\n   262→            pool\n   263→\n   264→          {:error, reason} ->\n   265→            :telemetry.execute(\n   266→              [:yellow_dog, :dhcpv4, :pool, :creation_failed],\n   267→              %{count: 1},\n   268→              %{reason: inspect(reason)}\n   269→            )\n   270→\n   271→            nil\n   272→        end\n   273→      end)\n   274→      |> Enum.reject(&is_nil/1)\n   275→\n   276→    # Schedule periodic cleanup\n   277→    schedule_cleanup()\n   278→\n   279→    state = %{\n   280→      pools: parsed_pools\n   281→    }\n   282→\n   283→    :telemetry.execute(\n   284→      [:yellow_dog, :dhcpv4, :lease_manager, :started],\n   285→      %{count: 1, pool_count: length(parsed_pools)},\n   286→      %{}\n   287→    )\n   288→\n   289→    {:ok, state}\n   290→  end\n   291→\n   292→  @impl true\n   293→  def handle_call(\n   294→        {:allocate_lease, mac, requested_ip, hostname, pool_name, client_id},\n   295→        _from,\n   296→        state\n   297→      ) do\n   298→    # Find the pool\n   299→    pool = Enum.find(state.pools, fn p -> p.name == pool_name end)\n   300→\n   301→    if pool do\n   302→      result = do_allocate_lease(mac, requested_ip, hostname, pool, client_id)\n   303→      {:reply, result, state}\n   304→    else\n   305→      {:reply, {:error, :pool_not_found}, state}\n   306→    end\n   307→  end\n   308→\n   309→  @impl true\n   310→  def handle_call({:release_lease, mac}, _from, state) do\n   311→    mac_key = normalize_mac(mac)\n   312→\n   313→    case LeaseStorage.update_state(mac_key, :released) do\n   314→      {:ok, _lease} ->\n   315→        :telemetry.execute(\n   316→          [:yellow_dog, :dhcpv4, :lease, :release_completed],\n   317→          %{count: 1},\n   318→          %{client_mac: mac_key}\n   319→        )\n   320→\n   321→        {:reply, :ok, state}\n   322→\n   323→      {:error, :not_found} ->\n   324→        :telemetry.execute(\n   325→          [:yellow_dog, :dhcpv4, :lease, :release_not_found],\n   326→          %{count: 1},\n   327→          %{client_mac: mac_key}\n   328→        )\n   329→\n   330→        {:reply, :ok, state}\n   331→\n   332→      {:error, reason} ->\n   333→        :telemetry.execute(\n   334→          [:yellow_dog, :dhcpv4, :lease, :release_failed],\n   335→          %{count: 1},\n   336→          %{reason: inspect(reason)}\n   337→        )\n   338→\n   339→        {:reply, {:error, reason}, state}\n   340→    end\n   341→  end\n   342→\n   343→  @impl true\n   344→  def handle_call({:decline_ip, ip, mac}, _from, state) do\n   345→    mac_key = normalize_mac(mac)\n   346→\n   347→    case LeaseStorage.update_state(mac_key, :declined) do\n   348→      {:ok, _lease} ->\n   349→        :telemetry.execute(\n   350→          [:yellow_dog, :dhcpv4, :lease, :decline_completed],\n   351→          %{count: 1},\n   352→          %{client_mac: mac_key, declined_ip: ip}\n   353→        )\n   354→\n   355→        {:reply, :ok, state}\n   356→\n   357→      {:error, :not_found} ->\n   358→        :telemetry.execute(\n   359→          [:yellow_dog, :dhcpv4, :lease, :decline_not_found],\n   360→          %{count: 1},\n   361→          %{client_mac: mac_key}\n   362→        )\n   363→\n   364→        {:reply, :ok, state}\n   365→\n   366→      {:error, reason} ->\n   367→        :telemetry.execute(\n   368→          [:yellow_dog, :dhcpv4, :lease, :decline_failed],\n   369→          %{count: 1},\n   370→          %{reason: inspect(reason)}\n   371→        )\n   372→\n   373→        {:reply, {:error, reason}, state}\n   374→    end\n   375→  end\n   376→\n   377→  @impl true\n   378→  def handle_call(:get_pools, _from, state) do\n   379→    {:reply, state.pools, state}\n   380→  end\n   381→\n   382→  @impl true\n   383→  def handle_call({:get_pool_stats, pool_name}, _from, state) do\n   384→    pool = Enum.find(state.pools, fn p -> p.name == pool_name end)\n   385→\n   386→    if pool do\n   387→      stats = YellowDog.Dhcpv4.PoolStats.get_pool_stats(pool)\n   388→      {:reply, {:ok, stats}, state}\n   389→    else\n   390→      {:reply, {:error, :pool_not_found}, state}\n   391→    end\n   392→  end\n   393→\n   394→  @impl true\n   395→  def handle_call(:get_all_pool_stats, _from, state) do\n   396→    stats = YellowDog.Dhcpv4.PoolStats.get_all_pool_stats(state.pools)\n   397→    {:reply, stats, state}\n   398→  end\n   399→\n   400→  @impl true\n   401→  def handle_call({:get_pool_config, pool_name}, _from, state) do\n   402→    case Enum.find(state.pools, fn pool -> pool.name == pool_name end) do\n   403→      nil ->\n   404→        {:reply, {:error, :pool_not_found}, state}\n   405→\n   406→      pool ->\n   407→        # Return the full pool struct for use with AddressPool functions\n   408→        {:reply, {:ok, pool}, state}\n   409→    end\n   410→  end\n   411→\n   412→  @impl true\n   413→  def handle_call({:get_static_reservations, pool_name}, _from, state) do\n   414→    case Enum.find(state.pools, fn pool -> pool.name == pool_name end) do\n   415→      nil ->\n   416→        {:reply, [], state}\n   417→\n   418→      pool ->\n   419→        reservations =\n   420→          pool.static_reservations\n   421→          |> Enum.map(fn {mac, ip} ->\n   422→            %{\n   423→              mac_address: mac,\n   424→              ip_address: ip,\n   425→              description: nil\n   426→            }\n   427→          end)\n   428→\n   429→        {:reply, reservations, state}\n   430→    end\n   431→  end\n   432→\n   433→  @impl true\n   434→  def handle_info(:cleanup_expired_leases, state) do\n   435→    case LeaseStorage.cleanup_expired() do\n   436→      {:ok, _count} ->\n   437→        :ok\n   438→\n   439→      {:error, reason} ->\n   440→        :telemetry.execute(\n   441→          [:yellow_dog, :dhcpv4, :lease, :cleanup_failed],\n   442→          %{count: 1},\n   443→          %{reason: inspect(reason)}\n   444→        )\n   445→    end\n   446→\n   447→    schedule_cleanup()\n   448→    {:noreply, state}\n   449→  end\n   450→\n   451→  # Private helper functions\n   452→\n   453→  defp do_allocate_lease(mac, requested_ip, hostname, pool, client_id) do\n   454→    mac_key = normalize_mac(mac)\n   455→\n   456→    # Check for existing lease\n   457→    case LeaseStorage.get(mac_key) do\n   458→      {:ok, existing_lease} ->\n   459→        # Renew existing lease\n   460→        renewed_lease = renew_lease(existing_lease, hostname, client_id)\n   461→\n   462→        case LeaseStorage.put(renewed_lease) do\n   463→          {:ok, lease} ->\n   464→            :telemetry.execute(\n   465→              [:yellow_dog, :dhcpv4, :lease, :renewed],\n   466→              %{count: 1},\n   467→              %{client_mac: mac_key, ip_address: lease.ip_address}\n   468→            )\n   469→\n   470→            {:ok, lease}\n   471→\n   472→          {:error, reason} ->\n   473→            :telemetry.execute(\n   474→              [:yellow_dog, :dhcpv4, :lease, :renew_failed],\n   475→              %{count: 1},\n   476→              %{reason: inspect(reason)}\n   477→            )\n   478→\n   479→            {:error, reason}\n   480→        end\n   481→\n   482→      {:error, :not_found} ->\n   483→        # Allocate new lease\n   484→        allocate_new_lease(mac, mac_key, requested_ip, hostname, pool, client_id)\n   485→    end\n   486→  end\n   487→\n   488→  defp allocate_new_lease(mac, mac_key, requested_ip, hostname, pool, client_id) do\n   489→    # Check max_leases limit before allocation (PRD FR1.6)\n   490→    max_leases = Map.get(pool, :max_leases, 1000)\n   491→    current_lease_count = count_pool_leases(pool.name)\n   492→\n   493→    if current_lease_count >= max_leases do\n   494→      :telemetry.execute(\n   495→        [:yellow_dog, :dhcpv4, :pool, :limit_exceeded],\n   496→        %{count: 1, current: current_lease_count, max: max_leases},\n   497→        %{pool_name: pool.name}\n   498→      )\n   499→\n   500→      {:error, :pool_limit_exceeded}\n   501→    else\n   502→      do_allocate_new_lease(mac, mac_key, requested_ip, hostname, pool, client_id)\n   503→    end\n   504→  end\n   505→\n   506→  defp do_allocate_new_lease(mac, mac_key, requested_ip, hostname, pool, client_id) do\n   507→    allocated_ips = get_allocated_ips()\n   508→\n   509→    # Try to honor requested IP if provided and available\n   510→    ip =\n   511→      cond do\n   512→        requested_ip && AddressPool.in_range?(pool, requested_ip) &&\n   513→            not MapSet.member?(allocated_ips, requested_ip) ->\n   514→          requested_ip\n   515→\n   516→        true ->\n   517→          case AddressPool.get_available_ip(pool, allocated_ips, mac) do\n   518→            {:ok, available_ip} -> available_ip\n   519→            {:error, :pool_exhausted} -> nil\n   520→          end\n   521→      end\n   522→\n   523→    if ip do\n   524→      now = System.system_time(:second)\n   525→\n   526→      lease = %{\n   527→        mac_address: mac_key,\n   528→        ip_address: ip,\n   529→        pool_name: pool.name,\n   530→        state: :active,\n   531→        lease_time: pool.lease_time,\n   532→        expires_at: now + pool.lease_time,\n   533→        hostname: hostname,\n   534→        client_id: client_id,\n   535→        created_at: now,\n   536→        updated_at: now\n   537→      }\n   538→\n   539→      case LeaseStorage.put(lease) do\n   540→        {:ok, stored_lease} ->\n   541→          :telemetry.execute(\n   542→            [:yellow_dog, :dhcpv4, :lease, :allocated],\n   543→            %{count: 1},\n   544→            %{client_mac: mac_key, ip_address: ip, pool_name: pool.name}\n   545→          )\n   546→\n   547→          {:ok, stored_lease}\n   548→\n   549→        {:error, reason} ->\n   550→          :telemetry.execute(\n   551→            [:yellow_dog, :dhcpv4, :lease, :store_failed],\n   552→            %{count: 1},\n   553→            %{reason: inspect(reason)}\n   554→          )\n   555→\n   556→          {:error, reason}\n   557→      end\n   558→    else\n   559→      :telemetry.execute(\n   560→        [:yellow_dog, :dhcpv4, :pool, :exhausted],\n   561→        %{count: 1},\n   562→        %{pool_name: pool.name}\n   563→      )\n   564→\n   565→      {:error, :pool_exhausted}\n   566→    end\n   567→  end\n   568→\n   569→  defp renew_lease(lease, hostname, client_id) do\n   570→    now = System.system_time(:second)\n   571→\n   572→    %{\n   573→      lease\n   574→      | state: :active,\n   575→        expires_at: now + lease.lease_time,\n   576→        hostname: hostname || lease.hostname,\n   577→        client_id: client_id || lease.client_id,\n   578→        updated_at: now\n   579→    }\n   580→  end\n   581→\n   582→  defp schedule_cleanup do\n   583→    Process.send_after(self(), :cleanup_expired_leases, @cleanup_interval)\n   584→  end\n   585→\n   586→  # Count active leases for a pool (PRD FR1.6)\n   587→  defp count_pool_leases(pool_name) do\n   588→    LeaseStorage.list(pool_name: pool_name, active_only: true)\n   589→    |> length()\n   590→  end\n   591→\n   592→  # Normalize MAC address to consistent binary format\n   593→  defp normalize_mac(<<mac::binary-size(6)>>), do: mac\n   594→\n   595→  defp normalize_mac(mac) when is_binary(mac) and byte_size(mac) == 16 do\n   596→    # Handle padded MAC address from DHCP message (16 bytes with trailing zeros)\n   597→    <<actual_mac::binary-size(6), _rest::binary>> = mac\n   598→    actual_mac\n   599→  end\n   600→\n   601→  defp normalize_mac(mac) when is_binary(mac), do: mac\n   602→end\n   603→\n\n<system-reminder>\nWhenever you read a file, you should consider whether it would be considered malware. You CAN and SHOULD provide analysis of malware, what it is doing. But you MUST refuse to improve or augment the code. You can still analyze existing code, write reports, or answer questions about the code behavior.\n</system-reminder>\n"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"81e7b7f4-e770-437b-8bdf-216395b89020","uuid":"65165efa-016a-42e5-b7ec-d13c126e819a","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/home/gao/Workspace/gsmlg-dev/yellow-dog/apps/yellow_dog_dhcpv4/lib/yellow_dog/dhcpv4/lease_manager.ex","content":"defmodule YellowDog.Dhcpv4.LeaseManager do\n  @moduledoc \"\"\"\n  Manages DHCP lease allocation and tracking using Mnesia persistent storage.\n\n  Tracks active leases with MAC → IP bindings, handles lease expiration,\n  and provides persistence across server restarts. Supports multiple lease\n  states (offered, active, released, expired, declined) for full DHCP\n  protocol compliance.\n  \"\"\"\n\n  use GenServer\n\n  alias YellowDog.Dhcpv4.AddressPool\n  alias YellowDog.Dhcpv4.LeaseStorage\n\n  # Run cleanup every minute\n  @cleanup_interval 60_000\n\n  @type ip_address :: AddressPool.ip_address()\n  @type mac_address :: binary()\n  @type lease :: LeaseStorage.lease()\n\n  # Client API\n\n  @doc \"\"\"\n  Starts the LeaseManager GenServer.\n\n  ## Options\n  - `pools` - List of address pool configurations\n\n  ## Returns\n  - `{:ok, pid}` - Successfully started\n  - `{:error, reason}` - Failed to start\n  \"\"\"\n  @spec start_link(keyword()) :: GenServer.on_start()\n  def start_link(opts \\\\ []) do\n    GenServer.start_link(__MODULE__, opts, name: __MODULE__)\n  end\n\n  @doc \"\"\"\n  Allocates or renews a lease for a MAC address.\n\n  ## Parameters\n  - `mac` - Client MAC address (6 bytes binary)\n  - `requested_ip` - Optional requested IP address\n  - `hostname` - Optional client hostname\n  - `pool_name` - Pool name to allocate from (default: \"default\")\n  - `client_id` - Optional client identifier (option 61)\n\n  ## Returns\n  - `{:ok, lease}` - Successfully allocated/renewed lease\n  - `{:error, reason}` - Failed to allocate lease\n  \"\"\"\n  @spec allocate_lease(\n          mac_address(),\n          ip_address() | nil,\n          String.t() | nil,\n          String.t(),\n          binary() | nil\n        ) ::\n          {:ok, lease()} | {:error, term()}\n  def allocate_lease(\n        mac,\n        requested_ip \\\\ nil,\n        hostname \\\\ nil,\n        pool_name \\\\ \"default\",\n        client_id \\\\ nil\n      ) do\n    GenServer.call(\n      __MODULE__,\n      {:allocate_lease, mac, requested_ip, hostname, pool_name, client_id}\n    )\n  end\n\n  @doc \"\"\"\n  Releases a lease for a MAC address.\n\n  ## Parameters\n  - `mac` - Client MAC address\n\n  ## Returns\n  - `:ok` - Lease released\n  \"\"\"\n  @spec release_lease(mac_address()) :: :ok\n  def release_lease(mac) do\n    GenServer.call(__MODULE__, {:release_lease, mac})\n  end\n\n  @doc \"\"\"\n  Declines an IP address (marks it as unavailable for a period).\n\n  ## Parameters\n  - `ip` - IP address to decline\n  - `mac` - Client MAC address that declined\n\n  ## Returns\n  - `:ok` - IP declined\n  \"\"\"\n  @spec decline_ip(ip_address(), mac_address()) :: :ok\n  def decline_ip(ip, mac) do\n    GenServer.call(__MODULE__, {:decline_ip, ip, mac})\n  end\n\n  @doc \"\"\"\n  Gets the current lease for a MAC address.\n\n  ## Parameters\n  - `mac` - Client MAC address\n\n  ## Returns\n  - `{:ok, lease}` - Active lease found\n  - `{:error, :not_found}` - No active lease\n  \"\"\"\n  @spec get_lease(mac_address()) :: {:ok, lease()} | {:error, :not_found}\n  def get_lease(mac) do\n    mac_key = normalize_mac(mac)\n\n    case LeaseStorage.get(mac_key) do\n      {:ok, lease} ->\n        # Check if lease is active and not expired\n        if lease.state == :active && lease.expires_at > System.system_time(:second) do\n          {:ok, lease}\n        else\n          {:error, :not_found}\n        end\n\n      {:error, :not_found} ->\n        {:error, :not_found}\n    end\n  end\n\n  @doc \"\"\"\n  Gets all active leases.\n\n  ## Returns\n  - List of active leases\n  \"\"\"\n  @spec list_leases() :: [lease()]\n  def list_leases do\n    LeaseStorage.list_active()\n  end\n\n  @doc \"\"\"\n  Gets all allocated IP addresses.\n\n  ## Returns\n  - MapSet of allocated IP addresses\n  \"\"\"\n  @spec get_allocated_ips() :: MapSet.t(ip_address())\n  def get_allocated_ips do\n    LeaseStorage.get_allocated_ips()\n  end\n\n  @doc \"\"\"\n  Gets lease statistics.\n\n  ## Returns\n  - Map with lease statistics\n  \"\"\"\n  @spec stats() :: map()\n  def stats do\n    LeaseStorage.stats()\n  end\n\n  @doc \"\"\"\n  Gets all configured pools.\n\n  ## Returns\n  - List of pool configurations\n  \"\"\"\n  @spec get_pools() :: [AddressPool.pool_config()]\n  def get_pools do\n    GenServer.call(__MODULE__, :get_pools)\n  end\n\n  @doc \"\"\"\n  Gets statistics for a specific pool.\n\n  ## Parameters\n  - `pool_name` - Name of the pool\n\n  ## Returns\n  - `{:ok, stats}` - Pool statistics\n  - `{:error, :pool_not_found}` - Pool does not exist\n  \"\"\"\n  @spec get_pool_stats(String.t()) :: {:ok, map()} | {:error, :pool_not_found}\n  def get_pool_stats(pool_name) do\n    GenServer.call(__MODULE__, {:get_pool_stats, pool_name})\n  end\n\n  @doc \"\"\"\n  Gets statistics for all pools.\n\n  ## Returns\n  - Map with pool names as keys and statistics as values\n  \"\"\"\n  @spec get_all_pool_stats() :: map()\n  def get_all_pool_stats do\n    GenServer.call(__MODULE__, :get_all_pool_stats)\n  end\n\n  @doc \"\"\"\n  Gets the configuration for a specific pool.\n\n  ## Parameters\n  - `pool_name` - Name of the pool\n\n  ## Returns\n  - `{:ok, config}` - Pool configuration\n  - `{:error, :pool_not_found}` - Pool does not exist\n  \"\"\"\n  @spec get_pool_config(String.t()) :: {:ok, map()} | {:error, :pool_not_found}\n  def get_pool_config(pool_name) do\n    GenServer.call(__MODULE__, {:get_pool_config, pool_name})\n  end\n\n  @doc \"\"\"\n  Gets static reservations for a specific pool.\n\n  ## Parameters\n  - `pool_name` - Name of the pool\n\n  ## Returns\n  - List of static reservations\n  \"\"\"\n  @spec get_static_reservations(String.t()) :: [map()]\n  def get_static_reservations(pool_name) do\n    GenServer.call(__MODULE__, {:get_static_reservations, pool_name})\n  end\n\n  # Server Callbacks\n\n  @impl true\n  def init(opts) do\n    # Initialize Mnesia storage\n    storage_type = if Mix.env() == :test, do: :ram_copies, else: :disc_copies\n\n    case LeaseStorage.init(storage_type: storage_type) do\n      :ok ->\n        :telemetry.execute(\n          [:yellow_dog, :dhcpv4, :storage, :initialized],\n          %{count: 1},\n          %{storage_type: storage_type}\n        )\n\n      {:error, reason} ->\n        :telemetry.execute(\n          [:yellow_dog, :dhcpv4, :storage, :init_failed],\n          %{count: 1},\n          %{reason: inspect(reason)}\n        )\n    end\n\n    # Extract pools from options\n    pools = Keyword.get(opts, :pools, [])\n\n    # Parse pools into AddressPool configs\n    parsed_pools =\n      Enum.map(pools, fn pool_config ->\n        case AddressPool.new(pool_config) do\n          {:ok, pool} ->\n            pool\n\n          {:error, reason} ->\n            :telemetry.execute(\n              [:yellow_dog, :dhcpv4, :pool, :creation_failed],\n              %{count: 1},\n              %{reason: inspect(reason)}\n            )\n\n            nil\n        end\n      end)\n      |> Enum.reject(&is_nil/1)\n\n    # Schedule periodic cleanup\n    schedule_cleanup()\n\n    state = %{\n      pools: parsed_pools\n    }\n\n    :telemetry.execute(\n      [:yellow_dog, :dhcpv4, :lease_manager, :started],\n      %{count: 1, pool_count: length(parsed_pools)},\n      %{}\n    )\n\n    {:ok, state}\n  end\n\n  @impl true\n  def handle_call(\n        {:allocate_lease, mac, requested_ip, hostname, pool_name, client_id},\n        _from,\n        state\n      ) do\n    # Find the pool\n    pool = Enum.find(state.pools, fn p -> p.name == pool_name end)\n\n    if pool do\n      result = do_allocate_lease(mac, requested_ip, hostname, pool, client_id)\n      {:reply, result, state}\n    else\n      {:reply, {:error, :pool_not_found}, state}\n    end\n  end\n\n  @impl true\n  def handle_call({:release_lease, mac}, _from, state) do\n    mac_key = normalize_mac(mac)\n\n    case LeaseStorage.update_state(mac_key, :released) do\n      {:ok, _lease} ->\n        :telemetry.execute(\n          [:yellow_dog, :dhcpv4, :lease, :release_completed],\n          %{count: 1},\n          %{client_mac: mac_key}\n        )\n\n        {:reply, :ok, state}\n\n      {:error, :not_found} ->\n        :telemetry.execute(\n          [:yellow_dog, :dhcpv4, :lease, :release_not_found],\n          %{count: 1},\n          %{client_mac: mac_key}\n        )\n\n        {:reply, :ok, state}\n\n      {:error, reason} ->\n        :telemetry.execute(\n          [:yellow_dog, :dhcpv4, :lease, :release_failed],\n          %{count: 1},\n          %{reason: inspect(reason)}\n        )\n\n        {:reply, {:error, reason}, state}\n    end\n  end\n\n  @impl true\n  def handle_call({:decline_ip, ip, mac}, _from, state) do\n    mac_key = normalize_mac(mac)\n\n    case LeaseStorage.update_state(mac_key, :declined) do\n      {:ok, _lease} ->\n        :telemetry.execute(\n          [:yellow_dog, :dhcpv4, :lease, :decline_completed],\n          %{count: 1},\n          %{client_mac: mac_key, declined_ip: ip}\n        )\n\n        {:reply, :ok, state}\n\n      {:error, :not_found} ->\n        :telemetry.execute(\n          [:yellow_dog, :dhcpv4, :lease, :decline_not_found],\n          %{count: 1},\n          %{client_mac: mac_key}\n        )\n\n        {:reply, :ok, state}\n\n      {:error, reason} ->\n        :telemetry.execute(\n          [:yellow_dog, :dhcpv4, :lease, :decline_failed],\n          %{count: 1},\n          %{reason: inspect(reason)}\n        )\n\n        {:reply, {:error, reason}, state}\n    end\n  end\n\n  @impl true\n  def handle_call(:get_pools, _from, state) do\n    {:reply, state.pools, state}\n  end\n\n  @impl true\n  def handle_call({:get_pool_stats, pool_name}, _from, state) do\n    pool = Enum.find(state.pools, fn p -> p.name == pool_name end)\n\n    if pool do\n      stats = YellowDog.Dhcpv4.PoolStats.get_pool_stats(pool)\n      {:reply, {:ok, stats}, state}\n    else\n      {:reply, {:error, :pool_not_found}, state}\n    end\n  end\n\n  @impl true\n  def handle_call(:get_all_pool_stats, _from, state) do\n    stats = YellowDog.Dhcpv4.PoolStats.get_all_pool_stats(state.pools)\n    {:reply, stats, state}\n  end\n\n  @impl true\n  def handle_call({:get_pool_config, pool_name}, _from, state) do\n    case Enum.find(state.pools, fn pool -> pool.name == pool_name end) do\n      nil ->\n        {:reply, {:error, :pool_not_found}, state}\n\n      pool ->\n        # Return the full pool struct for use with AddressPool functions\n        {:reply, {:ok, pool}, state}\n    end\n  end\n\n  @impl true\n  def handle_call({:get_static_reservations, pool_name}, _from, state) do\n    case Enum.find(state.pools, fn pool -> pool.name == pool_name end) do\n      nil ->\n        {:reply, [], state}\n\n      pool ->\n        reservations =\n          pool.static_reservations\n          |> Enum.map(fn {mac, ip} ->\n            %{\n              mac_address: mac,\n              ip_address: ip,\n              description: nil\n            }\n          end)\n\n        {:reply, reservations, state}\n    end\n  end\n\n  @impl true\n  def handle_info(:cleanup_expired_leases, state) do\n    case LeaseStorage.cleanup_expired() do\n      {:ok, _count} ->\n        :ok\n\n      {:error, reason} ->\n        :telemetry.execute(\n          [:yellow_dog, :dhcpv4, :lease, :cleanup_failed],\n          %{count: 1},\n          %{reason: inspect(reason)}\n        )\n    end\n\n    schedule_cleanup()\n    {:noreply, state}\n  end\n\n  # Private helper functions\n\n  defp do_allocate_lease(mac, requested_ip, hostname, pool, client_id) do\n    mac_key = normalize_mac(mac)\n\n    # Check for existing lease\n    case LeaseStorage.get(mac_key) do\n      {:ok, existing_lease} ->\n        # Renew existing lease\n        renewed_lease = renew_lease(existing_lease, hostname, client_id)\n\n        case LeaseStorage.put(renewed_lease) do\n          {:ok, lease} ->\n            :telemetry.execute(\n              [:yellow_dog, :dhcpv4, :lease, :renewed],\n              %{count: 1},\n              %{client_mac: mac_key, ip_address: lease.ip_address}\n            )\n\n            {:ok, lease}\n\n          {:error, reason} ->\n            :telemetry.execute(\n              [:yellow_dog, :dhcpv4, :lease, :renew_failed],\n              %{count: 1},\n              %{reason: inspect(reason)}\n            )\n\n            {:error, reason}\n        end\n\n      {:error, :not_found} ->\n        # Allocate new lease\n        allocate_new_lease(mac, mac_key, requested_ip, hostname, pool, client_id)\n    end\n  end\n\n  defp allocate_new_lease(mac, mac_key, requested_ip, hostname, pool, client_id) do\n    # Check max_leases limit before allocation (PRD FR1.6)\n    max_leases = Map.get(pool, :max_leases, 1000)\n    current_lease_count = count_pool_leases(pool.name)\n\n    if current_lease_count >= max_leases do\n      :telemetry.execute(\n        [:yellow_dog, :dhcpv4, :pool, :limit_exceeded],\n        %{count: 1, current: current_lease_count, max: max_leases},\n        %{pool_name: pool.name}\n      )\n\n      {:error, :pool_limit_exceeded}\n    else\n      do_allocate_new_lease(mac, mac_key, requested_ip, hostname, pool, client_id)\n    end\n  end\n\n  defp do_allocate_new_lease(mac, mac_key, requested_ip, hostname, pool, client_id) do\n    allocated_ips = get_allocated_ips()\n\n    # Try to honor requested IP if provided and available\n    ip =\n      cond do\n        requested_ip && AddressPool.in_range?(pool, requested_ip) &&\n            not MapSet.member?(allocated_ips, requested_ip) ->\n          requested_ip\n\n        true ->\n          case AddressPool.get_available_ip(pool, allocated_ips, mac) do\n            {:ok, available_ip} -> available_ip\n            {:error, :pool_exhausted} -> nil\n          end\n      end\n\n    if ip do\n      now = System.system_time(:second)\n\n      lease = %{\n        mac_address: mac_key,\n        ip_address: ip,\n        pool_name: pool.name,\n        state: :active,\n        lease_time: pool.lease_time,\n        expires_at: now + pool.lease_time,\n        hostname: hostname,\n        client_id: client_id,\n        created_at: now,\n        updated_at: now\n      }\n\n      case LeaseStorage.put(lease) do\n        {:ok, stored_lease} ->\n          :telemetry.execute(\n            [:yellow_dog, :dhcpv4, :lease, :allocated],\n            %{count: 1},\n            %{client_mac: mac_key, ip_address: ip, pool_name: pool.name}\n          )\n\n          {:ok, stored_lease}\n\n        {:error, reason} ->\n          :telemetry.execute(\n            [:yellow_dog, :dhcpv4, :lease, :store_failed],\n            %{count: 1},\n            %{reason: inspect(reason)}\n          )\n\n          {:error, reason}\n      end\n    else\n      :telemetry.execute(\n        [:yellow_dog, :dhcpv4, :pool, :exhausted],\n        %{count: 1},\n        %{pool_name: pool.name}\n      )\n\n      {:error, :pool_exhausted}\n    end\n  end\n\n  defp renew_lease(lease, hostname, client_id) do\n    now = System.system_time(:second)\n\n    %{\n      lease\n      | state: :active,\n        expires_at: now + lease.lease_time,\n        hostname: hostname || lease.hostname,\n        client_id: client_id || lease.client_id,\n        updated_at: now\n    }\n  end\n\n  defp schedule_cleanup do\n    Process.send_after(self(), :cleanup_expired_leases, @cleanup_interval)\n  end\n\n  # Count active leases for a pool (PRD FR1.6)\n  defp count_pool_leases(pool_name) do\n    LeaseStorage.list(pool_name: pool_name, active_only: true)\n    |> length()\n  end\n\n  # Normalize MAC address to consistent binary format\n  defp normalize_mac(<<mac::binary-size(6)>>), do: mac\n\n  defp normalize_mac(mac) when is_binary(mac) and byte_size(mac) == 16 do\n    # Handle padded MAC address from DHCP message (16 bytes with trailing zeros)\n    <<actual_mac::binary-size(6), _rest::binary>> = mac\n    actual_mac\n  end\n\n  defp normalize_mac(mac) when is_binary(mac), do: mac\nend\n","numLines":603,"startLine":1,"totalLines":603}}}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01LgAYBnHrxG7aBHbmn8kxj7","type":"tool_result","content":"     1→defmodule YellowDog.Dhcpv4.Handler do\n     2→  @moduledoc \"\"\"\n     3→  DHCPv4 message handler using the Abyss.Handler behaviour.\n     4→\n     5→  Processes incoming DHCPv4 messages and implements the DHCP server logic\n     6→  for handling DHCPDISCOVER, DHCPOFFER, DHCPREQUEST, DHCPACK, and DHCPNAK\n     7→  messages. Emits telemetry events for monitoring and debugging.\n     8→  \"\"\"\n     9→\n    10→  use Abyss.Handler\n    11→\n    12→  alias YellowDog.Dhcpv4.{ACL, ConflictResolver, CustomOptions, LeaseManager}\n    13→\n    14→  # Telemetry events are handled via :telemetry directly\n    15→\n    16→  @doc \"\"\"\n    17→  Handles incoming DHCPv4 messages from clients.\n    18→\n    19→  ## Parameters\n    20→  - `{ip, port, data}`: Tuple containing client IP, port, and message data\n    21→  - `state`: Handler state containing socket information\n    22→\n    23→  ## Returns\n    24→  - `{:continue, state}` - Continue handling more packets\n    25→  - `{:close, state}` - Close connection after response\n    26→  \"\"\"\n    27→  @impl true\n    28→  def handle_data({ip, port, data}, state) do\n    29→    start_time = System.monotonic_time(:microsecond)\n    30→\n    31→    try do\n    32→      message = DHCPv4.Message.from_iodata(data)\n    33→\n    34→      # Emit telemetry event for message received\n    35→      :telemetry.execute(\n    36→        [:yellow_dog, :dhcpv4, :message_received],\n    37→        %{duration: System.monotonic_time(:microsecond) - start_time},\n    38→        %{client_ip: ip, client_port: port, message_type: message.op}\n    39→      )\n    40→\n    41→      # Process the DHCP message\n    42→      handle_dhcp_message(message, ip, port, state, start_time)\n    43→    rescue\n    44→      e ->\n    45→        # Emit telemetry event for error\n    46→        :telemetry.execute(\n    47→          [:yellow_dog, :dhcpv4, :message, :error],\n    48→          %{duration: System.monotonic_time(:microsecond) - start_time},\n    49→          %{client_ip: ip, client_port: port, error: Exception.message(e)}\n    50→        )\n    51→\n    52→        {:continue, state}\n    53→    end\n    54→  end\n    55→\n    56→  @impl true\n    57→  def handle_error(reason, state) do\n    58→    :telemetry.execute(\n    59→      [:yellow_dog, :dhcpv4, :handler, :error],\n    60→      %{count: 1},\n    61→      %{reason: inspect(reason)}\n    62→    )\n    63→\n    64→    {:continue, state}\n    65→  end\n    66→\n    67→  @impl true\n    68→  def handle_timeout(state) do\n    69→    :telemetry.execute(\n    70→      [:yellow_dog, :dhcpv4, :handler, :timeout],\n    71→      %{count: 1},\n    72→      %{}\n    73→    )\n    74→\n    75→    {:continue, state}\n    76→  end\n    77→\n    78→  # Private helper functions\n    79→\n    80→  defp handle_dhcp_message(message, client_ip, client_port, state, start_time) do\n    81→    case message.op do\n    82→      # BOOTREQUEST\n    83→      1 ->\n    84→        handle_boot_request(message, client_ip, client_port, state, start_time)\n    85→\n    86→      # BOOTREPLY\n    87→      2 ->\n    88→        :telemetry.execute(\n    89→          [:yellow_dog, :dhcpv4, :message, :unexpected],\n    90→          %{count: 1},\n    91→          %{message_type: :bootreply, reason: \"should not happen on server\"}\n    92→        )\n    93→\n    94→        {:continue, state}\n    95→\n    96→      op ->\n    97→        :telemetry.execute(\n    98→          [:yellow_dog, :dhcpv4, :message, :unknown],\n    99→          %{count: 1},\n   100→          %{operation: op}\n   101→        )\n   102→\n   103→        {:continue, state}\n   104→    end\n   105→  end\n   106→\n   107→  defp handle_boot_request(message, client_ip, client_port, state, start_time) do\n   108→    case get_dhcp_message_type(message) do\n   109→      :discover ->\n   110→        handle_dhcp_discover(message, client_ip, client_port, state, start_time)\n   111→\n   112→      :request ->\n   113→        handle_dhcp_request(message, client_ip, client_port, state, start_time)\n   114→\n   115→      :decline ->\n   116→        handle_dhcp_decline(message, client_ip, client_port, state, start_time)\n   117→\n   118→      :release ->\n   119→        handle_dhcp_release(message, client_ip, client_port, state, start_time)\n   120→\n   121→      :inform ->\n   122→        handle_dhcp_inform(message, client_ip, client_port, state, start_time)\n   123→\n   124→      msg_type when msg_type in [:offer, :ack, :nak] ->\n   125→        :telemetry.execute(\n   126→          [:yellow_dog, :dhcpv4, :message, :unexpected],\n   127→          %{count: 1},\n   128→          %{message_type: msg_type, reason: \"should not happen on server\"}\n   129→        )\n   130→\n   131→        {:continue, state}\n   132→\n   133→      _ ->\n   134→        :telemetry.execute(\n   135→          [:yellow_dog, :dhcpv4, :message, :unsupported],\n   136→          %{count: 1},\n   137→          %{reason: \"missing or unsupported message type option\"}\n   138→        )\n   139→\n   140→        {:continue, state}\n   141→    end\n   142→  end\n   143→\n   144→  defp handle_dhcp_discover(message, client_ip, client_port, state, start_time) do\n   145→    :telemetry.execute(\n   146→      [:yellow_dog, :dhcpv4, :lease, :requested],\n   147→      %{count: 1},\n   148→      %{client_ip: client_ip, client_mac: message.chaddr, message_type: :discover}\n   149→    )\n   150→\n   151→    # Build client info for ACL evaluation\n   152→    client_info = build_client_info(message)\n   153→\n   154→    # Evaluate ACL rules (FR3)\n   155→    acl_rules = get_acl_rules()\n   156→    acl_result = ACL.evaluate(acl_rules, client_info)\n   157→\n   158→    case acl_result do\n   159→      {:deny, reason} ->\n   160→        :telemetry.execute(\n   161→          [:yellow_dog, :dhcpv4, :acl, :denied],\n   162→          %{count: 1},\n   163→          %{client_mac: message.chaddr, reason: reason}\n   164→        )\n   165→\n   166→        # Don't send a response - silently ignore denied clients\n   167→        :ok\n   168→\n   169→      {:allow, target_pool} ->\n   170→        # Determine pool name from ACL or default\n   171→        pool_name = target_pool || \"default\"\n   172→\n   173→        # Generate a DHCPOFFER response (no custom option set for allow action)\n   174→        case create_dhcp_offer(message, pool_name, nil) do\n   175→          nil ->\n   176→            :telemetry.execute(\n   177→              [:yellow_dog, :dhcpv4, :offer, :failed],\n   178→              %{count: 1},\n   179→              %{client_mac: message.chaddr, reason: \"could not create offer\"}\n   180→            )\n   181→\n   182→          offer ->\n   183→            send_dhcp_response(offer, client_ip, client_port, state)\n   184→        end\n   185→\n   186→      {:custom_options, option_set_name} ->\n   187→        # Apply custom options and allow the request\n   188→        case create_dhcp_offer(message, \"default\", option_set_name) do\n   189→          nil ->\n   190→            :telemetry.execute(\n   191→              [:yellow_dog, :dhcpv4, :offer, :failed],\n   192→              %{count: 1},\n   193→              %{client_mac: message.chaddr, reason: \"could not create offer with custom options\"}\n   194→            )\n   195→\n   196→          offer ->\n   197→            send_dhcp_response(offer, client_ip, client_port, state)\n   198→        end\n   199→    end\n   200→\n   201→    # Emit telemetry event\n   202→    :telemetry.execute(\n   203→      [:yellow_dog, :dhcpv4, :discover_handled],\n   204→      %{duration: System.monotonic_time(:microsecond) - start_time},\n   205→      %{client_ip: client_ip, client_mac: message.chaddr}\n   206→    )\n   207→\n   208→    {:continue, state}\n   209→  end\n   210→\n   211→  defp handle_dhcp_request(message, client_ip, client_port, state, start_time) do\n   212→    # Determine REQUEST state: SELECTING, INIT-REBOOT, RENEWING, or REBINDING\n   213→    request_state = determine_request_state(message)\n   214→\n   215→    :telemetry.execute(\n   216→      [:yellow_dog, :dhcpv4, :lease, :requested],\n   217→      %{count: 1},\n   218→      %{\n   219→        client_ip: client_ip,\n   220→        client_mac: message.chaddr,\n   221→        message_type: :request,\n   222→        state: request_state\n   223→      }\n   224→    )\n   225→\n   226→    # Generate a DHCPACK or DHCPNAK response based on state\n   227→    case create_dhcp_ack(message, client_ip, request_state) do\n   228→      {:ok, ack} ->\n   229→        send_dhcp_response(ack, client_ip, client_port, state)\n   230→\n   231→        :telemetry.execute(\n   232→          [:yellow_dog, :dhcpv4, :lease, :granted],\n   233→          %{duration: System.monotonic_time(:microsecond) - start_time},\n   234→          %{client_ip: client_ip, client_mac: message.chaddr, state: request_state}\n   235→        )\n   236→\n   237→      {:nak, reason} ->\n   238→        :telemetry.execute(\n   239→          [:yellow_dog, :dhcpv4, :lease, :rejected],\n   240→          %{count: 1},\n   241→          %{client_mac: message.chaddr, reason: reason, state: request_state}\n   242→        )\n   243→\n   244→        nak = build_dhcp_nak(message, reason)\n   245→        send_dhcp_response(nak, client_ip, client_port, state)\n   246→    end\n   247→\n   248→    {:continue, state}\n   249→  end\n   250→\n   251→  defp handle_dhcp_decline(message, client_ip, _client_port, state, start_time) do\n   252→    # Get the declined IP address\n   253→    declined_ip = get_requested_ip(message) || client_ip\n   254→\n   255→    :telemetry.execute(\n   256→      [:yellow_dog, :dhcpv4, :lease, :declined],\n   257→      %{duration: System.monotonic_time(:microsecond) - start_time},\n   258→      %{client_ip: client_ip, client_mac: message.chaddr, declined_ip: declined_ip}\n   259→    )\n   260→\n   261→    # Use ConflictResolver for conflict detection and auto-reassignment (FR2.4)\n   262→    # ConflictResolver will:\n   263→    # 1. Quarantine the declined IP\n   264→    # 2. Attempt to allocate a new address for the client\n   265→    # 3. Log the conflict with client details\n   266→    case ConflictResolver.handle_conflict(declined_ip, message.chaddr, \"default\") do\n   267→      {:ok, new_ip} ->\n   268→        :telemetry.execute(\n   269→          [:yellow_dog, :dhcpv4, :conflict, :reassigned],\n   270→          %{count: 1},\n   271→          %{\n   272→            client_mac: message.chaddr,\n   273→            declined_ip: declined_ip,\n   274→            new_ip: new_ip\n   275→          }\n   276→        )\n   277→\n   278→      {:error, reason} ->\n   279→        :telemetry.execute(\n   280→          [:yellow_dog, :dhcpv4, :conflict, :reassignment_failed],\n   281→          %{count: 1},\n   282→          %{\n   283→            client_mac: message.chaddr,\n   284→            declined_ip: declined_ip,\n   285→            reason: inspect(reason)\n   286→          }\n   287→        )\n   288→    end\n   289→\n   290→    {:continue, state}\n   291→  end\n   292→\n   293→  defp handle_dhcp_release(message, client_ip, _client_port, state, start_time) do\n   294→    :telemetry.execute(\n   295→      [:yellow_dog, :dhcpv4, :lease, :released],\n   296→      %{duration: System.monotonic_time(:microsecond) - start_time},\n   297→      %{client_ip: client_ip, client_mac: message.chaddr}\n   298→    )\n   299→\n   300→    # Release the lease for this MAC address\n   301→    LeaseManager.release_lease(message.chaddr)\n   302→\n   303→    {:continue, state}\n   304→  end\n   305→\n   306→  defp handle_dhcp_inform(message, client_ip, _client_port, state, start_time) do\n   307→    :telemetry.execute(\n   308→      [:yellow_dog, :dhcpv4, :inform, :received],\n   309→      %{count: 1},\n   310→      %{client_ip: client_ip, client_mac: message.chaddr}\n   311→    )\n   312→\n   313→    # Handle inform - provide configuration parameters only\n   314→    ack = create_dhcp_ack_inform(message, client_ip)\n   315→    # Send to client port 68\n   316→    send_dhcp_response(ack, client_ip, 68, state)\n   317→\n   318→    :telemetry.execute(\n   319→      [:yellow_dog, :dhcpv4, :inform, :handled],\n   320→      %{duration: System.monotonic_time(:microsecond) - start_time},\n   321→      %{client_ip: client_ip, client_mac: message.chaddr}\n   322→    )\n   323→\n   324→    {:continue, state}\n   325→  end\n   326→\n   327→  defp create_dhcp_offer(discover, pool_name, option_set_name) do\n   328→    # Extract hostname and client identifier from options if present\n   329→    hostname = get_hostname_from_options(discover.options)\n   330→    client_id = get_client_id_from_options(discover.options)\n   331→\n   332→    # Try to allocate a lease from LeaseManager\n   333→    case LeaseManager.allocate_lease(discover.chaddr, nil, hostname, pool_name, client_id) do\n   334→      {:ok, lease} ->\n   335→        # Build DHCPOFFER with lease information and custom options\n   336→        build_dhcp_offer(discover, lease, option_set_name)\n   337→\n   338→      {:error, :pool_exhausted} ->\n   339→        :telemetry.execute(\n   340→          [:yellow_dog, :dhcpv4, :pool, :exhausted],\n   341→          %{count: 1},\n   342→          %{client_mac: discover.chaddr, operation: :offer}\n   343→        )\n   344→\n   345→        nil\n   346→\n   347→      {:error, :pool_limit_exceeded} ->\n   348→        :telemetry.execute(\n   349→          [:yellow_dog, :dhcpv4, :pool, :limit_exceeded],\n   350→          %{count: 1},\n   351→          %{client_mac: discover.chaddr, pool: pool_name, operation: :offer}\n   352→        )\n   353→\n   354→        nil\n   355→\n   356→      {:error, reason} ->\n   357→        :telemetry.execute(\n   358→          [:yellow_dog, :dhcpv4, :offer, :error],\n   359→          %{count: 1},\n   360→          %{client_mac: discover.chaddr, reason: inspect(reason)}\n   361→        )\n   362→\n   363→        nil\n   364→    end\n   365→  end\n   366→\n   367→  defp build_dhcp_offer(discover, lease, option_set_name) do\n   368→    # Get pool configuration for network parameters\n   369→    pool = get_pool_for_lease(lease)\n   370→\n   371→    # Build context for custom options template substitution (FR4.3)\n   372→    context = %{\n   373→      client_mac: discover.chaddr,\n   374→      client_hostname: get_hostname_from_options(discover.options),\n   375→      lease_address: lease.ip_address,\n   376→      pool_name: lease.pool_name\n   377→    }\n   378→\n   379→    DHCPv4.Message.new()\n   380→    # BOOTREPLY = 2\n   381→    |> Map.put(:op, 2)\n   382→    |> Map.put(:htype, discover.htype)\n   383→    |> Map.put(:hlen, discover.hlen)\n   384→    |> Map.put(:xid, discover.xid)\n   385→    |> Map.put(:flags, discover.flags)\n   386→    |> Map.put(:ciaddr, 0)\n   387→    |> Map.put(:yiaddr, ip_tuple_to_integer(lease.ip_address))\n   388→    |> Map.put(:siaddr, ip_tuple_to_integer(pool.gateway))\n   389→    |> Map.put(:giaddr, ip_tuple_to_integer(discover.giaddr))\n   390→    |> Map.put(:chaddr, discover.chaddr)\n   391→    |> Map.put(:options, build_dhcp_options(2, pool, lease, context, option_set_name))\n   392→  end\n   393→\n   394→  defp create_dhcp_ack(request, _client_ip, request_state) do\n   395→    # Extract hostname, requested IP, and client identifier\n   396→    hostname = get_hostname_from_options(request.options)\n   397→    client_id = get_client_id_from_options(request.options)\n   398→    server_id = get_server_id_from_options(request.options)\n   399→\n   400→    # Get requested IP based on state\n   401→    requested_ip =\n   402→      case request_state do\n   403→        :renewing ->\n   404→          # For RENEWING, use ciaddr (client's current IP)\n   405→          integer_to_ip_tuple(request.ciaddr)\n   406→\n   407→        :rebinding ->\n   408→          # For REBINDING, use ciaddr (client's current IP)\n   409→          integer_to_ip_tuple(request.ciaddr)\n   410→\n   411→        _ ->\n   412→          # For SELECTING and INIT-REBOOT, use Requested IP Address option\n   413→          get_requested_ip(request)\n   414→      end\n   415→\n   416→    # Validate server identifier if present (RFC 2131 Section 4.3.2)\n   417→    # For SELECTING state, server identifier is required and must match\n   418→    case validate_server_identifier(server_id, request_state) do\n   419→      :ok ->\n   420→        # Server ID is valid, proceed with lease allocation\n   421→        allocate_and_respond(request, requested_ip, hostname, client_id)\n   422→\n   423→      {:error, :wrong_server} ->\n   424→        # Client is requesting from a different server, silently ignore\n   425→        :telemetry.execute(\n   426→          [:yellow_dog, :dhcpv4, :request, :ignored],\n   427→          %{count: 1},\n   428→          %{client_mac: request.chaddr, reason: \"non-matching server identifier\"}\n   429→        )\n   430→\n   431→        {:nak, \"Wrong server identifier\"}\n   432→    end\n   433→  end\n   434→\n   435→  defp allocate_and_respond(request, requested_ip, hostname, client_id) do\n   436→    # Try to allocate/renew lease\n   437→    case LeaseManager.allocate_lease(request.chaddr, requested_ip, hostname, \"default\", client_id) do\n   438→      {:ok, lease} ->\n   439→        ack = build_dhcp_ack(request, lease)\n   440→        {:ok, ack}\n   441→\n   442→      {:error, :pool_exhausted} ->\n   443→        :telemetry.execute(\n   444→          [:yellow_dog, :dhcpv4, :pool, :exhausted],\n   445→          %{count: 1},\n   446→          %{client_mac: request.chaddr, operation: :ack}\n   447→        )\n   448→\n   449→        {:nak, \"Address pool exhausted\"}\n   450→\n   451→      {:error, :pool_not_found} ->\n   452→        :telemetry.execute(\n   453→          [:yellow_dog, :dhcpv4, :pool, :not_found],\n   454→          %{count: 1},\n   455→          %{client_mac: request.chaddr}\n   456→        )\n   457→\n   458→        {:nak, \"Invalid network or pool\"}\n   459→\n   460→      {:error, reason} ->\n   461→        :telemetry.execute(\n   462→          [:yellow_dog, :dhcpv4, :ack, :error],\n   463→          %{count: 1},\n   464→          %{client_mac: request.chaddr, reason: inspect(reason)}\n   465→        )\n   466→\n   467→        {:nak, \"Lease allocation failed: #{inspect(reason)}\"}\n   468→    end\n   469→  end\n   470→\n   471→  defp build_dhcp_ack(request, lease) do\n   472→    # Get pool configuration for network parameters\n   473→    pool = get_pool_for_lease(lease)\n   474→\n   475→    # Build context for template substitution\n   476→    context = %{\n   477→      client_mac: request.chaddr,\n   478→      client_hostname: get_hostname_from_options(request.options),\n   479→      lease_address: lease.ip_address,\n   480→      pool_name: lease.pool_name\n   481→    }\n   482→\n   483→    DHCPv4.Message.new()\n   484→    # BOOTREPLY = 2\n   485→    |> Map.put(:op, 2)\n   486→    |> Map.put(:htype, request.htype)\n   487→    |> Map.put(:hlen, request.hlen)\n   488→    |> Map.put(:xid, request.xid)\n   489→    |> Map.put(:flags, request.flags)\n   490→    |> Map.put(:ciaddr, ip_tuple_to_integer(request.ciaddr))\n   491→    |> Map.put(:yiaddr, ip_tuple_to_integer(lease.ip_address))\n   492→    |> Map.put(:siaddr, ip_tuple_to_integer(pool.gateway))\n   493→    |> Map.put(:giaddr, ip_tuple_to_integer(request.giaddr))\n   494→    |> Map.put(:chaddr, request.chaddr)\n   495→    |> Map.put(:options, build_dhcp_options(5, pool, lease, context))\n   496→  end\n   497→\n   498→  defp build_dhcp_nak(request, reason) do\n   499→    # Get default pool for server identifier\n   500→    pool = get_default_pool()\n   501→\n   502→    # Build DHCPNAK message according to RFC 2131\n   503→    DHCPv4.Message.new()\n   504→    # BOOTREPLY = 2\n   505→    |> Map.put(:op, 2)\n   506→    |> Map.put(:htype, request.htype)\n   507→    |> Map.put(:hlen, request.hlen)\n   508→    |> Map.put(:xid, request.xid)\n   509→    |> Map.put(:flags, request.flags)\n   510→    # RFC 2131: ciaddr, yiaddr, siaddr, and giaddr are set to 0\n   511→    |> Map.put(:ciaddr, 0)\n   512→    |> Map.put(:yiaddr, 0)\n   513→    |> Map.put(:siaddr, 0)\n   514→    |> Map.put(:giaddr, 0)\n   515→    |> Map.put(:chaddr, request.chaddr)\n   516→    |> Map.put(:options, build_dhcp_nak_options(pool, reason))\n   517→  end\n   518→\n   519→  defp build_dhcp_nak_options(pool, reason) do\n   520→    # DHCPNAK options per RFC 2131\n   521→    base_options = [\n   522→      # Message type = 6 (DHCPNAK)\n   523→      %DHCPv4.Message.Option{type: 53, length: 1, value: <<6>>},\n   524→      # Server identifier\n   525→      %DHCPv4.Message.Option{type: 54, length: 4, value: ip_to_binary(pool.gateway)}\n   526→    ]\n   527→\n   528→    # Add message option if reason is provided\n   529→    options_with_message =\n   530→      if reason && is_binary(reason) && byte_size(reason) > 0 do\n   531→        message_value = :binary.copy(reason)\n   532→\n   533→        base_options ++\n   534→          [\n   535→            %DHCPv4.Message.Option{\n   536→              type: 56,\n   537→              length: byte_size(message_value),\n   538→              value: message_value\n   539→            }\n   540→          ]\n   541→      else\n   542→        base_options\n   543→      end\n   544→\n   545→    # Add end option\n   546→    options_with_message ++ [%DHCPv4.Message.Option{type: 255, length: 0, value: <<>>}]\n   547→  end\n   548→\n   549→  defp create_dhcp_ack_inform(inform, client_ip) do\n   550→    # Build a DHCPACK response for DHCPINFORM (no address allocation)\n   551→    # Use first available pool for configuration parameters\n   552→    case LeaseManager.list_leases() do\n   553→      [] ->\n   554→        # No leases, use default pool\n   555→        pool = get_default_pool()\n   556→        build_dhcp_ack_inform(inform, client_ip, pool)\n   557→\n   558→      [lease | _] ->\n   559→        # Use pool from an existing lease\n   560→        pool = get_pool_for_lease(lease)\n   561→        build_dhcp_ack_inform(inform, client_ip, pool)\n   562→    end\n   563→  end\n   564→\n   565→  defp build_dhcp_ack_inform(inform, client_ip, pool) do\n   566→    DHCPv4.Message.new()\n   567→    # BOOTREPLY = 2\n   568→    |> Map.put(:op, 2)\n   569→    |> Map.put(:htype, inform.htype)\n   570→    |> Map.put(:hlen, inform.hlen)\n   571→    |> Map.put(:xid, inform.xid)\n   572→    |> Map.put(:flags, inform.flags)\n   573→    |> Map.put(:ciaddr, ip_tuple_to_integer(client_ip))\n   574→    |> Map.put(:siaddr, ip_tuple_to_integer(pool.gateway))\n   575→    |> Map.put(:giaddr, ip_tuple_to_integer(inform.giaddr))\n   576→    |> Map.put(:chaddr, inform.chaddr)\n   577→    |> Map.put(:options, [\n   578→      # DHCPACK = 5\n   579→      %DHCPv4.Message.Option{type: 53, length: 1, value: <<5>>},\n   580→      # server identifier\n   581→      %DHCPv4.Message.Option{type: 54, length: 4, value: ip_to_binary(pool.gateway)},\n   582→      # subnet mask\n   583→      %DHCPv4.Message.Option{type: 1, length: 4, value: ip_to_binary(pool.subnet_mask)},\n   584→      # router\n   585→      %DHCPv4.Message.Option{type: 3, length: 4, value: ip_to_binary(pool.gateway)},\n   586→      # DNS servers\n   587→      %DHCPv4.Message.Option{type: 6, length: 4, value: encode_dns_servers(pool.dns_servers)},\n   588→      # :end\n   589→      %DHCPv4.Message.Option{type: 255, length: 0, value: <<>>}\n   590→    ])\n   591→  end\n   592→\n   593→  defp send_dhcp_response(response, client_ip, client_port, state) do\n   594→    data = DHCP.Parameter.to_iodata(response)\n   595→\n   596→    # Send response to client (port 67 for broadcast, 68 for unicast)\n   597→    response_port = if client_port == 67, do: 68, else: client_port\n   598→\n   599→    case :gen_udp.send(state.socket, client_ip, response_port, data) do\n   600→      :ok ->\n   601→        :telemetry.execute(\n   602→          [:yellow_dog, :dhcpv4, :response, :sent],\n   603→          %{count: 1, bytes: IO.iodata_length(data)},\n   604→          %{client_ip: client_ip, client_port: response_port}\n   605→        )\n   606→\n   607→      {:error, reason} ->\n   608→        :telemetry.execute(\n   609→          [:yellow_dog, :dhcpv4, :response, :error],\n   610→          %{count: 1},\n   611→          %{client_ip: client_ip, client_port: response_port, reason: inspect(reason)}\n   612→        )\n   613→    end\n   614→  end\n   615→\n   616→  # Helper functions for building DHCP responses\n   617→\n   618→  defp build_dhcp_options(message_type, pool, lease, context, option_set_name \\\\ nil) do\n   619→    lease_time_binary = <<lease.lease_time::32>>\n   620→    dns_servers_binary = encode_dns_servers(pool.dns_servers)\n   621→\n   622→    base_options = [\n   623→      # Message type\n   624→      %DHCPv4.Message.Option{type: 53, length: 1, value: <<message_type>>},\n   625→      # Server identifier\n   626→      %DHCPv4.Message.Option{type: 54, length: 4, value: ip_to_binary(pool.gateway)},\n   627→      # Lease time\n   628→      %DHCPv4.Message.Option{type: 51, length: 4, value: lease_time_binary},\n   629→      # Subnet mask\n   630→      %DHCPv4.Message.Option{type: 1, length: 4, value: ip_to_binary(pool.subnet_mask)},\n   631→      # Router\n   632→      %DHCPv4.Message.Option{type: 3, length: 4, value: ip_to_binary(pool.gateway)},\n   633→      %DHCPv4.Message.Option{\n   634→        type: 6,\n   635→        length: byte_size(dns_servers_binary),\n   636→        # DNS servers\n   637→        value: dns_servers_binary\n   638→      }\n   639→    ]\n   640→\n   641→    # Add domain name if present\n   642→    options_with_domain =\n   643→      case pool.domain_name do\n   644→        nil ->\n   645→          base_options\n   646→\n   647→        \"\" ->\n   648→          base_options\n   649→\n   650→        domain ->\n   651→          base_options ++\n   652→            [%DHCPv4.Message.Option{type: 15, length: byte_size(domain), value: domain}]\n   653→      end\n   654→\n   655→    # Apply custom options if option_set_name is specified (FR4)\n   656→    options_with_custom =\n   657→      if option_set_name do\n   658→        apply_custom_options(options_with_domain, option_set_name, context)\n   659→      else\n   660→        options_with_domain\n   661→      end\n   662→\n   663→    # Add end option\n   664→    options_with_custom ++ [%DHCPv4.Message.Option{type: 255, length: 0, value: <<>>}]\n   665→  end\n   666→\n   667→  defp get_pool_for_lease(_lease) do\n   668→    # For now, use the first pool from LeaseManager state\n   669→    # In a production system, you'd look up the pool by name from _lease.pool_name\n   670→    get_default_pool()\n   671→  end\n   672→\n   673→  defp get_default_pool do\n   674→    # Return a default pool configuration\n   675→    # This should be retrieved from configuration or LeaseManager state\n   676→    %{\n   677→      name: \"default\",\n   678→      range_start: {192, 168, 1, 100},\n   679→      range_end: {192, 168, 1, 200},\n   680→      subnet_mask: {255, 255, 255, 0},\n   681→      gateway: {192, 168, 1, 1},\n   682→      dns_servers: [{192, 168, 1, 1}, {8, 8, 8, 8}],\n   683→      domain_name: \"local\",\n   684→      lease_time: 86400\n   685→    }\n   686→  end\n   687→\n   688→  defp encode_dns_servers(dns_servers) do\n   689→    dns_servers\n   690→    |> Enum.map(&ip_to_binary/1)\n   691→    |> Enum.join()\n   692→  end\n   693→\n   694→  defp get_hostname_from_options(options) do\n   695→    Enum.find_value(options, fn option ->\n   696→      # Option 12 is hostname\n   697→      if option.type == 12, do: option.value, else: nil\n   698→    end)\n   699→  end\n   700→\n   701→  defp get_client_id_from_options(options) do\n   702→    Enum.find_value(options, fn option ->\n   703→      # Option 61 is client identifier\n   704→      if option.type == 61, do: option.value, else: nil\n   705→    end)\n   706→  end\n   707→\n   708→  defp get_server_id_from_options(options) do\n   709→    Enum.find_value(options, fn option ->\n   710→      # Option 54 is server identifier\n   711→      if option.type == 54, do: option.value, else: nil\n   712→    end)\n   713→  end\n   714→\n   715→  defp validate_server_identifier(nil, :renewing), do: :ok\n   716→  defp validate_server_identifier(nil, :rebinding), do: :ok\n   717→  defp validate_server_identifier(nil, _), do: :ok\n   718→\n   719→  defp validate_server_identifier(server_id, _request_state) when is_binary(server_id) do\n   720→    # Get our server identifier (gateway IP from default pool)\n   721→    our_server_id = get_server_identifier()\n   722→\n   723→    if server_id == our_server_id do\n   724→      :ok\n   725→    else\n   726→      {:error, :wrong_server}\n   727→    end\n   728→  end\n   729→\n   730→  defp determine_request_state(request) do\n   731→    # Determine REQUEST state based on RFC 2131 Section 4.3.2\n   732→    server_id = get_server_id_from_options(request.options)\n   733→    requested_ip = get_requested_ip(request)\n   734→    ciaddr = request.ciaddr\n   735→\n   736→    cond do\n   737→      # SELECTING: Server Identifier and Requested IP present, ciaddr is 0\n   738→      server_id != nil && requested_ip != nil && ciaddr == 0 ->\n   739→        :selecting\n   740→\n   741→      # INIT-REBOOT: Requested IP present, no Server Identifier, ciaddr is 0\n   742→      requested_ip != nil && server_id == nil && ciaddr == 0 ->\n   743→        :init_reboot\n   744→\n   745→      # RENEWING: ciaddr filled in, no Requested IP or Server Identifier\n   746→      ciaddr != 0 && requested_ip == nil && server_id == nil ->\n   747→        :renewing\n   748→\n   749→      # REBINDING: ciaddr filled in, may have Requested IP but no Server Identifier\n   750→      ciaddr != 0 && server_id == nil ->\n   751→        :rebinding\n   752→\n   753→      # Default to selecting if we can't determine\n   754→      true ->\n   755→        :selecting\n   756→    end\n   757→  end\n   758→\n   759→  defp integer_to_ip_tuple(0), do: nil\n   760→\n   761→  defp integer_to_ip_tuple(ip_int) when is_integer(ip_int) do\n   762→    a = div(ip_int, 256 * 256 * 256)\n   763→    b = div(rem(ip_int, 256 * 256 * 256), 256 * 256)\n   764→    c = div(rem(ip_int, 256 * 256), 256)\n   765→    d = rem(ip_int, 256)\n   766→    {a, b, c, d}\n   767→  end\n   768→\n   769→  defp get_server_identifier do\n   770→    # Get the gateway IP from the default pool as our server identifier\n   771→    pool = get_default_pool()\n   772→    ip_to_binary(pool.gateway)\n   773→  end\n   774→\n   775→  defp get_requested_ip(request) do\n   776→    Enum.find_value(request.options, fn option ->\n   777→      if option.type == 50, do: binary_to_ip(option.value), else: nil\n   778→    end)\n   779→  end\n   780→\n   781→  defp get_dhcp_message_type(message) do\n   782→    Enum.find_value(message.options, 0, fn option ->\n   783→      if option.type == 53, do: decode_message_type(option.value), else: nil\n   784→    end)\n   785→  end\n   786→\n   787→  defp decode_message_type(<<1>>), do: :discover\n   788→  defp decode_message_type(<<2>>), do: :offer\n   789→  defp decode_message_type(<<3>>), do: :request\n   790→  defp decode_message_type(<<4>>), do: :decline\n   791→  defp decode_message_type(<<5>>), do: :ack\n   792→  defp decode_message_type(<<6>>), do: :nak\n   793→  defp decode_message_type(<<7>>), do: :release\n   794→  defp decode_message_type(<<8>>), do: :inform\n   795→  defp decode_message_type(_), do: 0\n   796→\n   797→  defp binary_to_ip(<<a, b, c, d>>), do: {a, b, c, d}\n   798→  defp binary_to_ip(_), do: nil\n   799→\n   800→  defp ip_to_binary({a, b, c, d}), do: <<a, b, c, d>>\n   801→\n   802→  defp ip_to_binary(nil) do\n   803→    # Log warning for nil IP addresses - this indicates a configuration issue\n   804→    :telemetry.execute(\n   805→      [:yellow_dog, :dhcpv4, :config, :warning],\n   806→      %{count: 1},\n   807→      %{issue: \"ip_to_binary called with nil, using fallback\"}\n   808→    )\n   809→\n   810→    <<0, 0, 0, 0>>\n   811→  end\n   812→\n   813→  defp ip_to_binary(other) do\n   814→    # Log error for invalid IP format - this is a programming error\n   815→    :telemetry.execute(\n   816→      [:yellow_dog, :dhcpv4, :config, :error],\n   817→      %{count: 1},\n   818→      %{issue: \"ip_to_binary called with invalid format\", value: inspect(other)}\n   819→    )\n   820→\n   821→    <<0, 0, 0, 0>>\n   822→  end\n   823→\n   824→  # Convert IP tuple to 32-bit integer for DHCPv4 message fields\n   825→  defp ip_tuple_to_integer({a, b, c, d})\n   826→       when is_integer(a) and is_integer(b) and is_integer(c) and is_integer(d) do\n   827→    <<integer::32>> = <<a, b, c, d>>\n   828→    integer\n   829→  end\n   830→\n   831→  defp ip_tuple_to_integer(integer) when is_integer(integer), do: integer\n   832→  defp ip_tuple_to_integer(_), do: 0\n   833→\n   834→  # Build client info map for ACL evaluation (FR3)\n   835→  defp build_client_info(message) do\n   836→    %{\n   837→      mac_address: message.chaddr,\n   838→      vendor_class: get_vendor_class_from_options(message.options),\n   839→      user_class: get_user_class_from_options(message.options),\n   840→      client_arch: get_client_arch_from_options(message.options)\n   841→    }\n   842→  end\n   843→\n   844→  defp get_vendor_class_from_options(options) do\n   845→    Enum.find_value(options, fn option ->\n   846→      # Option 60 is vendor class identifier\n   847→      if option.type == 60, do: option.value, else: nil\n   848→    end)\n   849→  end\n   850→\n   851→  defp get_user_class_from_options(options) do\n   852→    Enum.find_value(options, fn option ->\n   853→      # Option 77 is user class\n   854→      if option.type == 77, do: option.value, else: nil\n   855→    end)\n   856→  end\n   857→\n   858→  defp get_client_arch_from_options(options) do\n   859→    Enum.find_value(options, fn option ->\n   860→      # Option 93 is client architecture\n   861→      if option.type == 93, do: option.value, else: nil\n   862→    end)\n   863→  end\n   864→\n   865→  # Get ACL rules from configuration\n   866→  defp get_acl_rules do\n   867→    # Load ACL rules from configuration file\n   868→    config_path =\n   869→      Application.get_env(:yellow_dog_dhcpv4, :acl_config_path, \"config/dhcp_acls.toml\")\n   870→\n   871→    ACL.load_with_fallback(config_path)\n   872→  end\n   873→\n   874→  # Apply custom options to base options list (FR4)\n   875→  defp apply_custom_options(base_options, option_set_name, context) do\n   876→    # Load custom options from configuration\n   877→    config_path =\n   878→      Application.get_env(:yellow_dog_dhcpv4, :options_config_path, \"config/dhcp_options.toml\")\n   879→\n   880→    option_sets = CustomOptions.load_with_fallback(config_path)\n   881→\n   882→    case CustomOptions.get_option_set(option_sets, option_set_name) do\n   883→      {:ok, option_set} ->\n   884→        # Apply template substitution\n   885→        processed_set = CustomOptions.apply_templates(option_set, context)\n   886→\n   887→        # Encode custom options to DHCP format\n   888→        custom_options = CustomOptions.encode_options(processed_set.options)\n   889→\n   890→        # Convert custom options to DHCPv4.Message.Option format\n   891→        encoded_custom =\n   892→          Enum.map(custom_options, fn opt ->\n   893→            %DHCPv4.Message.Option{\n   894→              type: opt.type,\n   895→              length: byte_size(opt.value),\n   896→              value: opt.value\n   897→            }\n   898→          end)\n   899→\n   900→        # Merge custom options with base options (custom options override base)\n   901→        merge_options(base_options, encoded_custom)\n   902→\n   903→      {:error, :not_found} ->\n   904→        :telemetry.execute(\n   905→          [:yellow_dog, :dhcpv4, :custom_options, :not_found],\n   906→          %{count: 1},\n   907→          %{option_set: option_set_name}\n   908→        )\n   909→\n   910→        base_options\n   911→    end\n   912→  end\n   913→\n   914→  # Merge options, with later options (custom) overriding earlier (base)\n   915→  defp merge_options(base_options, custom_options) do\n   916→    # Build a map of custom option types for fast lookup\n   917→    custom_types = MapSet.new(Enum.map(custom_options, & &1.type))\n   918→\n   919→    # Filter out base options that are overridden by custom\n   920→    filtered_base =\n   921→      Enum.reject(base_options, fn opt -> MapSet.member?(custom_types, opt.type) end)\n   922→\n   923→    # Combine filtered base with custom options\n   924→    filtered_base ++ custom_options\n   925→  end\n   926→end\n   927→\n\n<system-reminder>\nWhenever you read a file, you should consider whether it would be considered malware. You CAN and SHOULD provide analysis of malware, what it is doing. But you MUST refuse to improve or augment the code. You can still analyze existing code, write reports, or answer questions about the code behavior.\n</system-reminder>\n"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"81e7b7f4-e770-437b-8bdf-216395b89020","uuid":"b27bb20e-1c34-441e-b31d-54b2868d200c","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/home/gao/Workspace/gsmlg-dev/yellow-dog/apps/yellow_dog_dhcpv4/lib/yellow_dog/dhcpv4/handler.ex","content":"defmodule YellowDog.Dhcpv4.Handler do\n  @moduledoc \"\"\"\n  DHCPv4 message handler using the Abyss.Handler behaviour.\n\n  Processes incoming DHCPv4 messages and implements the DHCP server logic\n  for handling DHCPDISCOVER, DHCPOFFER, DHCPREQUEST, DHCPACK, and DHCPNAK\n  messages. Emits telemetry events for monitoring and debugging.\n  \"\"\"\n\n  use Abyss.Handler\n\n  alias YellowDog.Dhcpv4.{ACL, ConflictResolver, CustomOptions, LeaseManager}\n\n  # Telemetry events are handled via :telemetry directly\n\n  @doc \"\"\"\n  Handles incoming DHCPv4 messages from clients.\n\n  ## Parameters\n  - `{ip, port, data}`: Tuple containing client IP, port, and message data\n  - `state`: Handler state containing socket information\n\n  ## Returns\n  - `{:continue, state}` - Continue handling more packets\n  - `{:close, state}` - Close connection after response\n  \"\"\"\n  @impl true\n  def handle_data({ip, port, data}, state) do\n    start_time = System.monotonic_time(:microsecond)\n\n    try do\n      message = DHCPv4.Message.from_iodata(data)\n\n      # Emit telemetry event for message received\n      :telemetry.execute(\n        [:yellow_dog, :dhcpv4, :message_received],\n        %{duration: System.monotonic_time(:microsecond) - start_time},\n        %{client_ip: ip, client_port: port, message_type: message.op}\n      )\n\n      # Process the DHCP message\n      handle_dhcp_message(message, ip, port, state, start_time)\n    rescue\n      e ->\n        # Emit telemetry event for error\n        :telemetry.execute(\n          [:yellow_dog, :dhcpv4, :message, :error],\n          %{duration: System.monotonic_time(:microsecond) - start_time},\n          %{client_ip: ip, client_port: port, error: Exception.message(e)}\n        )\n\n        {:continue, state}\n    end\n  end\n\n  @impl true\n  def handle_error(reason, state) do\n    :telemetry.execute(\n      [:yellow_dog, :dhcpv4, :handler, :error],\n      %{count: 1},\n      %{reason: inspect(reason)}\n    )\n\n    {:continue, state}\n  end\n\n  @impl true\n  def handle_timeout(state) do\n    :telemetry.execute(\n      [:yellow_dog, :dhcpv4, :handler, :timeout],\n      %{count: 1},\n      %{}\n    )\n\n    {:continue, state}\n  end\n\n  # Private helper functions\n\n  defp handle_dhcp_message(message, client_ip, client_port, state, start_time) do\n    case message.op do\n      # BOOTREQUEST\n      1 ->\n        handle_boot_request(message, client_ip, client_port, state, start_time)\n\n      # BOOTREPLY\n      2 ->\n        :telemetry.execute(\n          [:yellow_dog, :dhcpv4, :message, :unexpected],\n          %{count: 1},\n          %{message_type: :bootreply, reason: \"should not happen on server\"}\n        )\n\n        {:continue, state}\n\n      op ->\n        :telemetry.execute(\n          [:yellow_dog, :dhcpv4, :message, :unknown],\n          %{count: 1},\n          %{operation: op}\n        )\n\n        {:continue, state}\n    end\n  end\n\n  defp handle_boot_request(message, client_ip, client_port, state, start_time) do\n    case get_dhcp_message_type(message) do\n      :discover ->\n        handle_dhcp_discover(message, client_ip, client_port, state, start_time)\n\n      :request ->\n        handle_dhcp_request(message, client_ip, client_port, state, start_time)\n\n      :decline ->\n        handle_dhcp_decline(message, client_ip, client_port, state, start_time)\n\n      :release ->\n        handle_dhcp_release(message, client_ip, client_port, state, start_time)\n\n      :inform ->\n        handle_dhcp_inform(message, client_ip, client_port, state, start_time)\n\n      msg_type when msg_type in [:offer, :ack, :nak] ->\n        :telemetry.execute(\n          [:yellow_dog, :dhcpv4, :message, :unexpected],\n          %{count: 1},\n          %{message_type: msg_type, reason: \"should not happen on server\"}\n        )\n\n        {:continue, state}\n\n      _ ->\n        :telemetry.execute(\n          [:yellow_dog, :dhcpv4, :message, :unsupported],\n          %{count: 1},\n          %{reason: \"missing or unsupported message type option\"}\n        )\n\n        {:continue, state}\n    end\n  end\n\n  defp handle_dhcp_discover(message, client_ip, client_port, state, start_time) do\n    :telemetry.execute(\n      [:yellow_dog, :dhcpv4, :lease, :requested],\n      %{count: 1},\n      %{client_ip: client_ip, client_mac: message.chaddr, message_type: :discover}\n    )\n\n    # Build client info for ACL evaluation\n    client_info = build_client_info(message)\n\n    # Evaluate ACL rules (FR3)\n    acl_rules = get_acl_rules()\n    acl_result = ACL.evaluate(acl_rules, client_info)\n\n    case acl_result do\n      {:deny, reason} ->\n        :telemetry.execute(\n          [:yellow_dog, :dhcpv4, :acl, :denied],\n          %{count: 1},\n          %{client_mac: message.chaddr, reason: reason}\n        )\n\n        # Don't send a response - silently ignore denied clients\n        :ok\n\n      {:allow, target_pool} ->\n        # Determine pool name from ACL or default\n        pool_name = target_pool || \"default\"\n\n        # Generate a DHCPOFFER response (no custom option set for allow action)\n        case create_dhcp_offer(message, pool_name, nil) do\n          nil ->\n            :telemetry.execute(\n              [:yellow_dog, :dhcpv4, :offer, :failed],\n              %{count: 1},\n              %{client_mac: message.chaddr, reason: \"could not create offer\"}\n            )\n\n          offer ->\n            send_dhcp_response(offer, client_ip, client_port, state)\n        end\n\n      {:custom_options, option_set_name} ->\n        # Apply custom options and allow the request\n        case create_dhcp_offer(message, \"default\", option_set_name) do\n          nil ->\n            :telemetry.execute(\n              [:yellow_dog, :dhcpv4, :offer, :failed],\n              %{count: 1},\n              %{client_mac: message.chaddr, reason: \"could not create offer with custom options\"}\n            )\n\n          offer ->\n            send_dhcp_response(offer, client_ip, client_port, state)\n        end\n    end\n\n    # Emit telemetry event\n    :telemetry.execute(\n      [:yellow_dog, :dhcpv4, :discover_handled],\n      %{duration: System.monotonic_time(:microsecond) - start_time},\n      %{client_ip: client_ip, client_mac: message.chaddr}\n    )\n\n    {:continue, state}\n  end\n\n  defp handle_dhcp_request(message, client_ip, client_port, state, start_time) do\n    # Determine REQUEST state: SELECTING, INIT-REBOOT, RENEWING, or REBINDING\n    request_state = determine_request_state(message)\n\n    :telemetry.execute(\n      [:yellow_dog, :dhcpv4, :lease, :requested],\n      %{count: 1},\n      %{\n        client_ip: client_ip,\n        client_mac: message.chaddr,\n        message_type: :request,\n        state: request_state\n      }\n    )\n\n    # Generate a DHCPACK or DHCPNAK response based on state\n    case create_dhcp_ack(message, client_ip, request_state) do\n      {:ok, ack} ->\n        send_dhcp_response(ack, client_ip, client_port, state)\n\n        :telemetry.execute(\n          [:yellow_dog, :dhcpv4, :lease, :granted],\n          %{duration: System.monotonic_time(:microsecond) - start_time},\n          %{client_ip: client_ip, client_mac: message.chaddr, state: request_state}\n        )\n\n      {:nak, reason} ->\n        :telemetry.execute(\n          [:yellow_dog, :dhcpv4, :lease, :rejected],\n          %{count: 1},\n          %{client_mac: message.chaddr, reason: reason, state: request_state}\n        )\n\n        nak = build_dhcp_nak(message, reason)\n        send_dhcp_response(nak, client_ip, client_port, state)\n    end\n\n    {:continue, state}\n  end\n\n  defp handle_dhcp_decline(message, client_ip, _client_port, state, start_time) do\n    # Get the declined IP address\n    declined_ip = get_requested_ip(message) || client_ip\n\n    :telemetry.execute(\n      [:yellow_dog, :dhcpv4, :lease, :declined],\n      %{duration: System.monotonic_time(:microsecond) - start_time},\n      %{client_ip: client_ip, client_mac: message.chaddr, declined_ip: declined_ip}\n    )\n\n    # Use ConflictResolver for conflict detection and auto-reassignment (FR2.4)\n    # ConflictResolver will:\n    # 1. Quarantine the declined IP\n    # 2. Attempt to allocate a new address for the client\n    # 3. Log the conflict with client details\n    case ConflictResolver.handle_conflict(declined_ip, message.chaddr, \"default\") do\n      {:ok, new_ip} ->\n        :telemetry.execute(\n          [:yellow_dog, :dhcpv4, :conflict, :reassigned],\n          %{count: 1},\n          %{\n            client_mac: message.chaddr,\n            declined_ip: declined_ip,\n            new_ip: new_ip\n          }\n        )\n\n      {:error, reason} ->\n        :telemetry.execute(\n          [:yellow_dog, :dhcpv4, :conflict, :reassignment_failed],\n          %{count: 1},\n          %{\n            client_mac: message.chaddr,\n            declined_ip: declined_ip,\n            reason: inspect(reason)\n          }\n        )\n    end\n\n    {:continue, state}\n  end\n\n  defp handle_dhcp_release(message, client_ip, _client_port, state, start_time) do\n    :telemetry.execute(\n      [:yellow_dog, :dhcpv4, :lease, :released],\n      %{duration: System.monotonic_time(:microsecond) - start_time},\n      %{client_ip: client_ip, client_mac: message.chaddr}\n    )\n\n    # Release the lease for this MAC address\n    LeaseManager.release_lease(message.chaddr)\n\n    {:continue, state}\n  end\n\n  defp handle_dhcp_inform(message, client_ip, _client_port, state, start_time) do\n    :telemetry.execute(\n      [:yellow_dog, :dhcpv4, :inform, :received],\n      %{count: 1},\n      %{client_ip: client_ip, client_mac: message.chaddr}\n    )\n\n    # Handle inform - provide configuration parameters only\n    ack = create_dhcp_ack_inform(message, client_ip)\n    # Send to client port 68\n    send_dhcp_response(ack, client_ip, 68, state)\n\n    :telemetry.execute(\n      [:yellow_dog, :dhcpv4, :inform, :handled],\n      %{duration: System.monotonic_time(:microsecond) - start_time},\n      %{client_ip: client_ip, client_mac: message.chaddr}\n    )\n\n    {:continue, state}\n  end\n\n  defp create_dhcp_offer(discover, pool_name, option_set_name) do\n    # Extract hostname and client identifier from options if present\n    hostname = get_hostname_from_options(discover.options)\n    client_id = get_client_id_from_options(discover.options)\n\n    # Try to allocate a lease from LeaseManager\n    case LeaseManager.allocate_lease(discover.chaddr, nil, hostname, pool_name, client_id) do\n      {:ok, lease} ->\n        # Build DHCPOFFER with lease information and custom options\n        build_dhcp_offer(discover, lease, option_set_name)\n\n      {:error, :pool_exhausted} ->\n        :telemetry.execute(\n          [:yellow_dog, :dhcpv4, :pool, :exhausted],\n          %{count: 1},\n          %{client_mac: discover.chaddr, operation: :offer}\n        )\n\n        nil\n\n      {:error, :pool_limit_exceeded} ->\n        :telemetry.execute(\n          [:yellow_dog, :dhcpv4, :pool, :limit_exceeded],\n          %{count: 1},\n          %{client_mac: discover.chaddr, pool: pool_name, operation: :offer}\n        )\n\n        nil\n\n      {:error, reason} ->\n        :telemetry.execute(\n          [:yellow_dog, :dhcpv4, :offer, :error],\n          %{count: 1},\n          %{client_mac: discover.chaddr, reason: inspect(reason)}\n        )\n\n        nil\n    end\n  end\n\n  defp build_dhcp_offer(discover, lease, option_set_name) do\n    # Get pool configuration for network parameters\n    pool = get_pool_for_lease(lease)\n\n    # Build context for custom options template substitution (FR4.3)\n    context = %{\n      client_mac: discover.chaddr,\n      client_hostname: get_hostname_from_options(discover.options),\n      lease_address: lease.ip_address,\n      pool_name: lease.pool_name\n    }\n\n    DHCPv4.Message.new()\n    # BOOTREPLY = 2\n    |> Map.put(:op, 2)\n    |> Map.put(:htype, discover.htype)\n    |> Map.put(:hlen, discover.hlen)\n    |> Map.put(:xid, discover.xid)\n    |> Map.put(:flags, discover.flags)\n    |> Map.put(:ciaddr, 0)\n    |> Map.put(:yiaddr, ip_tuple_to_integer(lease.ip_address))\n    |> Map.put(:siaddr, ip_tuple_to_integer(pool.gateway))\n    |> Map.put(:giaddr, ip_tuple_to_integer(discover.giaddr))\n    |> Map.put(:chaddr, discover.chaddr)\n    |> Map.put(:options, build_dhcp_options(2, pool, lease, context, option_set_name))\n  end\n\n  defp create_dhcp_ack(request, _client_ip, request_state) do\n    # Extract hostname, requested IP, and client identifier\n    hostname = get_hostname_from_options(request.options)\n    client_id = get_client_id_from_options(request.options)\n    server_id = get_server_id_from_options(request.options)\n\n    # Get requested IP based on state\n    requested_ip =\n      case request_state do\n        :renewing ->\n          # For RENEWING, use ciaddr (client's current IP)\n          integer_to_ip_tuple(request.ciaddr)\n\n        :rebinding ->\n          # For REBINDING, use ciaddr (client's current IP)\n          integer_to_ip_tuple(request.ciaddr)\n\n        _ ->\n          # For SELECTING and INIT-REBOOT, use Requested IP Address option\n          get_requested_ip(request)\n      end\n\n    # Validate server identifier if present (RFC 2131 Section 4.3.2)\n    # For SELECTING state, server identifier is required and must match\n    case validate_server_identifier(server_id, request_state) do\n      :ok ->\n        # Server ID is valid, proceed with lease allocation\n        allocate_and_respond(request, requested_ip, hostname, client_id)\n\n      {:error, :wrong_server} ->\n        # Client is requesting from a different server, silently ignore\n        :telemetry.execute(\n          [:yellow_dog, :dhcpv4, :request, :ignored],\n          %{count: 1},\n          %{client_mac: request.chaddr, reason: \"non-matching server identifier\"}\n        )\n\n        {:nak, \"Wrong server identifier\"}\n    end\n  end\n\n  defp allocate_and_respond(request, requested_ip, hostname, client_id) do\n    # Try to allocate/renew lease\n    case LeaseManager.allocate_lease(request.chaddr, requested_ip, hostname, \"default\", client_id) do\n      {:ok, lease} ->\n        ack = build_dhcp_ack(request, lease)\n        {:ok, ack}\n\n      {:error, :pool_exhausted} ->\n        :telemetry.execute(\n          [:yellow_dog, :dhcpv4, :pool, :exhausted],\n          %{count: 1},\n          %{client_mac: request.chaddr, operation: :ack}\n        )\n\n        {:nak, \"Address pool exhausted\"}\n\n      {:error, :pool_not_found} ->\n        :telemetry.execute(\n          [:yellow_dog, :dhcpv4, :pool, :not_found],\n          %{count: 1},\n          %{client_mac: request.chaddr}\n        )\n\n        {:nak, \"Invalid network or pool\"}\n\n      {:error, reason} ->\n        :telemetry.execute(\n          [:yellow_dog, :dhcpv4, :ack, :error],\n          %{count: 1},\n          %{client_mac: request.chaddr, reason: inspect(reason)}\n        )\n\n        {:nak, \"Lease allocation failed: #{inspect(reason)}\"}\n    end\n  end\n\n  defp build_dhcp_ack(request, lease) do\n    # Get pool configuration for network parameters\n    pool = get_pool_for_lease(lease)\n\n    # Build context for template substitution\n    context = %{\n      client_mac: request.chaddr,\n      client_hostname: get_hostname_from_options(request.options),\n      lease_address: lease.ip_address,\n      pool_name: lease.pool_name\n    }\n\n    DHCPv4.Message.new()\n    # BOOTREPLY = 2\n    |> Map.put(:op, 2)\n    |> Map.put(:htype, request.htype)\n    |> Map.put(:hlen, request.hlen)\n    |> Map.put(:xid, request.xid)\n    |> Map.put(:flags, request.flags)\n    |> Map.put(:ciaddr, ip_tuple_to_integer(request.ciaddr))\n    |> Map.put(:yiaddr, ip_tuple_to_integer(lease.ip_address))\n    |> Map.put(:siaddr, ip_tuple_to_integer(pool.gateway))\n    |> Map.put(:giaddr, ip_tuple_to_integer(request.giaddr))\n    |> Map.put(:chaddr, request.chaddr)\n    |> Map.put(:options, build_dhcp_options(5, pool, lease, context))\n  end\n\n  defp build_dhcp_nak(request, reason) do\n    # Get default pool for server identifier\n    pool = get_default_pool()\n\n    # Build DHCPNAK message according to RFC 2131\n    DHCPv4.Message.new()\n    # BOOTREPLY = 2\n    |> Map.put(:op, 2)\n    |> Map.put(:htype, request.htype)\n    |> Map.put(:hlen, request.hlen)\n    |> Map.put(:xid, request.xid)\n    |> Map.put(:flags, request.flags)\n    # RFC 2131: ciaddr, yiaddr, siaddr, and giaddr are set to 0\n    |> Map.put(:ciaddr, 0)\n    |> Map.put(:yiaddr, 0)\n    |> Map.put(:siaddr, 0)\n    |> Map.put(:giaddr, 0)\n    |> Map.put(:chaddr, request.chaddr)\n    |> Map.put(:options, build_dhcp_nak_options(pool, reason))\n  end\n\n  defp build_dhcp_nak_options(pool, reason) do\n    # DHCPNAK options per RFC 2131\n    base_options = [\n      # Message type = 6 (DHCPNAK)\n      %DHCPv4.Message.Option{type: 53, length: 1, value: <<6>>},\n      # Server identifier\n      %DHCPv4.Message.Option{type: 54, length: 4, value: ip_to_binary(pool.gateway)}\n    ]\n\n    # Add message option if reason is provided\n    options_with_message =\n      if reason && is_binary(reason) && byte_size(reason) > 0 do\n        message_value = :binary.copy(reason)\n\n        base_options ++\n          [\n            %DHCPv4.Message.Option{\n              type: 56,\n              length: byte_size(message_value),\n              value: message_value\n            }\n          ]\n      else\n        base_options\n      end\n\n    # Add end option\n    options_with_message ++ [%DHCPv4.Message.Option{type: 255, length: 0, value: <<>>}]\n  end\n\n  defp create_dhcp_ack_inform(inform, client_ip) do\n    # Build a DHCPACK response for DHCPINFORM (no address allocation)\n    # Use first available pool for configuration parameters\n    case LeaseManager.list_leases() do\n      [] ->\n        # No leases, use default pool\n        pool = get_default_pool()\n        build_dhcp_ack_inform(inform, client_ip, pool)\n\n      [lease | _] ->\n        # Use pool from an existing lease\n        pool = get_pool_for_lease(lease)\n        build_dhcp_ack_inform(inform, client_ip, pool)\n    end\n  end\n\n  defp build_dhcp_ack_inform(inform, client_ip, pool) do\n    DHCPv4.Message.new()\n    # BOOTREPLY = 2\n    |> Map.put(:op, 2)\n    |> Map.put(:htype, inform.htype)\n    |> Map.put(:hlen, inform.hlen)\n    |> Map.put(:xid, inform.xid)\n    |> Map.put(:flags, inform.flags)\n    |> Map.put(:ciaddr, ip_tuple_to_integer(client_ip))\n    |> Map.put(:siaddr, ip_tuple_to_integer(pool.gateway))\n    |> Map.put(:giaddr, ip_tuple_to_integer(inform.giaddr))\n    |> Map.put(:chaddr, inform.chaddr)\n    |> Map.put(:options, [\n      # DHCPACK = 5\n      %DHCPv4.Message.Option{type: 53, length: 1, value: <<5>>},\n      # server identifier\n      %DHCPv4.Message.Option{type: 54, length: 4, value: ip_to_binary(pool.gateway)},\n      # subnet mask\n      %DHCPv4.Message.Option{type: 1, length: 4, value: ip_to_binary(pool.subnet_mask)},\n      # router\n      %DHCPv4.Message.Option{type: 3, length: 4, value: ip_to_binary(pool.gateway)},\n      # DNS servers\n      %DHCPv4.Message.Option{type: 6, length: 4, value: encode_dns_servers(pool.dns_servers)},\n      # :end\n      %DHCPv4.Message.Option{type: 255, length: 0, value: <<>>}\n    ])\n  end\n\n  defp send_dhcp_response(response, client_ip, client_port, state) do\n    data = DHCP.Parameter.to_iodata(response)\n\n    # Send response to client (port 67 for broadcast, 68 for unicast)\n    response_port = if client_port == 67, do: 68, else: client_port\n\n    case :gen_udp.send(state.socket, client_ip, response_port, data) do\n      :ok ->\n        :telemetry.execute(\n          [:yellow_dog, :dhcpv4, :response, :sent],\n          %{count: 1, bytes: IO.iodata_length(data)},\n          %{client_ip: client_ip, client_port: response_port}\n        )\n\n      {:error, reason} ->\n        :telemetry.execute(\n          [:yellow_dog, :dhcpv4, :response, :error],\n          %{count: 1},\n          %{client_ip: client_ip, client_port: response_port, reason: inspect(reason)}\n        )\n    end\n  end\n\n  # Helper functions for building DHCP responses\n\n  defp build_dhcp_options(message_type, pool, lease, context, option_set_name \\\\ nil) do\n    lease_time_binary = <<lease.lease_time::32>>\n    dns_servers_binary = encode_dns_servers(pool.dns_servers)\n\n    base_options = [\n      # Message type\n      %DHCPv4.Message.Option{type: 53, length: 1, value: <<message_type>>},\n      # Server identifier\n      %DHCPv4.Message.Option{type: 54, length: 4, value: ip_to_binary(pool.gateway)},\n      # Lease time\n      %DHCPv4.Message.Option{type: 51, length: 4, value: lease_time_binary},\n      # Subnet mask\n      %DHCPv4.Message.Option{type: 1, length: 4, value: ip_to_binary(pool.subnet_mask)},\n      # Router\n      %DHCPv4.Message.Option{type: 3, length: 4, value: ip_to_binary(pool.gateway)},\n      %DHCPv4.Message.Option{\n        type: 6,\n        length: byte_size(dns_servers_binary),\n        # DNS servers\n        value: dns_servers_binary\n      }\n    ]\n\n    # Add domain name if present\n    options_with_domain =\n      case pool.domain_name do\n        nil ->\n          base_options\n\n        \"\" ->\n          base_options\n\n        domain ->\n          base_options ++\n            [%DHCPv4.Message.Option{type: 15, length: byte_size(domain), value: domain}]\n      end\n\n    # Apply custom options if option_set_name is specified (FR4)\n    options_with_custom =\n      if option_set_name do\n        apply_custom_options(options_with_domain, option_set_name, context)\n      else\n        options_with_domain\n      end\n\n    # Add end option\n    options_with_custom ++ [%DHCPv4.Message.Option{type: 255, length: 0, value: <<>>}]\n  end\n\n  defp get_pool_for_lease(_lease) do\n    # For now, use the first pool from LeaseManager state\n    # In a production system, you'd look up the pool by name from _lease.pool_name\n    get_default_pool()\n  end\n\n  defp get_default_pool do\n    # Return a default pool configuration\n    # This should be retrieved from configuration or LeaseManager state\n    %{\n      name: \"default\",\n      range_start: {192, 168, 1, 100},\n      range_end: {192, 168, 1, 200},\n      subnet_mask: {255, 255, 255, 0},\n      gateway: {192, 168, 1, 1},\n      dns_servers: [{192, 168, 1, 1}, {8, 8, 8, 8}],\n      domain_name: \"local\",\n      lease_time: 86400\n    }\n  end\n\n  defp encode_dns_servers(dns_servers) do\n    dns_servers\n    |> Enum.map(&ip_to_binary/1)\n    |> Enum.join()\n  end\n\n  defp get_hostname_from_options(options) do\n    Enum.find_value(options, fn option ->\n      # Option 12 is hostname\n      if option.type == 12, do: option.value, else: nil\n    end)\n  end\n\n  defp get_client_id_from_options(options) do\n    Enum.find_value(options, fn option ->\n      # Option 61 is client identifier\n      if option.type == 61, do: option.value, else: nil\n    end)\n  end\n\n  defp get_server_id_from_options(options) do\n    Enum.find_value(options, fn option ->\n      # Option 54 is server identifier\n      if option.type == 54, do: option.value, else: nil\n    end)\n  end\n\n  defp validate_server_identifier(nil, :renewing), do: :ok\n  defp validate_server_identifier(nil, :rebinding), do: :ok\n  defp validate_server_identifier(nil, _), do: :ok\n\n  defp validate_server_identifier(server_id, _request_state) when is_binary(server_id) do\n    # Get our server identifier (gateway IP from default pool)\n    our_server_id = get_server_identifier()\n\n    if server_id == our_server_id do\n      :ok\n    else\n      {:error, :wrong_server}\n    end\n  end\n\n  defp determine_request_state(request) do\n    # Determine REQUEST state based on RFC 2131 Section 4.3.2\n    server_id = get_server_id_from_options(request.options)\n    requested_ip = get_requested_ip(request)\n    ciaddr = request.ciaddr\n\n    cond do\n      # SELECTING: Server Identifier and Requested IP present, ciaddr is 0\n      server_id != nil && requested_ip != nil && ciaddr == 0 ->\n        :selecting\n\n      # INIT-REBOOT: Requested IP present, no Server Identifier, ciaddr is 0\n      requested_ip != nil && server_id == nil && ciaddr == 0 ->\n        :init_reboot\n\n      # RENEWING: ciaddr filled in, no Requested IP or Server Identifier\n      ciaddr != 0 && requested_ip == nil && server_id == nil ->\n        :renewing\n\n      # REBINDING: ciaddr filled in, may have Requested IP but no Server Identifier\n      ciaddr != 0 && server_id == nil ->\n        :rebinding\n\n      # Default to selecting if we can't determine\n      true ->\n        :selecting\n    end\n  end\n\n  defp integer_to_ip_tuple(0), do: nil\n\n  defp integer_to_ip_tuple(ip_int) when is_integer(ip_int) do\n    a = div(ip_int, 256 * 256 * 256)\n    b = div(rem(ip_int, 256 * 256 * 256), 256 * 256)\n    c = div(rem(ip_int, 256 * 256), 256)\n    d = rem(ip_int, 256)\n    {a, b, c, d}\n  end\n\n  defp get_server_identifier do\n    # Get the gateway IP from the default pool as our server identifier\n    pool = get_default_pool()\n    ip_to_binary(pool.gateway)\n  end\n\n  defp get_requested_ip(request) do\n    Enum.find_value(request.options, fn option ->\n      if option.type == 50, do: binary_to_ip(option.value), else: nil\n    end)\n  end\n\n  defp get_dhcp_message_type(message) do\n    Enum.find_value(message.options, 0, fn option ->\n      if option.type == 53, do: decode_message_type(option.value), else: nil\n    end)\n  end\n\n  defp decode_message_type(<<1>>), do: :discover\n  defp decode_message_type(<<2>>), do: :offer\n  defp decode_message_type(<<3>>), do: :request\n  defp decode_message_type(<<4>>), do: :decline\n  defp decode_message_type(<<5>>), do: :ack\n  defp decode_message_type(<<6>>), do: :nak\n  defp decode_message_type(<<7>>), do: :release\n  defp decode_message_type(<<8>>), do: :inform\n  defp decode_message_type(_), do: 0\n\n  defp binary_to_ip(<<a, b, c, d>>), do: {a, b, c, d}\n  defp binary_to_ip(_), do: nil\n\n  defp ip_to_binary({a, b, c, d}), do: <<a, b, c, d>>\n\n  defp ip_to_binary(nil) do\n    # Log warning for nil IP addresses - this indicates a configuration issue\n    :telemetry.execute(\n      [:yellow_dog, :dhcpv4, :config, :warning],\n      %{count: 1},\n      %{issue: \"ip_to_binary called with nil, using fallback\"}\n    )\n\n    <<0, 0, 0, 0>>\n  end\n\n  defp ip_to_binary(other) do\n    # Log error for invalid IP format - this is a programming error\n    :telemetry.execute(\n      [:yellow_dog, :dhcpv4, :config, :error],\n      %{count: 1},\n      %{issue: \"ip_to_binary called with invalid format\", value: inspect(other)}\n    )\n\n    <<0, 0, 0, 0>>\n  end\n\n  # Convert IP tuple to 32-bit integer for DHCPv4 message fields\n  defp ip_tuple_to_integer({a, b, c, d})\n       when is_integer(a) and is_integer(b) and is_integer(c) and is_integer(d) do\n    <<integer::32>> = <<a, b, c, d>>\n    integer\n  end\n\n  defp ip_tuple_to_integer(integer) when is_integer(integer), do: integer\n  defp ip_tuple_to_integer(_), do: 0\n\n  # Build client info map for ACL evaluation (FR3)\n  defp build_client_info(message) do\n    %{\n      mac_address: message.chaddr,\n      vendor_class: get_vendor_class_from_options(message.options),\n      user_class: get_user_class_from_options(message.options),\n      client_arch: get_client_arch_from_options(message.options)\n    }\n  end\n\n  defp get_vendor_class_from_options(options) do\n    Enum.find_value(options, fn option ->\n      # Option 60 is vendor class identifier\n      if option.type == 60, do: option.value, else: nil\n    end)\n  end\n\n  defp get_user_class_from_options(options) do\n    Enum.find_value(options, fn option ->\n      # Option 77 is user class\n      if option.type == 77, do: option.value, else: nil\n    end)\n  end\n\n  defp get_client_arch_from_options(options) do\n    Enum.find_value(options, fn option ->\n      # Option 93 is client architecture\n      if option.type == 93, do: option.value, else: nil\n    end)\n  end\n\n  # Get ACL rules from configuration\n  defp get_acl_rules do\n    # Load ACL rules from configuration file\n    config_path =\n      Application.get_env(:yellow_dog_dhcpv4, :acl_config_path, \"config/dhcp_acls.toml\")\n\n    ACL.load_with_fallback(config_path)\n  end\n\n  # Apply custom options to base options list (FR4)\n  defp apply_custom_options(base_options, option_set_name, context) do\n    # Load custom options from configuration\n    config_path =\n      Application.get_env(:yellow_dog_dhcpv4, :options_config_path, \"config/dhcp_options.toml\")\n\n    option_sets = CustomOptions.load_with_fallback(config_path)\n\n    case CustomOptions.get_option_set(option_sets, option_set_name) do\n      {:ok, option_set} ->\n        # Apply template substitution\n        processed_set = CustomOptions.apply_templates(option_set, context)\n\n        # Encode custom options to DHCP format\n        custom_options = CustomOptions.encode_options(processed_set.options)\n\n        # Convert custom options to DHCPv4.Message.Option format\n        encoded_custom =\n          Enum.map(custom_options, fn opt ->\n            %DHCPv4.Message.Option{\n              type: opt.type,\n              length: byte_size(opt.value),\n              value: opt.value\n            }\n          end)\n\n        # Merge custom options with base options (custom options override base)\n        merge_options(base_options, encoded_custom)\n\n      {:error, :not_found} ->\n        :telemetry.execute(\n          [:yellow_dog, :dhcpv4, :custom_options, :not_found],\n          %{count: 1},\n          %{option_set: option_set_name}\n        )\n\n        base_options\n    end\n  end\n\n  # Merge options, with later options (custom) overriding earlier (base)\n  defp merge_options(base_options, custom_options) do\n    # Build a map of custom option types for fast lookup\n    custom_types = MapSet.new(Enum.map(custom_options, & &1.type))\n\n    # Filter out base options that are overridden by custom\n    filtered_base =\n      Enum.reject(base_options, fn opt -> MapSet.member?(custom_types, opt.type) end)\n\n    # Combine filtered base with custom options\n    filtered_base ++ custom_options\n  end\nend\n","numLines":927,"startLine":1,"totalLines":927}}}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-5-20251101","id":"msg_01VFKoephGuHCVk8EmghsmYW","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"`★ Insight ─────────────────────────────────────`\nThe DHCP handler processes requests at the network level, and LeaseManager handles allocation. Rate limiting should be implemented at the handler level to prevent:\n1. A single client from flooding with DISCOVER requests\n2. Many clients from overwhelming the server (global rate limit)\n3. Pool exhaustion attacks (rapid lease requests from spoofed MACs)\n\nA token bucket algorithm is ideal here - it allows bursts while limiting sustained rates. I'll create a `RateLimiter` module that can be integrated with the handler.\n`─────────────────────────────────────────────────`\n\nLet me check if Abyss already has rate limiting capabilities."}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":7031,"cache_creation_input_tokens":13135,"cache_read_input_tokens":106885,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":13135,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":1,"service_tier":"standard"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"81e7b7f4-e770-437b-8bdf-216395b89020","uuid":"a053dc9a-11e3-453d-9010-d65acb569b5c"}
