ontinuous improvement loop for the YellowDog project. Key directives from the continuation context:\n   - Resume iteration work with PRD at ./prd.md\n   - Read CONTINUITY.md including 'Mistakes & Learnings'\n   - Follow Reason-Act-Reflect-VERIFY cycle\n   - Never ask questions, never wait for confirmation\n   - Execute all enabled SDLC phases (UNIT_TESTS, API_TESTS, etc.)\n   - Work perpetually finding improvements\n   - Continue from where the previous session left off (investigating DNS compression loop vulnerability)\n\n2. Key Technical Concepts:\n   - Elixir umbrella project with 11 apps\n   - Token bucket algorithm for rate limiting\n   - ETS tables for high-performance state storage\n   - GenServer for stateful processes\n   - Telemetry for observability\n   - DNS compression loop detection via visited positions MapSet\n   - Per-client and global rate limiting\n   - Graceful degradation when rate limiter not running\n   - Different rate limits for different services based on traffic patterns\n\n3. Files and Code Sections:\n\n   - **`apps/yellow_dog_dhcpv6/lib/yellow_dog/dhcpv6/rate_limiter.ex`** (created)\n     - Token bucket rate limiter for DHCPv6 DoS protection\n     - Uses ETS table `:dhcpv6_rate_buckets` for state\n     - Handles 8-tuple IPv6 addresses\n     ```elixir\n     defmodule YellowDog.Dhcpv6.RateLimiter do\n       use GenServer\n       @default_config %{\n         enabled: true,\n         client_tokens: 10,\n         client_refill_rate: 2,\n         global_tokens: 1000,\n         global_refill_rate: 100,\n         bucket_ttl: 300_000,\n         cleanup_interval: 60_000\n       }\n       \n       def check_rate(client_id) do\n         GenServer.call(__MODULE__, {:check_rate, client_id})\n       catch\n         :exit, {:noproc, _} -> :ok\n       end\n     end\n     ```\n\n   - **`apps/yellow_dog_dhcpv6/lib/yellow_dog/dhcpv6/handler.ex`** (modified)\n     - Added rate limiting integration at the beginning of handle_data\n     ```elixir\n     alias YellowDog.Dhcpv6.{LeaseManager, RateLimiter}\n     \n     @impl true\n     def handle_data({client_ip, client_port, data}, state) do\n       start_time = System.monotonic_time(:microsecond)\n       case RateLimiter.check_rate(client_ip) do\n         :ok ->\n           process_message(client_ip, client_port, data, state, start_time)\n         {:error, :rate_limited} ->\n           :telemetry.execute([:yellow_dog, :dhcpv6, :message, :rate_limited], %{count: 1}, %{client_ip: client_ip, client_port: client_port})\n           {:continue, state}\n       end\n     end\n     ```\n\n   - **`apps/yellow_dog_dhcpv6/lib/yellow_dog/dhcpv6/supervisor.ex`** (modified)\n     - Added RateLimiter to supervisor children\n     ```elixir\n     # Rate limiter - must start before server for DoS protection\n     YellowDog.Dhcpv6.RateLimiter\n     |> Supervisor.child_spec(id: :rate_limiter),\n     ```\n\n   - **`apps/yellow_dog_dns/lib/yellow_dog/dns/rate_limiter.ex`** (created)\n     - Token bucket rate limiter for DNS with higher burst capacity\n     - Uses ETS table `:dns_rate_buckets`\n     ```elixir\n     @default_config %{\n       enabled: true,\n       client_tokens: 50,\n       client_refill_rate: 20,\n       global_tokens: 5000,\n       global_refill_rate: 1000,\n       bucket_ttl: 300_000,\n       cleanup_interval: 60_000\n     }\n     ```\n\n   - **`apps/yellow_dog_dns/lib/yellow_dog/dns/handler/udp.ex`** (modified)\n     - Added rate limiting before processing DNS requests\n     ```elixir\n     alias YellowDog.Dns.{ConnectionManager, RateLimiter}\n     \n     @impl true\n     def handle_data({client_ip, client_port, data}, state) do\n       case RateLimiter.check_rate(client_ip) do\n         :ok -> process_data(client_ip, client_port, data, state)\n         {:error, :rate_limited} ->\n           Telemetry.warning(\"DNS request rate limited\", %{client_ip: format_ip(client_ip), client_port: client_port})\n           {:continue, state}\n       end\n     end\n     ```\n\n   - **`apps/yellow_dog_mdns/lib/yellow_dog/mdns/rate_limiter.ex`** (created)\n     - Token bucket rate limiter for mDNS with highest burst capacity\n     - Uses ETS table `:mdns_rate_buckets`\n     ```elixir\n     @default_config %{\n       enabled: true,\n       client_tokens: 100,\n       client_refill_rate: 50,\n       global_tokens: 10000,\n       global_refill_rate: 5000,\n       bucket_ttl: 300_000,\n       cleanup_interval: 60_000\n     }\n     ```\n\n   - **`apps/yellow_dog_mdns/lib/yellow_dog/mdns/handler.ex`** (modified)\n     - Added rate limiting integration\n     ```elixir\n     alias YellowDog.Mdns.{MessageCache, NetworkMonitor, RateLimiter, Responder, ServiceRegistry}\n     \n     @impl true\n     def handle_data({ip, port, data}, state) do\n       case RateLimiter.check_rate(ip) do\n         :ok -> process_data(ip, port, data, state)\n         {:error, :rate_limited} ->\n           :telemetry.execute([:yellow_dog, :mdns, :message, :rate_limited], %{count: 1, bytes: byte_size(data)}, %{source_ip: ip, source_port: port})\n           {:continue, state}\n       end\n     end\n     ```\n\n   - **`.loki/CONTINUITY.md`** (modified)\n     - Updated iteration count from 8 to 9\n     - Added Iteration 7 (DHCPv6 rate limiting), Iteration 8 (DNS rate limiting), Iteration 9 (mDNS rate limiting)\n     - Added Rate Limiting Summary table\n     - Updated Known Issues to show all security issues resolved\n     - Added commit 5d535ea to session metadata\n\n4. Errors and fixes:\n   - **Path issues with mix test**:\n     - Error: `Paths given to \"mix test\" did not match any directory/file`\n     - Fix: Run tests from inside the app directory using `cd apps/yellow_dog_dhcpv6 && mix test test/...`\n   \n   - **File not read error**:\n     - Error: `File has not been read yet. Read it first before writing to it.`\n     - Fix: Read the file first before attempting to edit it\n\n5. Problem Solving:\n   - **DNS compression loop vulnerability**: Verified it was already mitigated in ex