ity)` blocked GenServer calls\n   206→- Fix: Changed to `recv(socket, 0, 100)` with retry loop for responsiveness\n   207→\n   208→### Console Config Validation (FIXED - Iteration 2)\n   209→- Location: `config/test.exs`\n   210→- Issue: `code_reloader` set at compile time in dev.exs but missing in test config\n   211→- Fix: Added `code_reloader: false` to test endpoint config\n   212→\n   213→### Security Improvements (Iteration 2)\n   214→1. DNS UDP handler: Added try-rescue for exception handling\n   215→2. DHCPv4: Replaced silent fallback with logging for ip_to_binary\n   216→3. DHCPv6: Added DNS label length validation (max 63 bytes per RFC 1035)\n   217→\n   218→## Mistakes & Learnings\n   219→1. **Umbrella dependency order matters**: When one umbrella app uses modules from another, it must declare the dependency explicitly.\n   220→2. **UDP server tests can be flaky**: Tests involving UDP servers with blocking recv calls can timeout - better to mark as integration tests.\n   221→3. **Handler modules need proper macros**: Protocol handler modules (like DHCPv6) need `use Abyss.Handler` to be supervised correctly.\n   222→4. **Blocking recv prevents GenServer responsiveness**: GenServer calls timeout if the process is blocked in recv(:infinity). Use timeouts with retry.\n   223→5. **Compile-time config needs runtime match**: Phoenix endpoints with compile-time config (like code_reloader) need matching runtime config in all environments.\n   224→6. **Silent fallbacks mask bugs**: Functions like ip_to_binary should log errors instead of silently using default values.\n   225→7. **RFC compliance matters**: DNS labels must be ≤63 bytes; validation prevents buffer issues.\n   226→\n   227→## Architecture Notes\n   228→- 11-app umbrella project\n   229→- Core services: DNS, mDNS, DHCPv4, DHCPv6\n   230→- Infrastructure libs: abyss (UDP), ex_dns (DNS protocol), ex_dhcp (DHCP protocol), geo_ip_db (IP geolocation)\n   231→- Web console: Phoenix LiveView with DaisyUI\n   