{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01N9MwTEigxWDSvj78suMrRb","type":"tool_result","content":"     1→# Loki Mode Continuity\n     2→\n     3→## Current Status\n     4→**Phase**: CONTINUOUS IMPROVEMENT\n     5→**Task**: Performance optimization and additional improvements\n     6→**Iteration**: 11\n     7→\n     8→## Progress\n     9→\n    10→### Completed (Iteration 1)\n    11→- [x] Analyzed codebase structure\n    12→- [x] Identified compilation warning in YellowDog.Application\n    13→- [x] Generated PRD at .loki/generated-prd.md\n    14→- [x] Fixed Abyss.Logger dependency in yellow_dog/mix.exs\n    15→- [x] Verified compilation without warnings\n    16→- [x] Marked flaky integration tests with @tag :integration\n    17→- [x] All tests pass (excluding integration tests by default)\n    18→- [x] Code formatting applied via mix format\n    19→- [x] Credo linting passes - no issues\n    20→- [x] Committed changes (226e25e)\n    21→\n    22→### Completed (Iteration 2)\n    23→- [x] Fixed DHCPv6 Handler missing `use Abyss.Handler` (ff7c617)\n    24→- [x] Fixed Abyss listener blocking recv(:infinity) causing GenServer call timeouts (4dfa6c4)\n    25→- [x] Fixed yellow_dog_console compile-time config validation error (5d119ad)\n    26→- [x] Security audit completed - identified CRITICAL web console auth issue\n    27→- [x] Security fix: DNS UDP handler try-rescue (f287c42)\n    28→- [x] Security fix: DHCPv4 ip_to_binary logging (f287c42)\n    29→- [x] Security fix: DHCPv6 DNS label length validation (f287c42)\n    30→- [x] All 335 tests pass (172 + 163)\n    31→\n    32→### Completed (Iteration 3 - PRD Implementation)\n    33→- [x] Implemented PRD: TOML-based pool configuration loading (FR1)\n    34→  - Created `YellowDog.Dhcpv4.PoolConfig` module\n    35→  - Subnet CIDR parsing with mask calculation\n    36→  - Range validation and IP tuple conversion\n    37→  - Static reservation support (MAC → IP)\n    38→  - Optional field defaults (enabled, lease_time, max_leases, priority)\n    39→- [x] Implemented PRD: Max lease limits per pool (FR1.6, default 1000)\n    40→  - Added `max_leases` field to pool config\n    41→  - Enforced in LeaseManager allocation logic\n    42→- [x] Implemented PRD: ACL rules enforcement (FR3)\n    43→  - Created `YellowDog.Dhcpv4.ACL` module\n    44→  - MAC pattern matching with glob support (e.g., `aa:bb:cc:*`)\n    45→  - Vendor class and user class matching\n    46→  - Priority-ordered rule evaluation\n    47→  - Actions: allow, deny, custom_options with target pool/option set\n    48→- [x] Implemented PRD: Conflict detection and auto-reassignment (FR2.4)\n    49→  - Created `YellowDog.Dhcpv4.ConflictResolver` GenServer\n    50→  - Quarantine management for conflicted IPs\n    51→  - Stats tracking (total conflicts, active quarantines)\n    52→  - Automatic reassignment via LeaseManager integration\n    53→- [x] Implemented PRD: Custom options with template variables (FR4)\n    54→  - Created `YellowDog.Dhcpv4.CustomOptions` module\n    55→  - Type validation: string, ip, ip_list, uint8/16/32, hex\n    56→  - Template substitution: `${client_mac}`, `${client_hostname}`, `${lease_address}`, `${pool_name}`\n    57→  - Option set merging with scope hierarchy\n    58→  - Binary encoding for DHCP packet generation\n    59→- [x] Fixed LeaseManager bugs discovered via testing\n    60→  - `get_pool_config` used Map.get on list → changed to Enum.find\n    61→  - `get_static_reservations` same issue → fixed\n    62→  - Partial config map missing required fields → return full pool struct\n    63→- [x] Added comprehensive unit tests (all 103 DHCPv4 tests pass)\n    64→  - `acl_test.exs` - 25+ test cases\n    65→  - `custom_options_test.exs` - validation and template tests\n    66→  - `conflict_resolver_test.exs` - quarantine and conflict handling tests\n    67→  - `pool_config_test.exs` - TOML parsing and validation tests\n    68→- [x] Integrated PRD modules with DHCPv4 handler (80c73c1)\n    69→  - ACL evaluation in DISCOVER handling (allow/deny/custom_options)\n    70→  - ConflictResolver integration in DECLINE handling\n    71→  - CustomOptions template substitution in responses\n    72→- [x] Added handler integration tests (68c77b3)\n    73→  - DECLINE triggers ConflictResolver\n    74→  - IP quarantine verification\n    75→  - Conflict stats tracking\n    76→- [x] Fixed format_mac to handle 16-byte chaddr field\n    77→- [x] All 105 DHCPv4 tests pass, 1314 tests across all apps\n    78→\n    79→### Completed (Iteration 4 - Test Quality)\n    80→- [x] Reduced test log noise from expected error behaviors\n    81→  - DNS zone auth: Changed to debug level for \"No zone file path configured\"\n    82→  - ZoneService: Added suppress function for expected save errors\n    83→  - Added `@tag :capture_log` to tests that intentionally trigger errors:\n    84→    - `conflict_resolver_test.exs` - conflict handling tests\n    85→    - `handler_test.exs` (DHCPv4) - DECLINE handling tests\n    86→    - `handler_test.exs` (DNS) - error handling tests\n    87→    - `config_test.exs` - missing file and malformed TOML tests\n    88→    - `integration_test.exs` - error recovery tests\n    89→    - `config_manager_test.exs` - file not found tests\n    90→    - `settings_live_test.exs` - missing configuration tests\n    91→- [x] All 335+ tests pass with clean output (96c582d)\n    92→\n    93→### Completed (Iteration 5 - Security: Web Console Authentication)\n    94→- [x] Created `YellowDog.Console.Plugs.BasicAuth` module (b32bbd7)\n    95→  - Environment-based configuration (CONSOLE_USERNAME, CONSOLE_PASSWORD)\n    96→  - Constant-time string comparison to prevent timing attacks\n    97→  - Graceful degradation when password not configured (with warning log)\n    98→  - Configurable realm for WWW-Authenticate header\n    99→- [x] Added plug to browser pipeline in router.ex\n   100→- [x] Configured authentication per environment:\n   101→  - Disabled by default in dev (set CONSOLE_AUTH_ENABLED=true to enable)\n   102→  - Disabled by default in test (for automated testing)\n   103→  - Enabled by default in production (requires CONSOLE_PASSWORD env var)\n   104→- [x] Added comprehensive unit tests (14 tests)\n   105→- [x] All 177 tests pass\n   106→\n   107→### Completed (Iteration 6 - Security: DHCP Rate Limiting)\n   108→- [x] Created `YellowDog.Dhcpv4.RateLimiter` module (e8f5f5e)\n   109→  - Token bucket algorithm for per-client and global rate limiting\n   110→  - Configurable burst capacity and refill rates\n   111→  - ETS-based storage for high-performance bucket tracking\n   112→  - Automatic cleanup of expired client buckets\n   113→  - Telemetry events for monitoring rate limit violations\n   114→- [x] Integrated rate limiter with DHCPv4 handler\n   115→  - Rate check before processing any DHCP message\n   116→  - Silent drop of rate-limited requests (per RFC)\n   117→- [x] Added RateLimiter to supervisor child list\n   118→- [x] Added comprehensive unit tests (16 tests)\n   119→- [x] All 121 tests pass (7 excluded)\n   120→\n   121→### Completed (Iteration 7 - DHCPv6 Rate Limiting)\n   122→- [x] Verified DNS compression loop protection is already implemented\n   123→  - `DNS.Message.Domain` has loop detection via visited positions MapSet\n   124→  - Max compression depth limiting (5 levels)\n   125→  - Comprehensive security tests in `dns/security_test.exs`\n   126→- [x] Created `YellowDog.Dhcpv6.RateLimiter` module (b1096df)\n   127→  - Token bucket algorithm for per-client and global rate limiting\n   128→  - ETS-based storage for high-performance bucket tracking\n   129→  - Configurable burst capacity and refill rates\n   130→  - Automatic cleanup of expired client buckets\n   131→  - Telemetry events for monitoring rate limit violations\n   132→  - Graceful handling when not running\n   133→- [x] Integrated rate limiter with DHCPv6 handler\n   134→  - Rate check before processing any DHCPv6 message\n   135→  - Silent drop of rate-limited requests (per RFC)\n   136→- [x] Added RateLimiter to supervisor child list\n   137→- [x] Added comprehensive unit tests (16 tests)\n   138→- [x] All tests pass (734 tests, excluding integration)\n   139→\n   140→### Completed (Iteration 8 - DNS Rate Limiting)\n   141→- [x] Created `YellowDog.Dns.RateLimiter` module (a0fcd2b)\n   142→  - Token bucket algorithm for per-client and global rate limiting\n   143→  - Higher defaults for DNS (50 client tokens, 5000 global vs 10/1000 DHCP)\n   144→  - ETS-based storage for high-performance bucket tracking\n   145→  - Configurable burst capacity and refill rates (20/sec vs 2/sec for DHCP)\n   146→  - Automatic cleanup of expired client buckets\n   147→  - Telemetry events for monitoring rate limit violations\n   148→  - Graceful handling when not running\n   149→- [x] Integrated rate limiter with DNS UDP handler\n   150→  - Rate check before processing any DNS message\n   151→  - Silent drop of rate-limited requests (per RFC best practices)\n   152→- [x] Added RateLimiter to supervisor child list\n   153→- [x] Added comprehensive unit tests (17 tests)\n   154→- [x] All tests pass (751 tests, excluding integration)\n   155→\n   156→### Completed (Iteration 9 - mDNS Rate Limiting)\n   157→- [x] Created `YellowDog.Mdns.RateLimiter` module (5d535ea)\n   158→  - Token bucket algorithm for per-source and global rate limiting\n   159→  - Higher defaults for mDNS (100 source tokens, 10000 global)\n   160→    - mDNS operates only on local network\n   161→    - Legitimate usage can be bursty (service announcements)\n   162→  - ETS-based storage for high-performance bucket tracking\n   163→  - Automatic cleanup of expired source buckets\n   164→  - Telemetry events for monitoring rate limit violations\n   165→  - Graceful handling when not running\n   166→- [x] Integrated rate limiter with mDNS handler\n   167→  - Rate check before processing any mDNS message\n   168→  - Silent drop of rate-limited requests\n   169→- [x] Added RateLimiter to supervisor child list\n   170→- [x] Added comprehensive unit tests (17 tests)\n   171→- [x] All tests pass (768 tests, excluding integration)\n   172→\n   173→### Rate Limiting Summary (All Services Complete)\n   174→| Service | Client Tokens | Client Refill | Global Tokens | Global Refill |\n   175→|---------|--------------|---------------|---------------|---------------|\n   176→| DHCPv4  | 10           | 2/sec         | 1000          | 100/sec       |\n   177→| DHCPv6  | 10           | 2/sec         | 1000          | 100/sec       |\n   178→| DNS     | 50           | 20/sec        | 5000          | 1000/sec      |\n   179→| mDNS    | 100          | 50/sec        | 10000         | 5000/sec      |\n   180→\n   181→### Completed (Iteration 10 - Performance: DHCPv4 Option Parsing)\n   182→- [x] Created `YellowDog.Dhcpv4.OptionParser` module (8b01401)\n   183→  - Single-pass option extraction O(n) vs previous O(n*m)\n   184→  - Extracts 8 commonly needed options in one iteration:\n   185→    - message_type, hostname, client_id, server_id\n   186→    - requested_ip, vendor_class, user_class, client_arch\n   187→  - `extract_common/1` - full option extraction\n   188→  - `extract_message_type/1` - lightweight type-only extraction\n   189→  - `build_client_info/2` - construct ACL evaluation context\n   190→- [x] Refactored DHCPv4 handler to use pre-parsed options\n   191→  - Parse once in `handle_boot_request`, pass to handlers\n   192→  - Modified `handle_dhcp_discover`, `handle_dhcp_request`, `handle_dhcp_decline`\n   193→  - Modified `create_dhcp_offer`, `create_dhcp_ack`\n   194→  - Added `determine_request_state_fast` using pre-parsed options\n   195→- [x] Removed legacy duplicate helper functions\n   196→  - Removed: `get_hostname_from_options`, `get_client_id_from_options`\n   197→  - Removed: `get_server_id_from_options`, `get_requested_ip`\n   198→  - Removed: `get_dhcp_message_type`, `decode_message_type`\n   199→  - R