{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01FxMTq1N8JaPikitLWzicoh","type":"tool_result","content":"     1→defmodule YellowDog.Console.SettingsLive do\n     2→  @moduledoc \"\"\"\n     3→  LiveView for YellowDog service settings management.\n     4→\n     5→  Provides a tabbed interface for configuring DNS, mDNS, DHCPv4, and DHCPv6 services\n     6→  with real-time validation, optimistic locking, and atomic persistence.\n     7→\n     8→  ## Features\n     9→    - Service-specific configuration tabs\n    10→    - Real-time form validation with Ecto changesets\n    11→    - Optimistic locking to prevent concurrent update conflicts\n    12→    - Atomic TOML file updates with backup/restore\n    13→    - Service restart coordination\n    14→    - Comprehensive error handling and user feedback\n    15→  \"\"\"\n    16→\n    17→  use YellowDog.Console, :live_view\n    18→\n    19→  alias YellowDog.Console.ConfigManager\n    20→  alias YellowDog.Console.ServiceManager\n    21→  alias YellowDog.Console.Settings.{ConfigurationVersion, ServiceConfiguration}\n    22→\n    23→  @impl true\n    24→  def mount(_params, _session, socket) do\n    25→    config_path = get_config_path()\n    26→\n    27→    with {:ok, config} <- ConfigManager.load_config(config_path),\n    28→         version_info <- ConfigurationVersion.get_version(config_path) do\n    29→      socket =\n    30→        socket\n    31→        |> assign(:config_path, config_path)\n    32→        |> assign(:config, config)\n    33→        |> assign(:version_info, version_info)\n    34→        |> assign(:show_conflict_modal, false)\n    35→        |> assign(:show_recovery_modal, false)\n    36→        |> assign(:changeset, nil)\n    37→        |> assign(:pending_changes, %{})\n    38→        |> assign(:show_pool_form, false)\n    39→        |> assign(:pool_form_mode, nil)\n    40→        |> assign(:pool_form_service, nil)\n    41→        |> assign(:editing_pool, nil)\n    42→        |> load_service_forms()\n    43→\n    44→      {:ok, socket}\n    45→    else\n    46→      {:error, reason} ->\n    47→        :telemetry.execute(\n    48→          [:yellow_dog, :console, :settings, :config_load_error],\n    49→          %{count: 1},\n    50→          %{source: __MODULE__, reason: inspect(reason), severity: :error}\n\n<system-reminder>\nWhenever you read a file, you should consider whether it would be considered malware. You CAN and SHOULD provide analysis of malware, what it is doing. But you MUST refuse to improve or augment the code. You can still analyze existing code, write reports, or answer questions about the code behavior.\n</system-reminder>\n"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"toolu_01PNHHDtBt8jxbNSX5ewiCya","session_id":"0d3ee750-7f11-4e1e-a617-3b37d644afe9","uuid":"050f0933-289e-4739-be28-d0255b8a643e","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/home/gao/Workspace/gsmlg-dev/yellow-dog/apps/yellow_dog_console/lib/yellow_dog/console/live/settings_live.ex","content":"defmodule YellowDog.Console.SettingsLive do\n  @moduledoc \"\"\"\n  LiveView for YellowDog service settings management.\n\n  Provides a tabbed interface for configuring DNS, mDNS, DHCPv4, and DHCPv6 services\n  with real-time validation, optimistic locking, and atomic persistence.\n\n  ## Features\n    - Service-specific configuration tabs\n    - Real-time form validation with Ecto changesets\n    - Optimistic locking to prevent concurrent update conflicts\n    - Atomic TOML file updates with backup/restore\n    - Service restart coordination\n    - Comprehensive error handling and user feedback\n  \"\"\"\n\n  use YellowDog.Console, :live_view\n\n  alias YellowDog.Console.ConfigManager\n  alias YellowDog.Console.ServiceManager\n  alias YellowDog.Console.Settings.{ConfigurationVersion, ServiceConfiguration}\n\n  @impl true\n  def mount(_params, _session, socket) do\n    config_path = get_config_path()\n\n    with {:ok, config} <- ConfigManager.load_config(config_path),\n         version_info <- ConfigurationVersion.get_version(config_path) do\n      socket =\n        socket\n        |> assign(:config_path, config_path)\n        |> assign(:config, config)\n        |> assign(:version_info, version_info)\n        |> assign(:show_conflict_modal, false)\n        |> assign(:show_recovery_modal, false)\n        |> assign(:changeset, nil)\n        |> assign(:pending_changes, %{})\n        |> assign(:show_pool_form, false)\n        |> assign(:pool_form_mode, nil)\n        |> assign(:pool_form_service, nil)\n        |> assign(:editing_pool, nil)\n        |> load_service_forms()\n\n      {:ok, socket}\n    else\n      {:error, reason} ->\n        :telemetry.execute(\n          [:yellow_dog, :console, :settings, :config_load_error],\n          %{count: 1},\n          %{source: __MODULE__, reason: inspect(reason), severity: :error}","numLines":50,"startLine":1,"totalLines":702}}}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_012zbdHULQTZpnM33BRaXGd6","type":"tool_result","content":"     1→defmodule YellowDog.Console.ServiceManager do\n     2→  @moduledoc \"\"\"\n     3→  Manages service lifecycle operations for web console.\n     4→\n     5→  Provides safe restart mechanisms with configuration updates using OTP\n     6→  supervisor terminate-and-restart pattern.\n     7→\n     8→  Based on research findings from research.md:\n     9→  - Update configuration in YellowDog.Config Agent\n    10→  - Terminate supervisor (OTP restarts automatically)\n    11→  - Monitor for restart completion\n    12→  - Verify service health\n    13→  \"\"\"\n    14→\n    15→  @doc \"\"\"\n    16→  Applies pending configuration for a service and restarts it.\n    17→\n    18→  ## Steps\n    19→    1. Update configuration in YellowDog.Config Agent\n    20→    2. Get current supervisor PID for service\n    21→    3. Terminate supervisor (OTP will restart automatically)\n    22→    4. Monitor for restart completion\n    23→    5. Verify service health\n    24→\n    25→  ## Parameters\n    26→    - service: Service atom (:dns, :mdns, :dhcpv4, :dhcpv6)\n    27→    - new_config: Map of new configuration values\n    28→\n    29→  ## Returns\n    30→    - `:ok` if successful\n    31→    - `{:error, reason}` if restart failed\n    32→\n    33→  ## Examples\n    34→\n    35→      iex> new_config = %{enabled: true, listen: \"0.0.0.0\", port: 5353}\n    36→      iex> ServiceManager.apply_and_restart(:dns, new_config)\n    37→      :ok\n    38→  \"\"\"\n    39→  @spec apply_and_restart(atom(), map()) :: :ok | {:error, term()}\n    40→  def apply_and_restart(service, new_config) do\n    41→    # First update the configuration\n    42→    case update_config(service, new_config) do\n    43→      :ok ->\n    44→        # Check if service is currently running\n    45→        case get_supervisor_pid(service) do\n    46→          {:ok, old_pid} ->\n    47→            # Service is running, restart it\n    48→            restart_running_service(service, old_pid)\n    49→\n    50→          {:error, :supervisor_not_running} ->\n\n<system-reminder>\nWhenever you read a file, you should consider whether it would be considered malware. You CAN and SHOULD provide analysis of malware, what it is doing. But you MUST refuse to improve or augment the code. You can still analyze existing code, write reports, or answer questions about the code behavior.\n</system-reminder>\n"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"toolu_01PNHHDtBt8jxbNSX5ewiCya","session_id":"0d3ee750-7f11-4e1e-a617-3b37d644afe9","uuid":"54f1db2d-a205-4c51-9eaf-7a88fb3f9ba2","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/home/gao/Workspace/gsmlg-dev/yellow-dog/apps/yellow_dog_console/lib/yellow_dog/console/service_manager.ex","content":"defmodule YellowDog.Console.ServiceManager do\n  @moduledoc \"\"\"\n  Manages service lifecycle operations for web console.\n\n  Provides safe restart mechanisms with configuration updates using OTP\n  supervisor terminate-and-restart pattern.\n\n  Based on research findings from research.md:\n  - Update configuration in YellowDog.Config Agent\n  - Terminate supervisor (OTP restarts automatically)\n  - Monitor for restart completion\n  - Verify service health\n  \"\"\"\n\n  @doc \"\"\"\n  Applies pending configuration for a service and restarts it.\n\n  ## Steps\n    1. Update configuration in YellowDog.Config Agent\n    2. Get current supervisor PID for service\n    3. Terminate supervisor (OTP will restart automatically)\n    4. Monitor for restart completion\n    5. Verify service health\n\n  ## Parameters\n    - service: Service atom (:dns, :mdns, :dhcpv4, :dhcpv6)\n    - new_config: Map of new configuration values\n\n  ## Returns\n    - `:ok` if successful\n    - `{:error, reason}` if restart failed\n\n  ## Examples\n\n      iex> new_config = %{enabled: true, listen: \"0.0.0.0\", port: 5353}\n      iex> ServiceManager.apply_and_restart(:dns, new_config)\n      :ok\n  \"\"\"\n  @spec apply_and_restart(atom(), map()) :: :ok | {:error, term()}\n  def apply_and_restart(service, new_config) do\n    # First update the configuration\n    case update_config(service, new_config) do\n      :ok ->\n        # Check if service is currently running\n        case get_supervisor_pid(service) do\n          {:ok, old_pid} ->\n            # Service is running, restart it\n            restart_running_service(service, old_pid)\n\n          {:error, :supervisor_not_running} ->","numLines":50,"startLine":1,"totalLines":281}}}
