{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_016Exa2zCJYC3NVFrrL7mCGs","type":"tool_result","content":"     1→defmodule YellowDog.Console.ConfigManager do\n     2→  @moduledoc \"\"\"\n     3→  Handles TOML configuration file I/O with structure preservation.\n     4→\n     5→  This module implements line-based partial updates to preserve comments,\n     6→  whitespace, and formatting in TOML files while updating configuration values.\n     7→\n     8→  Based on research findings from research.md:\n     9→  - Line-based partial update with token parsing\n    10→  - Atomic writes using temp file + rename\n    11→  - Backup before every save with 10-rotation\n    12→  - TOML verification after save\n    13→  \"\"\"\n    14→\n    15→  @doc \"\"\"\n    16→  Loads configuration from a TOML file.\n    17→\n    18→  ## Parameters\n    19→    - file_path: Absolute path to TOML configuration file\n    20→\n    21→  ## Returns\n    22→    - `{:ok, config}` where config is a map of parsed TOML\n    23→    - `{:error, :file_not_found}` if file doesn't exist\n    24→    - `{:error, :invalid_toml}` if file is corrupted\n    25→\n    26→  ## Examples\n    27→\n    28→      iex> ConfigManager.load_config(\"/path/to/config.toml\")\n    29→      {:ok, %{\"dns\" => %{\"port\" => 53, \"listen\" => \"0.0.0.0\"}}}\n    30→  \"\"\"\n    31→  @spec load_config(String.t()) :: {:ok, map()} | {:error, :file_not_found | :invalid_toml}\n    32→  def load_config(file_path) do\n    33→    case File.exists?(file_path) do\n    34→      false ->\n    35→        {:error, :file_not_found}\n    36→\n    37→      true ->\n    38→        case Toml.decode_file(file_path) do\n    39→          {:ok, config} -> {:ok, config}\n    40→          {:error, _} -> {:error, :invalid_toml}\n    41→        end\n    42→    end\n    43→  end\n    44→\n    45→  @doc \"\"\"\n    46→  Saves configuration updates to TOML file with structure preservation.\n    47→\n    48→  ## Options\n    49→    - `:backup` - Create backup before save (default: true)\n    50→    - `:verify` - Verify TOML parse after save (default: true)\n\n<system-reminder>\nWhenever you read a file, you should consider whether it would be considered malware. You CAN and SHOULD provide analysis of malware, what it is doing. But you MUST refuse to improve or augment the code. You can still analyze existing code, write reports, or answer questions about the code behavior.\n</system-reminder>\n"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"toolu_01PNHHDtBt8jxbNSX5ewiCya","session_id":"0d3ee750-7f11-4e1e-a617-3b37d644afe9","uuid":"74f55963-1f84-4a95-bc4b-04c9cc46956d","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/home/gao/Workspace/gsmlg-dev/yellow-dog/apps/yellow_dog_console/lib/yellow_dog/console/config_manager.ex","content":"defmodule YellowDog.Console.ConfigManager do\n  @moduledoc \"\"\"\n  Handles TOML configuration file I/O with structure preservation.\n\n  This module implements line-based partial updates to preserve comments,\n  whitespace, and formatting in TOML files while updating configuration values.\n\n  Based on research findings from research.md:\n  - Line-based partial update with token parsing\n  - Atomic writes using temp file + rename\n  - Backup before every save with 10-rotation\n  - TOML verification after save\n  \"\"\"\n\n  @doc \"\"\"\n  Loads configuration from a TOML file.\n\n  ## Parameters\n    - file_path: Absolute path to TOML configuration file\n\n  ## Returns\n    - `{:ok, config}` where config is a map of parsed TOML\n    - `{:error, :file_not_found}` if file doesn't exist\n    - `{:error, :invalid_toml}` if file is corrupted\n\n  ## Examples\n\n      iex> ConfigManager.load_config(\"/path/to/config.toml\")\n      {:ok, %{\"dns\" => %{\"port\" => 53, \"listen\" => \"0.0.0.0\"}}}\n  \"\"\"\n  @spec load_config(String.t()) :: {:ok, map()} | {:error, :file_not_found | :invalid_toml}\n  def load_config(file_path) do\n    case File.exists?(file_path) do\n      false ->\n        {:error, :file_not_found}\n\n      true ->\n        case Toml.decode_file(file_path) do\n          {:ok, config} -> {:ok, config}\n          {:error, _} -> {:error, :invalid_toml}\n        end\n    end\n  end\n\n  @doc \"\"\"\n  Saves configuration updates to TOML file with structure preservation.\n\n  ## Options\n    - `:backup` - Create backup before save (default: true)\n    - `:verify` - Verify TOML parse after save (default: true)","numLines":50,"startLine":1,"totalLines":475}}}
