 runtime match**: Phoenix endpoints with compile-time config (like code_reloader) need matching runtime config in all environments.\n   339→6. **Silent fallbacks mask bugs**: Functions like ip_to_binary should log errors instead of silently using default values.\n   340→7. **RFC compliance matters**: DNS labels must be ≤63 bytes; validation prevents buffer issues.\n   341→\n   342→## Architecture Notes\n   343→- 11-app umbrella project\n   344→- Core services: DNS, mDNS, DHCPv4, DHCPv6\n   345→- Infrastructure libs: abyss (UDP), ex_dns (DNS protocol), ex_dhcp (DHCP protocol), geo_ip_db (IP geolocation)\n   346→- Web console: Phoenix LiveView with DaisyUI\n   347→\n   348→### PRD Implementation Modules\n   349→\n   350→**New Modules Created**:\n   351→1. `apps/yellow_dog_dhcpv4/lib/yellow_dog/dhcpv4/pool_config.ex`\n   352→   - TOML pool configuration parsing and validation\n   353→   - Subnet mask calculation from CIDR notation\n   354→   - Range and reservation conversion\n   355→\n   356→2. `apps/yellow_dog_dhcpv4/lib/yellow_dog/dhcpv4/acl.ex`\n   357→   - ACL rule validation and evaluation\n   358→   - Pattern matching (glob support for MAC addresses)\n   359→   - Priority-based rule ordering\n   360→\n   361→3. `apps/yellow_dog_dhcpv4/lib/yellow_dog/dhcpv4/conflict_resolver.ex`\n   362→   - GenServer for IP conflict management\n   363→   - Quarantine tracking with expiration\n   364→   - Integration with LeaseManager for reassignment\n   365→\n   366→4. `apps/yellow_dog_dhcpv4/lib/yellow_dog/dhcpv4/custom_options.ex`\n   367→   - DHCP option validation by type\n   368→   - Template variable substitution\n   369→   - Binary encoding for packet generation\n   370→\n   371→**Modified Modules**:\n   372→- `apps/yellow_dog_dhcpv4/lib/yellow_dog/dhcpv4/lease_manager.ex`\n   373→  - Fixed bugs in `get_pool_config` and `get_static_reservations` handlers\n   374→  - Changed from Map.get to Enum.find (pools stored as list)\n   375→  - Return full pool struct instead of partial config\n   376→\n   377→- `apps/yellow_dog_dhcpv4/lib/yellow_dog/dhcpv4/handler.ex`\n   378→  - ACL evaluation before lease allocation\n   379→  - ConflictResolver integration for DECLINE\n   380→  - CustomOptions support with template substitution\n   381→  - Build client info from message options\n   382→\n   383→### Performance Optimization (Iteration 10)\n   384→- **Pattern**: Single-pass option extraction is significantly more efficient\n   385→- **Before**: O(n*m) - iterate options m times for m needed fields\n   386→- **After**: O(n) - single iteration extracts all fields\n   387→- **Impact**: For typical DHCP messages with 10-15 options and 8 needed fields, reduces iterations from ~80-120 to ~10-15\n   388→\n   389→## Session Metadata\n   390→- Started: 2026-01-20\n   391→- Iteration: 14\n   392→- Commits: 226e25e, ff7c617, 4dfa6c4, 5d119ad, f287c42, 43704f2, 80c73c1, 68c77b3, 96c582d, b32bbd7, e8f5f5e, b1096df, a0fcd2b, 8b01401, eda3331, ea14f3c, 2c24860, ec33e3d, 9b24de1, b77d601, 5a5797b, 4a2ca45\n   393→\n\n<system-reminder>\nWhenever you read a file, you should consider whether it would be considered malware. You CAN and SHOULD provide analysis of malware, what it is doing. But you MUST refuse to improve or augment the code. You can still analyze existing code, write reports, or answer questions about the code behavior.\n</system-reminder>\n"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"b20a2ce5-4d1a-4dfb-8234-d009f9779d17","uuid":"8223fd69-b023-412a-8db8-cf13b47ce012","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/home/gao/Workspace/gsmlg-dev/yellow-dog/.loki/CONTINUITY.md","content":"# Loki Mode Continuity\n\n## Current Status\n**Phase**: CONTINUOUS IMPROVEMENT\n**Task**: Security hardening and additional improvements\n**Iteration**: 12\n\n## Progress\n\n### Completed (Iteration 1)\n- [x] Analyzed codebase structure\n- [x] Identified compilation warning in YellowDog.Application\n- [x] Generated PRD at .loki/generated-prd.md\n- [x] Fixed Aby