{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01JV4Wn46h4DTx7pTeGA3eHu","type":"tool_result","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Perfect! Now I have a comprehensive understanding of the codebase. Let me compile the findings by comparing lib modules to test files.\n\n## Summary: Modules Missing Test Coverage\n\nBased on my comprehensive search across all four Yellow Dog applications, here's a structured analysis of modules that lack unit test coverage and have significant business logic:\n\n### **1. YELLOW_DOG_MDNS (5 modules without tests)**\n\n**High Priority (Complex business logic):**\n\n1. **`YellowDog.Mdns.FileWatcher`** (/home/gao/Workspace/gsmlg-dev/yellow-dog/apps/yellow_dog_mdns/lib/yellow_dog/mdns/file_watcher.ex)\n   - GenServer that monitors service configuration files for changes\n   - Handles hot-reload with debouncing and error recovery\n   - Complex state management with reload tracking\n\n2. **`YellowDog.Mdns.MessageCache`** (/home/gao/Workspace/gsmlg-dev/yellow-dog/apps/yellow_dog_mdns/lib/yellow_dog/mdns/message_cache.ex)\n   - ETS-based message caching with TTL expiration\n   - Filters cached messages by domain and record type\n   - Periodic cleanup of expired entries\n   - Domain normalization logic\n\n3. **`YellowDog.Mdns.NetworkMonitor`** (/home/gao/Workspace/gsmlg-dev/yellow-dog/apps/yellow_dog_mdns/lib/yellow_dog/mdns/network_monitor.ex)\n   - Advanced network activity tracking (queries + responses)\n   - Service discovery and extraction from mDNS messages\n   - Complex logic to mark queries as answered and update discovered services\n   - Statistics aggregation (queries per minute, most queried services)\n\n4. **`YellowDog.Mdns.Responder`** (/home/gao/Workspace/gsmlg-dev/yellow-dog/apps/yellow_dog_mdns/lib/yellow_dog/mdns/responder.ex)\n   - RFC 6762 compliance (known-answer suppression, response filtering)\n   - Complex record matching and normalization\n   - Message size validation against MTU limits\n   - Respons