{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"text","text":"This session is being continued from a previous conversation that ran out of context. The summary below covers the earlier portion of the conversation.\n\nAnalysis:\nLet me analyze the conversation chronologically:\n\n1. **Initial Request**: User is running \"Loki Mode\" - an autonomous iteration system for continuous improvement on a yellow-dog project (Elixir umbrella project with DNS, mDNS, DHCPv4, DHCPv6 services). This is iteration #4 (retry #3), asking to follow a REASON-ACT-REFLECT-VERIFY cycle.\n\n2. **Initial State Reading**: I read multiple files:\n   - `.loki/CONTINUITY.md` - Shows 14 iterations completed with extensive work\n   - `.loki/state/relevant-learnings.json` - Empty patterns\n   - `.loki/state/resources.json` - Memory at 80% (warning threshold)\n   - `.loki/queue/in-progress.json` - Empty queue\n   - `prd.md` - DHCP service data persistence PRD\n\n3. **Initial Test Run**: Tests initially failed in DNS Server test with `function_exported?` check. After clean rebuild, tests passed. The issue was a stale build.\n\n4. **Coverage Analysis**: Used Task subagent to find modules lacking test coverage:\n   - mDNS: NetworkMonitor, MessageCache, Responder, FileWatcher\n   - DHCPv4: AddressPool, LeaseStorage, ConfigWatcher\n   - DNS: ConnectionManager, ViewStore, AclStore\n\n5. **MessageCache Tests**: Created tests for `YellowDog.Mdns.MessageCache`:\n   - Initial attempt used wrong struct `DNS.ResourceRecord` (doesn't exist)\n   - Fixed to use `DNS.Message.Record` and `DNS.Message.Question`\n   - Tests needed to run from mdns app directory, not umbrella root\n   - 22 tests all pass\n\n6. **AddressPool Tests**: Created tests for `YellowDog.Dhcpv4.AddressPool`:\n   - 36 tests covering pool creation, IP allocation, range checking, static reservations\n   - All tests pass\n\n7. **Committed Changes**: Commit `6c4acfb` with new tests\n\n8. **NetworkMonitor Tests**: Created tests for `Yellow