2 unit tests for MessageCache GenServer\n     - Tests cache_message/3, query/2, list_all/0, stats/0, clear/0\n     - Key helper functions for creating DNS messages:\n     ```elixir\n     defp create_dns_message(opts \\\\ []) do\n       answers = Keyword.get(opts, :answers, [])\n       questions = Keyword.get(opts, :questions, [])\n       %DNS.Message{\n         header: %DNS.Message.Header{...},\n         qdlist: questions,\n         anlist: answers,\n         nslist: authority,\n         arlist: additional\n       }\n     end\n     \n     defp create_a_record(name, ip, ttl \\\\ 4500) do\n       %Record{name: name, type: :A, class: :IN, ttl: ttl, data: ip}\n     end\n     ```\n\n   - **`apps/yellow_dog_dhcpv4/test/yellow_dog/dhcpv4/address_pool_test.exs`** (CREATED)\n     - 36 unit tests for AddressPool module\n     - Tests pool creation, IP allocation, range checking, static reservations\n     - Test fixtures:\n     ```elixir\n     @legacy_config %{\n       name: \"test_pool\",\n       range_start: {192, 168, 1, 100},\n       range_end: {192, 168, 1, 200},\n       subnet_mask: {255, 255, 255, 0},\n       ...\n     }\n     ```\n\n   - **`apps/yellow_dog_mdns/test/yellow_dog/mdns/network_monitor_test.exs`** (CREATED - IN PROGRESS)\n     - 26 tests for NetworkMonitor GenServer\n     - Tests query logging, response caching, service discovery, network stats\n     - One test currently failing\n\n   - **`apps/yellow_dog_mdns/lib/yellow_dog/mdns/message_cache.ex`** (READ)\n     - GenServer with ETS-based message caching\n     - cache_message/3, query/2, list_all/0, stats/0, clear/0 functions\n\n   - **`apps/yellow_dog_mdns/lib/yellow_dog/mdns/network_monitor.ex`** (READ)\n     - Complex GenServer for network visibility\n     - Tracks queries + responses\n     - Service discovery from mDNS announcements\n     - Uses 3 ETS tables: responses, queries, discovered_services\n\n   - **`apps/yellow_dog_dhcpv4/lib/yellow_dog/dhcpv4/address_pool.ex`** (READ)\n     - IP address pool management\n     - new/1, validate_pool_config/1, get_available_ip/3, in_range?/2, get_static_reservation/2, pool_size/1\n\n4. Errors and fixes:\n   - **DNS Server test failure (stale build)**:\n     - Error: `function_exported?(Server, :start_link, 0)` returned false\n     - Fix: `MIX_ENV=test mix clean && mix compile` resolved it\n   \n   - **Wrong DNS struct name**:\n     - Error: `DNS.ResourceRecord.__struct__/1 is undefined`\n     - Fix: Changed to `DNS.Message.Record` after examining ex_dns library\n   \n   - **Umbrella test path issues**:\n     - Error: Tests couldn't find MessageCache module when run from umbrella root\n     - Fix: Run tests from individual app directory: `cd apps/yellow_dog_mdns && mix test ...`\n   \n   - **NetworkMonitor test - most_queried assertion**:\n     - Error: Expected `popular.local` with count 5, got count 1\n     - First fix attempt: Changed from assuming order to searching by domain\n     - Still failing - count is 1 instead of 5 (ongoing)\n\n5. Problem Solving:\n   - Identified modules lacking test coverage using Task subagent\n   - Created 58 new tests (22 MessageCache + 36 AddressPool)\n   - Successfully committed changes\n   - Currently debugging NetworkMonitor test that counts queries incorrectly\n\n6. All user messages:\n   - Single initial message activating Loki Mode iteration #4 with detailed instructions for autonomous operation, REASON-ACT-REFLECT-VERIFY cycle, and continuous improvement requirements.\n\n7. Pending Tasks:\n   - Fix failing NetworkMonitor test (`tracks most queried services`)\n   - Commit NetworkMonitor tests once passing\n   - Continue expanding test coverage (Responder, LeaseStorage, etc.)\n   - Update CONTINUITY.md with NetworkMonitor progress\n\n8. Current Work:\n   Working on NetworkMonitor unit tests. One test is failing:\n   ```\n   test \"tracks most queried services\" (YellowDog.Mdns.NetworkMonitorTest)\n   Assertion with == failed\n   code:  assert popular.count == 5\n   left:  1\n   right: 5\n   ```\n   \n   The test logs 5 queries for \"popular.local\" but the count shows 1. This suggests the ETS bag table may be storing entries differently than expected, or the grouping logic in `network_stats/0` isn't working correctly.\n\n9. Optional Next Step:\n   Debug the failing NetworkMonitor test. The issue is that 5 queries are being logged for \"popular.local\" but only 1 is being counted. Need to investigate:\n   1. How `log_query/3` stores entries in ETS (bag table with domain_key)\n   2. How `get_queries/1` retrieves them\n   3. How `network_stats/0` groups and counts by domain\n   \n   The test code:\n   ```elixir\n   for _ <- 1..5 do\n     question = create_question(\"popular.local\", :A)\n     message = create_dns_message(questions: [question], qr: 0)\n     NetworkMonitor.log_query(message, {192, 168, 1, 10}, 5353)\n   end\n   ```\n   \n   The ETS table uses `:bag` type which allows duplicates, so all 5 should be stored with the same key \"popular.local\". The `get_queries/1` function should return all of them.\n\nIf you need specific details from before compaction (like exact code snippets, error messages, or content you generated), read the full transcript at: /home/gao/.claude/projects/-home-gao-Workspace-gsmlg-dev-yellow-dog/b20a2ce5-4d1a-4dfb-8234-d009f9779d17.jsonl\nPlease continue the conversation from where we left it off without asking the user any further questions. Continue with the last task that you were asked to work on."}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"b20a2ce5-4d1a-4dfb-8234-d009f9779d17","uuid":"42fbf5e3-485f-4fda-be0e-c17c9b080eda","isSynthetic":true}
