{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-5-20251101","id":"msg_01VhHAG8TsF5dUQwn5nYng2y","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"This confirms the issue. The ETS table only has 1 entry, not 5. This is because all 5 queries have the same key `\"popular.local\"` and ETS `:bag` tables allow duplicates only when the entire tuple is different. Since the timestamp is the same second and other fields are identical, the entries are being deduplicated or overwritten.\n\nLooking at the code more carefully - the ETS insert on line 353 uses `{domain_key, entry}` as the tuple. With `:bag`, duplicates are allowed only if the entire tuple differs. Since the entries have the same `domain_key` and potentially the same timestamp (within the same second), entries with different timestamps should be stored.\n\nLet me check if the timestamp is the issue:"}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1,"cache_creation_input_tokens":845,"cache_read_input_tokens":89113,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":845,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":1,"service_tier":"standard"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"b20a2ce5-4d1a-4dfb-8234-d009f9779d17","uuid":"82492be2-7746-45b1-9180-0f4a88f26567"}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-5-20251101","id":"msg_01VhHAG8TsF5dUQwn5nYng2y","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_011hcKVTojEBGP69QkHLmNnE","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"cd /home/gao/Workspace/gsmlg-dev/yellow-dog && MIX_ENV=test mix run -e '\nalias YellowDog.Mdns.NetworkMonitor\nalias DNS.Message.Question\n\n# Start the monitor\nNetworkMonitor.start_link([])\nNetworkMonitor.clear()\n\n# Create 5 queries for the same domain with small delays\nfor i <- 1..5 do\n  question = %Question{name: \"popular.local\", type: :A, class: :IN}\n  message = %DNS.Message{\n    header: %DNS.Message.Header{id: i, qr: 0, opcode: 0, aa: 1, tc: 0, rd: 0, ra: 0, z: 0, rcode: 0, qdcount: 1, ancount: 0, nscount: 0, arcount: 0},\n    qdlist: [question],\n    anlist: [],\n    nslist: [],\n    arlist: []\n  }\n  NetworkMonitor.log_query(message, {192, 168, 1, 10}, 5353)\n  IO.puts(\"Logged query #{i}, sleeping...\")\n  :timer.sleep(1100) # sleep more than 1 second to get different timestamps\nend\n\n:timer.sleep(50)\n\n# Get the raw queries\nqueries = NetworkMonitor.get_queries()\nIO.puts(\"Total queries from get_queries: #{length(queries)}\")\n\n# Get ETS table size directly\nets_size = :ets.info(:mdns_queries, :size)\nIO.puts(\"ETS table size: #{ets_size}\")\n\n# Get all from ETS \nall_ets = :ets.tab2list(:mdns_queries)\nIO.puts(\"Raw ETS entries: #{length(all_ets)}\")\n\n# Inspect timestamps\ntimestamps = Enum.map(all_ets, fn {_k, entry} -> entry.timestamp end)\nIO.puts(\"Timestamps: #{inspect(timestamps)}\")\n' 2>&1","description":"Debug with longer delays between queries","timeout":60000}}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1,"cache_creation_input_tokens":845,"cache_read_input_tokens":89113,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":845,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":1,"service_tier":"standard"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"b20a2ce5-4