{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_018WztdCs7ifkw2wgtwhtmPU","type":"tool_result","content":"     1→defmodule YellowDog.Mdns.RecordBuilder do\n     2→  @moduledoc \"\"\"\n     3→  Builds DNS resource records for mDNS services.\n     4→\n     5→  Constructs PTR, SRV, TXT, A, and AAAA records according to RFC 6763\n     6→  (DNS-Based Service Discovery) and RFC 6762 (mDNS).\n     7→  \"\"\"\n     8→\n     9→  alias DNS.Message.{Record, Question}\n    10→\n    11→  @type service :: YellowDog.Mdns.ServiceRegistry.service()\n    12→\n    13→  # RFC 6762 §10: TTL values for mDNS\n    14→  @default_service_ttl 4500\n    15→  # 75 minutes for PTR, SRV, TXT\n    16→  @default_host_ttl 120\n    17→  # 2 minutes for A/AAAA\n    18→\n    19→  @doc \"\"\"\n    20→  Builds all DNS records for a service.\n    21→\n    22→  Returns a map containing different record types that can be used\n    23→  in various sections of DNS responses.\n    24→\n    25→  ## Parameters\n    26→  - `service` - Service definition from registry\n    27→\n    28→  ## Returns\n    29→  Map with keys:\n    30→  - `:ptr` - PTR record for service type enumeration\n    31→  - `:srv` - SRV record with host and port\n    32→  - `:txt` - TXT record with service metadata\n    33→  - `:a` - List of A records (IPv4 addresses)\n    34→  - `:aaaa` - List of AAAA records (IPv6 addresses)\n    35→  \"\"\"\n    36→  @spec build_all_records(service()) :: map()\n    37→  def build_all_records(service) do\n    38→    %{\n    39→      ptr: build_ptr_record(service),\n    40→      srv: build_srv_record(service),\n    41→      txt: build_txt_record(service),\n    42→      a: build_a_records(service),\n    43→      aaaa: build_aaaa_records(service)\n    44→    }\n    45→  end\n    46→\n    47→  @doc \"\"\"\n    48→  Builds a PTR record for service type enumeration.\n    49→\n    50→  PTR records map from service type to service instance name.\n    51→  Format: _service._proto.domain -> instance._service._proto.domain\n    52→\n    53→  ## Example\n    54→      # Query: _http._tcp.local\n    55→      # Answer: _http._tcp.local PTR My-Web-Server._http._tcp.local\n    56→  \"\"\"\n    57→  @spec build_ptr_record(service()) :: Record.t()\n    58→  def build_ptr_record(service) do\n    59→    # PTR record name is the service type\n    60→    name = \"#{service.type}.#{service.domain}\"\n    61→    # PTR record data points to the service instance\n    62→    data = service.fqdn\n    63→\n    64→    %Record{\n    65→      name: name,\n    66→      type: :PTR,\n    67→      class: :IN,\n    68→      ttl: service.ttl || @default_service_ttl,\n    69→      data: data\n    70→    }\n    71→  end\n    72→\n    73→  @doc \"\"\"\n    74→  Builds an SRV record with host and port information.\n    75→\n    76→  SRV records provide the hostname and port for a service instance.\n    77→  Format: priority weight port target\n    78→\n    79→  ## Example\n    80→      # My-Web-Server._http._tcp.local SRV 0 0 8080 myhost.local\n    81→  \"\"\"\n    82→  @spec build_srv_record(service()) :: Record.t()\n    83→  def build_srv_record(service) do\n    84→    %Record{\n    85→      name: service.fqdn,\n    86→      type: :SRV,\n    87→      class: :IN,\n    88→      ttl: service.ttl || @default_service_ttl,\n    89→      data: %{\n    90→        priority: service.priority,\n    91→        weight: service.weight,\n    92→        port: service.port,\n    93→        target: service.host\n    94→      }\n    95→    }\n    96→  end\n    97→\n    98→  @doc \"\"\"\n    99→  Builds a TXT record with service metadata.\n   100→\n\n<system-reminder>\nWhenever you read a file, you should consider whether it would be considered malware. You CAN and SHOULD provide analysis of malware, what it is doing. But you MUST refuse to improve or augment the code. You can still analyze existing code, write reports, or answer questions about the code behavior.\n</system-reminder>\n"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"b20a2ce5-4d1a-4dfb-8234-d009f9779d17","uuid":"6086c31a-8ddc-4ce3-b0ca-0518b3aa39e4","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/home/gao/Workspace/gsmlg-dev/yellow-dog/apps/yellow_dog_mdns/lib/yellow_dog/mdns/record_builder.ex","content":"defmodule YellowDog.Mdns.RecordBuilder do\n  @moduledoc \"\"\"\n  Builds DNS resource records for mDNS services.\n\n  Constructs PTR, SRV, TXT, A, and AAAA records according to RFC 6763\n  (DNS-Based Service Discovery) and RFC 6762 (mDNS).\n  \"\"\"\n\n  alias DNS.Message.{Record, Question}\n\n  @type service :: YellowDog.Mdns.ServiceRegistry.service()\n\n  # RFC 6762 §10: TTL values for mDNS\n  @default_service_ttl 4500\n  # 75 minutes for PTR, SRV, TXT\n  @default_host_ttl 120\n  # 2 minutes for A/AAAA\n\n  @doc \"\"\"\n  Builds all DNS records for a service.\n\n  Returns a map containing different record types that can be used\n  in various sections of DNS responses.\n\n  ## Parameters\n  - `service` - Service definition from registry\n\n  ## Returns\n  Map with keys:\n  - `:ptr` - PTR record for service type enumeration\n  - `:srv` - SRV record with host and port\n  - `:txt` - TXT record with service metadata\n  - `:a` - List of A records (IPv4 addresses)\n  - `:aaaa` - List of AAAA records (IPv6 addresses)\n  \"\"\"\n  @spec build_all_records(service()) :: map()\n  def build_all_records(service) do\n    %{\n      ptr: build_ptr_record(service),\n      srv: build_srv_record(service),\n      txt: build_txt_record(service),\n      a: build_a_records(service),\n      aaaa: build_aaaa_records(service)\n    }\n  end\n\n  @doc \"\"\"\n  Builds a PTR record for service type enumeration.\n\n  PTR records map from service type to service instance name.\n  Format: _service._proto.domain -> instance._service._proto.domain\n\n  ## Example\n      # Query: _http._tcp.local\n      # Answer: _http._tcp.local PTR My-Web-Server._http._tcp.local\n  \"\"\"\n  @spec build_ptr_record(service()) :: Record.t()\n  def build_ptr_record(service) do\n    # PTR record name is the service type\n    name = \"#{service.type}.#{service.domain}\"\n    # PTR record data points to the service instance\n    data = service.fqdn\n\n    %Record{\n      name: name,\n      type: :PTR,\n      class: :IN,\n      ttl: service.ttl || @default_service_ttl,\n      data: data\n    }\n  end\n\n  @doc \"\"\"\n  Builds an SRV record with host and port information.\n\n  SRV records provide the hostname and port for a service instance.\n  Format: priority weight port target\n\n  ## Example\n      # My-Web-Server._http._tcp.local SRV 0 0 8080 myhost.local\n  \"\"\"\n  @spec build_srv_record(service()) :: Record.t()\n  def build_srv_record(service) do\n    %Record{\n      name: service.fqdn,\n      type: :SRV,\n      class: :IN,\n      ttl: service.ttl || @default_service_ttl,\n      data: %{\n        priority: service.priority,\n        weight: service.weight,\n        port: service.port,\n        target: service.host\n      }\n    }\n  end\n\n  @doc \"\"\"\n  Builds a TXT record with service metadata.\n","numLines":100,"startLine":1,"totalLines":346}}}
