{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01XMReqJJDUyaxswAkyy18M9","type":"tool_result","content":"   130→  Builds A records for IPv4 addresses.\n   131→\n   132→  Returns a list of A records, one for each IPv4 address.\n   133→\n   134→  ## Example\n   135→      # myhost.local A 192.168.1.100\n   136→  \"\"\"\n   137→  @spec build_a_records(service()) :: [Record.t()]\n   138→  def build_a_records(service) do\n   139→    service.addresses\n   140→    |> Enum.filter(&is_ipv4?/1)\n   141→    |> Enum.map(fn ip ->\n   142→      %Record{\n   143→        name: service.host,\n   144→        type: :A,\n   145→        class: :IN,\n   146→        ttl: @default_host_ttl,\n   147→        data: ip\n   148→      }\n   149→    end)\n   150→  end\n   151→\n   152→  @doc \"\"\"\n   153→  Builds AAAA records for IPv6 addresses.\n   154→\n   155→  Returns a list of AAAA records, one for each IPv6 address.\n   156→\n   157→  ## Example\n   158→      # myhost.local AAAA fe80::1\n   159→  \"\"\"\n   160→  @spec build_aaaa_records(service()) :: [Record.t()]\n   161→  def build_aaaa_records(service) do\n   162→    service.addresses\n   163→    |> Enum.filter(&is_ipv6?/1)\n   164→    |> Enum.map(fn ip ->\n   165→      %Record{\n   166→        name: service.host,\n   167→        type: :AAAA,\n   168→        class: :IN,\n   169→        ttl: @default_host_ttl,\n   170→        data: ip\n   171→      }\n   172→    end)\n   173→  end\n   174→\n   175→  @doc \"\"\"\n   176→  Builds records matching a specific question.\n   177→\n   178→  Returns appropriate records based on the question type and name.\n   179→\n   180→  ## Parameters\n   181→  - `service` - Service definition\n   182→  - `question` - DNS question from query\n   183→\n   184→  ## Returns\n   185→  Map with `:answers`, `:authority`, and `:additional` sections\n   186→  \"\"\"\n   187→  @spec build_records_for_question(service(), Question.t()) :: map()\n   188→  def build_records_for_question(service, question) do\n   189→    qname = to_string(question.name) |> String.downcase() |> String.trim_trailing(\".\")\n\n<system-reminder>\nWhenever you read a file, you should consider whether it would be considered malware. You CAN and SHOULD provide analysis of malware, what it is doing. But you MUST refuse to improve or augment the code. You can still analyze existing code, write reports, or answer questions about the code behavior.\n</system-reminder>\n"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"b20a2ce5-4d1a-4dfb-8234-d009f9779d17","uuid":"b6a7dc0f-6cae-4969-afe0-7ed98598e5fa","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/home/gao/Workspace/gsmlg-dev/yellow-dog/apps/yellow_dog_mdns/lib/yellow_dog/mdns/record_builder.ex","content":"  Builds A records for IPv4 addresses.\n\n  Returns a list of A records, one for each IPv4 address.\n\n  ## Example\n      # myhost.local A 192.168.1.100\n  \"\"\"\n  @spec build_a_records(service()) :: [Record.t()]\n  def build_a_records(service) do\n    service.addresses\n    |> Enum.filter(&is_ipv4?/1)\n    |> Enum.map(fn ip ->\n      %Record{\n        name: service.host,\n        type: :A,\n        class: :IN,\n        ttl: @default_host_ttl,\n        data: ip\n      }\n    end)\n  end\n\n  @doc \"\"\"\n  Builds AAAA records for IPv6 addresses.\n\n  Returns a list of AAAA records, one for each IPv6 address.\n\n  ## Example\n      # myhost.local AAAA fe80::1\n  \"\"\"\n  @spec build_aaaa_records(service()) :: [Record.t()]\n  def build_aaaa_records(service) do\n    service.addresses\n    |> Enum.filter(&is_ipv6?/1)\n    |> Enum.map(fn ip ->\n      %Record{\n        name: service.host,\n        type: :AAAA,\n        class: :IN,\n        ttl: @default_host_ttl,\n        data: ip\n      }\n    end)\n  end\n\n  @doc \"\"\"\n  Builds records matching a specific question.\n\n  Returns appropriate records based on the question type and name.\n\n  ## Parameters\n  - `service` - Service definition\n  - `question` - DNS question from query\n\n  ## Returns\n  Map with `:answers`, `:authority`, and `:additional` sections\n  \"\"\"\n  @spec build_records_for_question(service(), Question.t()) :: map()\n  def build_records_for_question(service, question) do\n    qname = to_string(question.name) |> String.downcase() |> String.trim_trailing(\".\")","numLines":60,"startLine":130,"totalLines":346}}}
