{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01W3ibQEfKN3ojYMJduaTPgM","type":"tool_result","content":"   180→      services when is_list(services) -> {:ok, services}\n   181→      service when is_map(service) -> {:ok, [service]}\n   182→    end\n   183→  end\n   184→\n   185→  defp extract_services(data, :json) do\n   186→    case Map.get(data, :services) do\n   187→      nil -> {:ok, []}\n   188→      services when is_list(services) -> {:ok, services}\n   189→      _ -> {:error, :invalid_json_structure}\n   190→    end\n   191→  end\n   192→\n   193→  defp validate_and_normalize_service(service) do\n   194→    normalized = normalize_service_keys(service)\n   195→\n   196→    case validate_service(normalized) do\n   197→      :ok -> {:ok, normalized}\n   198→      {:error, reason} -> {:error, reason}\n   199→    end\n   200→  end\n   201→\n   202→  defp normalize_service_keys(service) when is_map(service) do\n   203→    %{\n   204→      name: get_string_value(service, [:name, \"name\"]),\n   205→      type: get_string_value(service, [:type, \"type\"]),\n   206→      port: get_integer_value(service, [:port, \"port\"]),\n   207→      host: get_string_value(service, [:host, \"host\"]),\n   208→      txt: get_map_value(service, [:txt, \"txt\"]),\n   209→      addresses: get_addresses(service),\n\n<system-reminder>\nWhenever you read a file, you should consider whether it would be considered malware. You CAN and SHOULD provide analysis of malware, what it is doing. But you MUST refuse to improve or augment the code. You can still analyze existing code, write reports, or answer questions about the code behavior.\n</system-reminder>\n"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"b20a2ce5-4d1a-4dfb-8234-d009f9779d17","uuid":"abec78a5-2add-4d5e-a0ab-d47f68a9aa1e","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/home/gao/Workspace/gsmlg-dev/yellow-dog/apps/yellow_dog_mdns/lib/yellow_dog/mdns/service_store.ex","content":"      services when is_