{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_012JiYLJsQKmRdqHrxPAnMsh","type":"tool_result","content":"     1→defmodule YellowDog.Dns.Zone.Forward do\n     2→  @moduledoc \"\"\"\n     3→  Forwarding zone process.\n     4→\n     5→  Forwards DNS queries to configured upstream servers.\n     6→  Supports multiple upstream servers with failover.\n     7→\n     8→  ## Features\n     9→\n    10→  - Multiple upstream servers with round-robin selection\n    11→  - Timeout and retry handling\n    12→  - Response caching (optional)\n    13→  - Health checking of upstream servers\n    14→\n    15→  ## Legacy API\n    16→\n    17→  This module also provides a legacy struct-based API for configuration\n    18→  and validation, used by Zone.Manager for loading forward zones.\n    19→  \"\"\"\n    20→\n    21→  use GenServer\n    22→\n    23→  @behaviour YellowDog.Dns.Zone.Behaviour\n    24→\n    25→  alias YellowDog.Telemetry\n    26→\n    27→  @default_timeout 5000\n    28→  @default_retries 2\n    29→\n    30→  @type t :: %__MODULE__{\n    31→          name: String.t() | nil,\n    32→          view_name: String.t() | nil,\n    33→          upstreams: [{:inet.ip_address(), :inet.port_number()}] | nil,\n    34→          socket: :gen_udp.socket() | nil,\n    35→          timeout: non_neg_integer() | nil,\n    36→          retries: non_neg_integer() | nil,\n    37→          forwarders: [:inet.ip_address()] | nil,\n    38→          forward_mode: :only | :first | nil,\n    39→          timeout_ms: non_neg_integer() | nil,\n    40→          max_retries: non_neg_integer() | nil,\n    41→          current_upstream: non_neg_integer(),\n    42→          query_count: non_neg_integer(),\n    43→          success_count: non_neg_integer(),\n    44→          error_count: non_neg_integer(),\n    45→          pending: map()\n    46→        }\n    47→\n    48→  defstruct [\n    49→    :name,\n    50→    :view_name,\n    51→    :upstreams,\n    52→    :socket,\n    53→    :timeout,\n    54→    :retries,\n    55→    # Legacy fields for struct-based API\n    56→    :forwarders,\n    57→    :forward_mode,\n    58→    :timeout_ms,\n    59→    :max_retries,\n    60→    current_upstream: 0,\n    61→    query_count: 0,\n    62→    success_count: 0,\n    63→    error_count: 0,\n    64→    pending: %{}\n    65→  ]\n    66→\n    67→  # Client API\n    68→\n    69→  @doc \"\"\"\n    70→  Starts a forwarding zone process.\n    71→\n    72→  ## Options\n    73→\n    74→  - `:name` - Zone name (required)\n    75→  - `:upstreams` - List of upstream servers [{ip, port}, ...]\n    76→  - `:timeout` - Query timeout in ms (default: 5000)\n    77→  - `:retries` - Number of retries (default: 2)\n    78→  \"\"\"\n    79→  @spec start_link(keyword()) :: GenServer.on_start()\n    80→  def start_link(opts) do\n    81→    zone_name = Keyword.fetch!(opts, :name)\n    82→    view_name = Keyword.get(opts, :view_name, \"default\")\n    83→    GenServer.start_link(__MODULE__, opts, name: via_tuple(view_name, zone_name))\n    84→  end\n    85→\n    86→  @impl YellowDog.Dns.Zone.Behaviour\n    87→  def get_name(pid) do\n    88→    GenServer.call(pid, :get_name)\n    89→  end\n    90→\n    91→  @doc \"\"\"\n    92→  Gets the view name this zone belongs to.\n    93→  \"\"\"\n    94→  @spec get_view(pid()) :: String.t()\n    95→  def get_view(pid) do\n    96→    GenServer.call(pid, :get_view)\n    97→  end\n    98→\n    99→  @impl YellowDog.Dns.Zone.Behaviour\n   100→  def resolve(pid, query) do\n   101→    GenServer.call(pid, {:resolve, query}, @default_timeout + 1000)\n   102→  end\n   103→\n   104→  @impl YellowDog.Dns.Zone.Behaviour\n   105→  def reload(pid, config) do\n   106→    GenServer.call(pid, {:reload, config})\n   107→  end\n   108→\n   109→  @impl YellowDog.Dns.Zone.Behaviour\n   110→  def stats(pid) do\n   111→    GenServer.call(pid, :stats)\n   112→  end\n   113→\n   114→  # Server Callbacks\n   115→\n   116→  @impl true\n   117→  def init(opts) do\n   118→    zone_name = Keyword.fetch!(opts, :name)\n   119→    view_name = Keyword.get(opts, :view_name, \"default\")\n   120→    upstreams = parse_upstreams(Keyword.get(opts, :upstreams, []))\n   121→    timeout = Keyword.get(opts, :timeout, @default_timeout)\n   122→    retries = Keyword.get(opts, :retries, @default_retries)\n   123→\n   124→    # Open UDP socket for forwarding\n   125→    {:ok, socket} = :gen_udp.open(0, [:binary, active: true])\n   126→\n   127→    state = %__MODULE__{\n   128→      name: zone_name,\n   129→      view_name: view_name,\n   130→      upstreams: upstreams,\n   131→      socket: socket,\n   132→      timeout: timeout,\n   133→      retries: retries\n   134→    }\n   135→\n   136→    Telemetry.info(\"Forward zone started\", %{\n   137→      name: zone_name,\n   138→      upstreams: length(upstreams)\n   139→    })\n   140→\n   141→    {:ok, state}\n   142→  end\n   143→\n   144→  @impl true\n   145→  def handle_call(:get_name, _from, state) do\n   146→    {:reply, state.name, state}\n   147→  end\n   148→\n   149→  @impl true\n   150→  def handle_call(:get_view, _from, state) do\n   151→    {:reply, state.view_name, state}\n   152→  end\n   153→\n   154→  @impl true\n   155→  def handle_call({:resolve, query}, from, state) do\n   156→    state = %{state | query_count: state.query_count + 1}\n   157→\n   158→    case state.upstreams do\n   159→      [] ->\n   160→        {:reply, {:error, :no_upstreams}, state}\n   161→\n   162→      _upstreams ->\n   163→        # Select upstream (round-robin)\n   164→        {upstream, state} = select_upstream(state)\n   165→\n   166→        # Send query\n   167→        case send_query(state, upstream, query) do\n   168→          :ok ->\n   169→            # Store pending request\n   170→            query_id = query.header.id\n   171→            timer_ref = Process.send_after(self(), {:timeout, query_id}, state.timeout)\n   172→\n   173→            pending = %{\n   174→              from: from,\n   175→              query: query,\n   176→              upstream: upstream,\n   177→              timer: timer_ref,\n   178→              retries: state.retries,\n   179→              started_at: System.monotonic_time(:microsecond)\n   180→            }\n   181→\n   182→            state = %{state | pending: Map.put(state.pending, query_id, pending)}\n   183→            {:noreply, state}\n   184→\n   185→          {:error, reason} ->\n   186→            state = %{state | error_count: state.error_count + 1}\n   187→            {:reply, {:error, reason}, state}\n   188→        end\n   189→    end\n   190→  end\n   191→\n   192→  @impl true\n   193→  def handle_call({:reload, config}, _from, state) do\n   194→    upstreams = parse_upstreams(Keyword.get(config, :upstreams, state.upstreams))\n   195→    timeout = Keyword.get(config, :timeout, state.timeout)\n   196→    retries = Keyword.get(config, :retries, state.retries)\n   197→\n   198→    new_state = %{state | upstreams: upstreams, timeout: timeout, retries: retries}\n   199→\n   200→    Telemetry.info(\"Forward zone reloaded\", %{name: state.name})\n   201→\n   202→    {:reply, :ok, new_state}\n   203→  end\n   204→\n   205→  @impl true\n   206→  def handle_call(:stats, _from, state) do\n   207→    stats = %{\n   208→      name: state.name,\n   209→      upstream_count: length(state.upstreams),\n   210→      upstreams: format_upstreams(state.upstreams),\n   211→      query_count: state.query_count,\n   212→      success_count: state.success_count,\n   213→      error_count: state.error_count,\n   214→      pending_count: map_size(state.pending)\n   215→    }\n   216→\n   217→    {:reply, stats, state}\n   218→  end\n   219→\n   220→  # Format upstreams back to string format for display/editing\n   221→  defp format_upstreams(upstreams) do\n   222→    Enum.map(upstreams, &format_upstream/1)\n   223→  end\n   224→\n   225→  @impl true\n   226→  def handle_info({:udp, socket, ip, port, data}, %{socket: socket} = state) do\n   227→    try do\n   228→      response = DNS.Message.from_iodata(data)\n   229→      query_id = response.header.id\n   230→\n   231→      case Map.pop(state.pending, query_id) do\n   232→        {nil, _pending} ->\n   233→          # Unknown response, ignore\n   234→          {:noreply, state}\n   235→\n   236→        {pending, remaining} ->\n   237→          # Cancel timeout timer\n   238→          Process.cancel_timer(pending.timer)\n   239→\n   240→          # Calculate elapsed time\n   241→          elapsed = System.monotonic_time(:microsecond) - pending.started_at\n   242→\n   243→          Telemetry.debug(\"Forward query completed\", %{\n   244→            zone: state.name,\n   245→            upstream: format_upstream({ip, port}),\n   246→            elapsed_us: elapsed\n   247→          })\n   248→\n   249→          # Reply to caller\n   250→          GenServer.reply(pending.from, {:ok, response})\n   251→\n   252→          state = %{\n   253→            state\n   254→            | pending: remaining,\n   255→              success_count: state.success_count + 1\n   256→          }\n   257→\n   258→          {:noreply, state}\n   259→      end\n   260→    catch\n   261→      :throw, _reason ->\n   262→        {:noreply, state}\n   263→    end\n   264→  end\n   265→\n   266→  @impl true\n   267→  def handle_info({:timeout, query_id}, state) do\n   268→    case Map.pop(state.pending, query_id) do\n   269→      {nil, _pending} ->\n   270→        # Already handled\n   271→        {:noreply, state}\n   272→\n   273→      {pending, remaining} ->\n   274→        if pending.retries > 0 do\n   275→          # Retry with next upstream\n   276→          {upstream, state} = select_upstream(%{state | pending: remaining})\n   277→\n   278→          case send_query(state, upstream, pending.query) do\n   279→            :ok ->\n   280→              timer_ref = Process.send_after(self(), {:timeout, query_id}, state.timeout)\n   281→\n   282→              new_pending = %{\n   283→                pending\n   284→                | upstream: upstream,\n   285→                  timer: timer_ref,\n   286→                  retries: pending.retries - 1\n   287→              }\n   288→\n   289→              state = %{state | pending: Map.put(state.pending, query_id, new_pending)}\n   290→              {:noreply, state}\n   291→\n   292→            {:error, _reason} ->\n   293→              GenServer.reply(pending.from, {:error, :servfail})\n   294→              state = %{state | error_count: state.error_count + 1}\n   295→              {:noreply, state}\n   296→          end\n   297→        else\n   298→          # No more retries\n   299→          Telemetry.warning(\"Forward query timeout\", %{\n   300→            zone: state.name,\n   301→            query_id: query_id\n   302→          })\n   303→\n   304→          GenServer.reply(pending.from, {:error, :servfail})\n   305→          state = %{state | pending: remaining, error_count: state.error_count + 1}\n   306→          {:noreply, state}\n   307→        end\n   308→    end\n   309→  end\n   310→\n   311→  @impl true\n   312→  def terminate(_reason, state) do\n   313→    :gen_udp.close(state.socket)\n   314→    :ok\n   315→  end\n   316→\n   317→  # Private Functions\n   318→\n   319→  defp parse_upstreams(upstreams) when is_list(upstreams) do\n   320→    Enum.map(upstreams, fn\n   321→      {ip, port} when is_tuple(ip) and is_integer(port) ->\n   322→        {ip, port}\n   323→\n   324→      ip_str when is_binary(ip_str) ->\n   325→        parse_upstream_string(ip_str)\n   326→\n   327→      {ip_str, port} when is_binary(ip_str) and is_integer(port) ->\n   328→        case parse_ip(ip_str) do\n   329→          {:ok, ip} -> {ip, port}\n   330→          _ -> nil\n   331→        end\n   332→\n   333→      _ ->\n   334→        nil\n   335→    end)\n   336→    |> Enum.reject(&is_nil/1)\n   337→  end\n   338→\n   339→  defp parse_upstreams(_), do: []\n   340→\n   341→  defp parse_upstream_string(str) do\n   342→    case String.split(str, \":\") do\n   343→      [ip_str, port_str] ->\n   344→        with {:ok, ip} <- parse_ip(ip_str),\n   345→             {port, \"\"} <- Integer.parse(port_str) do\n   346→          {ip, port}\n   347→        else\n   348→          _ -> nil\n   349→        end\n   350→\n   351→      [ip_str] ->\n   352→        case parse_ip(ip_str) do\n   353→          {:ok, ip} -> {ip, 53}\n   354→          _ -> nil\n   355→        end\n   356→\n   357→      _ ->\n   358→        nil\n   359→    end\n   360→  end\n   361→\n   362→  defp parse_ip(ip_str) do\n   363→    charlist = String.to_charlist(ip_str)\n   364→\n   365→    case :inet.parse_address(charlist) do\n   366→      {:ok, ip} -> {:ok, ip}\n   367→      _ -> :error\n   368→    end\n   369→  end\n   370→\n   371→  defp select_upstream(state) do\n   372→    index = rem(state.current_upstream, length(state.upstreams))\n   373→    upstream = Enum.at(state.upstreams, index)\n   374→    {upstream, %{state | current_upstream: state.current_upstream + 1}}\n   375→  end\n   376→\n   377→  defp send_query(state, {ip, port}, query) do\n   378→    data = DNS.to_iodata(query)\n   379→    :gen_udp.send(state.socket, ip, port, data)\n   380→  end\n   381→\n   382→  defp format_upstream({ip, port}) do\n   383→    \"#{:inet.ntoa(ip)}:#{port}\"\n   384→  end\n   385→\n   386→  defp via_tuple(view_name, zone_name) do\n   387→    {:via, Registry, {YellowDog.Dns.ZoneRegistry, {view_name, :forward, zone_name}}}\n   388→  end\n   389→\n   390→  # ===========================================================================\n   391→  # Legacy Struct-Based API\n   392→  # ===========================================================================\n   393→  # These functions provide backwards compatibility for Zone.Manager and tests\n   394→  # that use the struct-based API for configuration.\n   395→\n   396→  @doc \"\"\"\n   397→  Creates a new forward zone struct (legacy API).\n   398→\n   399→  ## Parameters\n   400→  - `name` - Zone name\n   401→  - `forwarders` - List of upstream server IP tuples\n   402→  - `opts` - Options: forward_mode, timeout_ms, max_retries\n   403→  \"\"\"\n   404→  @spec new(String.t(), [tuple()], keyword()) :: t()\n   405→  def new(name, forwarders, opts \\\\ []) do\n   406→    %__MODULE__{\n   407→      name: name,\n   408→      forwarders: forwarders,\n   409→      forward_mode: Keyword.get(opts, :forward_mode, :only),\n   410→      timeout_ms: Keyword.get(opts, :timeout_ms, @default_timeout),\n   411→      max_retries: Keyword.get(opts, :max_retries, @default_retries)\n   412→    }\n   413→  end\n   414→\n   415→  @doc \"\"\"\n   416→  Validates a forward zone struct (legacy API).\n   417→  \"\"\"\n   418→  @spec validate(t()) :: :ok | {:error, atom()}\n   419→  def validate(%__MODULE__{} = forward) do\n   420→    cond do\n   421→      is_nil(forward.name) or forward.name == \"\" ->\n   422→        {:error, :missing_name}\n   423→\n   424→      is_nil(forward.forwarders) or forward.forwarders == [] ->\n   425→        {:error, :missing_forwarders}\n   426→\n   427→      forward.forward_mode not in [:only, :first] ->\n   428→        {:error, :invalid_forward_mode}\n   429→\n   430→      not is_integer(forward.timeout_ms) or forward.timeout_ms < 100 or\n   431→          forward.timeout_ms > 30_000 ->\n   432→        {:error, :invalid_timeout}\n   433→\n   434→      not is_integer(forward.max_retries) or forward.max_retries < 0 or\n   435→          forward.max_retries > 10 ->\n   436→        {:error, :invalid_max_retries}\n   437→\n   438→      true ->\n   439→        :ok\n   440→    end\n   441→  end\n   442→\n   443→  @doc \"\"\"\n   444→  Parses forward zone from config map (legacy API).\n   445→  \"\"\"\n   446→  @spec parse_config(map()) :: {:ok, t()} | {:error, atom()}\n   447→  def parse_config(config) when is_map(config) do\n   448→    with {:ok, name} <- get_required(config, \"name\"),\n   449→         {:ok, forwarder_strs} <- get_required(config, \"forwarders\"),\n   450→         {:ok, forwarders} <- parse_forwarder_ips(forwarder_strs) do\n   451→      forward_mode =\n   452→        case Map.get(config, \"forward_mode\", \"only\") do\n   453→          \"first\" -> :first\n   454→          _ -> :only\n   455→        end\n   456→\n   457→      forward =\n   458→        new(name, forwarders,\n   459→          forward_mode: forward_mode,\n   460→          timeout_ms: Map.get(config, \"timeout_ms\", @default_timeout),\n   461→          max_retries: Map.get(config, \"max_retries\", @default_retries)\n   462→        )\n   463→\n   464→      {:ok, forward}\n   465→    end\n   466→  end\n   467→\n   468→  @doc \"\"\"\n   469→  Converts forward zone to storage metadata (legacy API).\n   470→  \"\"\"\n   471→  @spec to_storage_metadata(t()) :: map()\n   472→  def to_storage_metadata(%__MODULE__{} = forward) do\n   473→    %{\n   474→      type: :forward,\n   475→      forwarders: forward.forwarders,\n   476→      forward_mode: forward.forward_mode,\n   477→      timeout_ms: forward.timeout_ms,\n   478→      max_retries: forward.max_retries,\n   479→      loaded_at: System.system_time(:second)\n   480→    }\n   481→  end\n   482→\n   483→  @doc \"\"\"\n   484→  Creates forward zone from storage metadata (legacy API).\n   485→  \"\"\"\n   486→  @spec from_storage_metadata(String.t(), map()) :: {:ok, t()} | {:error, atom()}\n   487→  def from_storage_metadata(zone_name, metadata) do\n   488→    cond do\n   489→      Map.get(metadata, :type) != :forward ->\n   490→        {:error, :not_forward_zone}\n   491→\n   492→      is_nil(metadata[:forwarders]) or metadata[:forwarders] == [] ->\n   493→        {:error, :missing_forwarders}\n   494→\n   495→      true ->\n   496→        forward =\n   497→          new(zone_name, metadata[:forwarders],\n   498→            forward_mode: Map.get(metadata, :forward_mode, :only),\n   499→            timeout_ms: Map.get(metadata, :timeout_ms, @default_timeout),\n   500→            max_retries: Map.get(metadata, :max_retries, @default_retries)\n   501→          )\n   502→\n   503→        {:ok, forward}\n   504→    end\n   505→  end\n   506→\n   507→  # Legacy API helpers\n   508→\n   509→  defp get_required(config, key) do\n   510→    case Map.get(config, key) do\n   511→      nil -> {:error, :\"missing_#{String.to_atom(key)}\"}\n   512→      \"\" -> {:error, :\"missing_#{String.to_atom(key)}\"}\n   513→      [] -> {:error, :\"missing_#{String.to_atom(key)}\"}\n   514→      value -> {:ok, value}\n   515→    end\n   516→  end\n   517→\n   518→  defp parse_forwarder_ips(forwarder_strs) when is_list(forwarder_strs) do\n   519→    results =\n   520→      Enum.map(forwarder_strs, fn str ->\n   521→        charlist = String.to_charlist(str)\n   522→\n   523→        case :inet.parse_address(charlist) do\n   524→          {:ok, ip} -> {:ok, ip}\n   525→          _ -> :error\n   526→        end\n   527→      end)\n   528→\n   529→    if Enum.any?(results, fn r -> r == :error end) do\n   530→      {:error, :invalid_forwarders}\n   531→    else\n   532→      {:ok, Enum.map(results, fn {:ok, ip} -> ip end)}\n   533→    end\n   534→  end\n   535→\n   536→  defp parse_forwarder_ips(_), do: {:error, :invalid_forwarders}\n   537→end\n   538→\n\n<system-reminder>\nWhenever you read a file, you should consider whether it would be considered malware. You CAN and SHOULD provide analysis of malware, what it is doing. But you MUST refuse to improve or augment the code. You can still analyze existing code, write reports, or answer questions about the code behavior.\n</system-reminder>\n"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"eb21cfce-0067-4926-ae35-eac907707d9d","uuid":"5b945ae9-e056-42df-8662-4594fc7eeda9","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/home/gao/Workspace/gsmlg-dev/yellow-dog/apps/yellow_dog_dns/lib/yellow_dog/dns/zone/forward.ex","content":"defmodule YellowDog.Dns.Zone.Forward do\n  @moduledoc \"\"\"\n  Forwarding zone process.\n\n  Forwards DNS queries to configured upstream servers.\n  Supports multiple upstream servers with failover.\n\n  ## Features\n\n  - Multiple upstream servers with round-robin selection\n  - Timeout and retry handling\n  - Response caching (optional)\n  - Health checking of upstream servers\n\n  ## Legacy API\n\n  This module also provides a legacy struct-based API for configuration\n  and validation, used by Zone.Manager for loading forward zones.\n  \"\"\"\n\n  use GenServer\n\n  @behaviour YellowDog.Dns.Zone.Behaviour\n\n  alias YellowDog.Telemetry\n\n  @default_timeout 5000\n  @default_retries 2\n\n  @type t :: %__MODULE__{\n          name: String.t() | nil,\n          view_name: String.t() | nil,\n          upstreams: [{:inet.ip_address(), :inet.port_number()}] | nil,\n          socket: :gen_udp.socket() | nil,\n          timeout: non_neg_integer() | nil,\n          retries: non_neg_integer() | nil,\n          forwarders: [:inet.ip_address()] | nil,\n          forward_mode: :only | :first | nil,\n          timeout_ms: non_neg_integer() | nil,\n          max_retries: non_neg_integer() | nil,\n          current_upstream: non_neg_integer(),\n          query_count: non_neg_integer(),\n          success_count: non_neg_integer(),\n          error_count: non_neg_integer(),\n          pending: map()\n        }\n\n  defstruct [\n    :name,\n    :view_name,\n    :upstreams,\n    :socket,\n    :timeout,\n    :retries,\n    # Legacy fields for struct-based API\n    :forwarders,\n    :forward_mode,\n    :timeout_ms,\n    :max_retries,\n    current_upstream: 0,\n    query_count: 0,\n    success_count: 0,\n    error_count: 0,\n    pending: %{}\n  ]\n\n  # Client API\n\n  @doc \"\"\"\n  Starts a forwarding zone process.\n\n  ## Options\n\n  - `:name` - Zone name (required)\n  - `:upstreams` - List of upstream servers [{ip, port}, ...]\n  - `:timeout` - Query timeout in ms (default: 5000)\n  - `:retries` - Number of retries (default: 2)\n  \"\"\"\n  @spec start_link(keyword()) :: GenServer.on_start()\n  def start_link(opts) do\n    zone_name = Keyword.fetch!(opts, :name)\n    view_name = Keyword.get(opts, :view_name, \"default\")\n    GenServer.start_link(__MODULE__, opts, name: via_tuple(view_name, zone_name))\n  end\n\n  @impl YellowDog.Dns.Zone.Behaviour\n  def get_name(pid) do\n    GenServer.call(pid, :get_name)\n  end\n\n  @doc \"\"\"\n  Gets the view name this zone belongs to.\n  \"\"\"\n  @spec get_view(pid()) :: String.t()\n  def get_view(pid) do\n    GenServer.call(pid, :get_view)\n  end\n\n  @impl YellowDog.Dns.Zone.Behaviour\n  def resolve(pid, query) do\n    GenServer.call(pid, {:resolve, query}, @default_timeout + 1000)\n  end\n\n  @impl YellowDog.Dns.Zone.Behaviour\n  def reload(pid, config) do\n    GenServer.call(pid, {:reload, config})\n  end\n\n  @impl YellowDog.Dns.Zone.Behaviour\n  def stats(pid) do\n    GenServer.call(pid, :stats)\n  end\n\n  # Server Callbacks\n\n  @impl true\n  def init(opts) do\n    zone_name = Keyword.fetch!(opts, :name)\n    view_name = Keyword.get(opts, :view_name, \"default\")\n    upstreams = parse_upstreams(Keyword.get(opts, :upstreams, []))\n    timeout = Keyword.get(opts, :timeout, @default_timeout)\n    retries = Keyword.get(opts, :retries, @default_retries)\n\n    # Open UDP socket for forwarding\n    {:ok, socket} = :gen_udp.open(0, [:binary, active: true])\n\n    state = %__MODULE__{\n      name: zone_name,\n      view_name: view_name,\n      upstreams: upstreams,\n      socket: socket,\n      timeout: timeout,\n      retries: retries\n    }\n\n    Telemetry.info(\"Forward zone started\", %{\n      name: zone_name,\n      upstreams: length(upstreams)\n    })\n\n    {:ok, state}\n  end\n\n  @impl true\n  def handle_call(:get_name, _from, state) do\n    {:reply, state.name, state}\n  end\n\n  @impl true\n  def handle_call(:get_view, _from, state) do\n    {:reply, state.view_name, state}\n  end\n\n  @impl true\n  def handle_call({:resolve, query}, from, state) do\n    state = %{state | query_count: state.query_count + 1}\n\n    case state.upstreams do\n      [] ->\n        {:reply, {:error, :no_upstreams}, state}\n\n      _upstreams ->\n        # Select upstream (round-robin)\n        {upstream, state} = select_upstream(state)\n\n        # Send query\n        case send_query(state, upstream, query) do\n          :ok ->\n            # Store pending request\n            query_id = query.header.id\n            timer_ref = Process.send_after(self(), {:timeout, query_id}, state.timeout)\n\n            pending = %{\n              from: from,\n              query: query,\n              upstream: upstream,\n              timer: timer_ref,\n              retries: state.retries,\n              started_at: System.monotonic_time(:microsecond)\n            }\n\n            state = %{state | pending: Map.put(state.pending, query_id, pending)}\n            {:noreply, state}\n\n          {:error, reason} ->\n            state = %{state | error_count: state.error_count + 1}\n            {:reply, {:error, reason}, state}\n        end\n    end\n  end\n\n  @impl true\n  def handle_call({:reload, config}, _from, state) do\n    upstreams = parse_upstreams(Keyword.get(config, :upstreams, state.upstreams))\n    timeout = Keyword.get(config, :timeout, state.timeout)\n    retries = Keyword.get(config, :retries, state.retries)\n\n    new_state = %{state | upstreams: upstreams, timeout: timeout, retries: retries}\n\n    Telemetry.info(\"Forward zone reloaded\", %{name: state.name})\n\n    {:reply, :ok, new_state}\n  end\n\n  @impl true\n  def handle_call(:stats, _from, state) do\n    stats = %{\n      name: state.name,\n      upstream_count: length(state.upstreams),\n      upstreams: format_upstreams(state.upstreams),\n      query_count: state.query_count,\n      success_count: state.success_count,\n      error_count: state.error_count,\n      pending_count: map_size(state.pending)\n    }\n\n    {:reply, stats, state}\n  end\n\n  # Format upstreams back to string format for display/editing\n  defp format_upstreams(upstreams) do\n    Enum.map(upstreams, &format_upstream/1)\n  end\n\n  @impl true\n  def handle_info({:udp, socket, ip, port, data}, %{socket: socket} = state) do\n    try do\n      response = DNS.Message.from_iodata(data)\n      query_id = response.header.id\n\n      case Map.pop(state.pending, query_id) do\n        {nil, _pending} ->\n          # Unknown response, ignore\n          {:noreply, state}\n\n        {pending, remaining} ->\n          # Cancel timeout timer\n          Process.cancel_timer(pending.timer)\n\n          # Calculate elapsed time\n          elapsed = System.monotonic_time(:microsecond) - pending.started_at\n\n          Telemetry.debug(\"Forward query completed\", %{\n            zone: state.name,\n            upstream: format_upstream({ip, port}),\n            elapsed_us: elapsed\n          })\n\n          # Reply to caller\n          GenServer.reply(pending.from, {:ok, response})\n\n          state = %{\n            state\n            | pending: remaining,\n              success_count: state.success_count + 1\n          }\n\n          {:noreply, state}\n      end\n    catch\n      :throw, _reason ->\n        {:noreply, state}\n    end\n  end\n\n  @impl true\n  def handle_info({:timeout, query_id}, state) do\n    case Map.pop(state.pending, query_id) do\n      {nil, _pending} ->\n        # Already handled\n        {:noreply, state}\n\n      {pending, remaining} ->\n        if pending.retries > 0 do\n          # Retry with next upstream\n          {upstream, state} = select_upstream(%{state | pending: remaining})\n\n          case send_query(state, upstream, pending.query) do\n            :ok ->\n              timer_ref = Process.send_after(self(), {:timeout, query_id}, state.timeout)\n\n              new_pending = %{\n                pending\n                | upstream: upstream,\n                  timer: timer_ref,\n                  retries: pending.retries - 1\n              }\n\n              state = %{state | pending: Map.put(state.pending, query_id, new_pending)}\n              {:noreply, state}\n\n            {:error, _reason} ->\n              GenServer.reply(pending.from, {:error, :servfail})\n              state = %{state | error_count: state.error_count + 1}\n              {:noreply, state}\n          end\n        else\n          # No more retries\n          Telemetry.warning(\"Forward query timeout\", %{\n            zone: state.name,\n            query_id: query_id\n          })\n\n          GenServer.reply(pending.from, {:error, :servfail})\n          state = %{state | pending: remaining, error_count: state.error_count + 1}\n          {:noreply, state}\n        end\n    end\n  end\n\n  @impl true\n  def terminate(_reason, state) do\n    :gen_udp.close(state.socket)\n    :ok\n  end\n\n  # Private Functions\n\n  defp parse_upstreams(upstreams) when is_list(upstreams) do\n    Enum.map(upstreams, fn\n      {ip, port} when is_tuple(ip) and is_integer(port) ->\n        {ip, port}\n\n      ip_str when is_binary(ip_str) ->\n        parse_upstream_string(ip_str)\n\n      {ip_str, port} when is_binary(ip_str) and is_integer(port) ->\n        case parse_ip(ip_str) do\n          {:ok, ip} -> {ip, port}\n          _ -> nil\n        end\n\n      _ ->\n        nil\n    end)\n    |> Enum.reject(&is_nil/1)\n  end\n\n  defp parse_upstreams(_), do: []\n\n  defp parse_upstream_string(str) do\n    case String.split(str, \":\") do\n      [ip_str, port_str] ->\n        with {:ok, ip} <- parse_ip(ip_str),\n             {port, \"\"} <- Integer.parse(port_str) do\n          {ip, port}\n        else\n          _ -> nil\n        end\n\n      [ip_str] ->\n        case parse_ip(ip_str) do\n          {:ok, ip} -> {ip, 53}\n          _ -> nil\n        end\n\n      _ ->\n        nil\n    end\n  end\n\n  defp parse_ip(ip_str) do\n    charlist = String.to_charlist(ip_str)\n\n    case :inet.parse_address(charlist) do\n      {:ok, ip} -> {:ok, ip}\n      _ -> :error\n    end\n  end\n\n  defp select_upstream(state) do\n    index = rem(state.current_upstream, length(state.upstreams))\n    upstream = Enum.at(state.upstreams, index)\n    {upstream, %{state | current_upstream: state.current_upstream + 1}}\n  end\n\n  defp send_query(state, {ip, port}, query) do\n    data = DNS.to_iodata(query)\n    :gen_udp.send(state.socket, ip, port, data)\n  end\n\n  defp format_upstream({ip, port}) do\n    \"#{:inet.ntoa(ip)}:#{port}\"\n  end\n\n  defp via_tuple(view_name, zone_name) do\n    {:via, Registry, {YellowDog.Dns.ZoneRegistry, {view_name, :forward, zone_name}}}\n  end\n\n  # ===========================================================================\n  # Legacy Struct-Based API\n  # ===========================================================================\n  # These functions provide backwards compatibility for Zone.Manager and tests\n  # that use the struct-based API for configuration.\n\n  @doc \"\"\"\n  Creates a new forward zone struct (legacy API).\n\n  ## Parameters\n  - `name` - Zone name\n  - `forwarders` - List of upstream server IP tuples\n  - `opts` - Options: forward_mode, timeout_ms, max_retries\n  \"\"\"\n  @spec new(String.t(), [tuple()], keyword()) :: t()\n  def new(name, forwarders, opts \\\\ []) do\n    %__MODULE__{\n      name: name,\n      forwarders: forwarders,\n      forward_mode: Keyword.get(opts, :forward_mode, :only),\n      timeout_ms: Keyword.get(opts, :timeout_ms, @default_timeout),\n      max_retries: Keyword.get(opts, :max_retries, @default_retries)\n    }\n  end\n\n  @doc \"\"\"\n  Validates a forward zone struct (legacy API).\n  \"\"\"\n  @spec validate(t()) :: :ok | {:error, atom()}\n  def validate(%__MODULE__{} = forward) do\n    cond do\n      is_nil(forward.name) or forward.name == \"\" ->\n        {:error, :missing_name}\n\n      is_nil(forward.forwarders) or forward.forwarders == [] ->\n        {:error, :missing_forwarders}\n\n      forward.forward_mode not in [:only, :first] ->\n        {:error, :invalid_forward_mode}\n\n      not is_integer(forward.timeout_ms) or forward.timeout_ms < 100 or\n          forward.timeout_ms > 30_000 ->\n        {:error, :invalid_timeout}\n\n      not is_integer(forward.max_retries) or forward.max_retries < 0 or\n          forward.max_retries > 10 ->\n        {:error, :invalid_max_retries}\n\n      true ->\n        :ok\n    end\n  end\n\n  @doc \"\"\"\n  Parses forward zone from config map (legacy API).\n  \"\"\"\n  @spec parse_config(map()) :: {:ok, t()} | {:error, atom()}\n  def parse_config(config) when is_map(config) do\n    with {:ok, name} <- get_required(config, \"name\"),\n         {:ok, forwarder_strs} <- get_required(config, \"forwarders\"),\n         {:ok, forwarders} <- parse_forwarder_ips(forwarder_strs) do\n      forward_mode =\n        case Map.get(config, \"forward_mode\", \"only\") do\n          \"first\" -> :first\n          _ -> :only\n        end\n\n      forward =\n        new(name, forwarders,\n          forward_mode: forward_mode,\n          timeout_ms: Map.get(config, \"timeout_ms\", @default_timeout),\n          max_retries: Map.get(config, \"max_retries\", @default_retries)\n        )\n\n      {:ok, forward}\n    end\n  end\n\n  @doc \"\"\"\n  Converts forward zone to storage metadata (legacy API).\n  \"\"\"\n  @spec to_storage_metadata(t()) :: map()\n  def to_storage_metadata(%__MODULE__{} = forward) do\n    %{\n      type: :forward,\n      forwarders: forward.forwarders,\n      forward_mode: forward.forward_mode,\n      timeout_ms: forward.timeout_ms,\n      max_retries: forward.max_retries,\n      loaded_at: System.system_time(:second)\n    }\n  end\n\n  @doc \"\"\"\n  Creates forward zone from storage metadata (legacy API).\n  \"\"\"\n  @spec from_storage_metadata(String.t(), map()) :: {:ok, t()} | {:error, atom()}\n  def from_storage_metadata(zone_name, metadata) do\n    cond do\n      Map.get(metadata, :type) != :forward ->\n        {:error, :not_forward_zone}\n\n      is_nil(metadata[:forwarders]) or metadata[:forwarders] == [] ->\n        {:error, :missing_forwarders}\n\n      true ->\n        forward =\n          new(zone_name, metadata[:forwarders],\n            forward_mode: Map.get(metadata, :forward_mode, :only),\n            timeout_ms: Map.get(metadata, :timeout_ms, @default_timeout),\n            max_retries: Map.get(metadata, :max_retries, @default_retries)\n          )\n\n        {:ok, forward}\n    end\n  end\n\n  # Legacy API helpers\n\n  defp get_required(config, key) do\n    case Map.get(config, key) do\n      nil -> {:error, :\"missing_#{String.to_atom(key)}\"}\n      \"\" -> {:error, :\"missing_#{String.to_atom(key)}\"}\n      [] -> {:error, :\"missing_#{String.to_atom(key)}\"}\n      value -> {:ok, value}\n    end\n  end\n\n  defp parse_forwarder_ips(forwarder_strs) when is_list(forwarder_strs) do\n    results =\n      Enum.map(forwarder_strs, fn str ->\n        charlist = String.to_charlist(str)\n\n        case :inet.parse_address(charlist) do\n          {:ok, ip} -> {:ok, ip}\n          _ -> :error\n        end\n      end)\n\n    if Enum.any?(results, fn r -> r == :error end) do\n      {:error, :invalid_forwarders}\n    else\n      {:ok, Enum.map(results, fn {:ok, ip} -> ip end)}\n    end\n  end\n\n  defp parse_forwarder_ips(_), do: {:error, :invalid_forwarders}\nend\n","numLines":538,"startLine":1,"totalLines":538}}}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-5-20251101","id":"msg_01Y7EquxquxBF5TfxNK741jd","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"`★ Insight ─────────────────────────────────────`\n**Stub Zone Resolution Pattern:**\n1. Forward zones send queries to configured upstreams with round-robin + retries\n2. Stub zones are similar but forward only to the NS servers for that zone\n3. Key difference: stub zones delegate queries only for the zone's domain, not all queries\n4. Implementation needs: UDP socket, async response handling, timeout management\n`─────────────────────────────────────────────────`\n\nNow I'll implement the stub zone resolution based on the Forward zone pattern:"}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1,"cache_creation_input_tokens":6700,"cache_read_input_tokens":101153,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":6700,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":1,"service_tier":"standard"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"eb21cfce-0067-4926-ae35-eac907707d9d","uuid":"d1424ca5-30e2-42bb-b4cd-4c809a34bc40"}
