{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"text","text":"This session is being continued from a previous conversation that ran out of context. The summary below covers the earlier portion of the conversation.\n\nAnalysis:\nLet me chronologically analyze the conversation:\n\n1. Initial Request: The user invoked \"Loki Mode\" - an autonomous development mode where I should read continuity files, identify tasks, execute them, and continue improving the codebase. This is iteration #5 (retry #4) with a PRD at ./prd.md.\n\n2. First Actions: I read multiple files in parallel:\n   - `.loki/CONTINUITY.md` - Shows extensive progress through 16 iterations, including security fixes, rate limiting, test coverage expansion\n   - `.loki/state/relevant-learnings.json` - Empty patterns/mistakes/successes\n   - `.loki/state/resources.json` - Memory at 80% (warning threshold)\n   - `.loki/queue/in-progress.json` - Empty queue\n   - `prd.md` - PRD for DHCP Service Data Persistence\n\n3. From CONTINUITY.md, I identified next steps:\n   - Fix LeaseStorage implementation bugs (cleanup_expired, clear_all)\n   - Add unit tests for ServiceStore (mDNS) - already exists\n   - Add unit tests for ServiceRegistry (mDNS) - already exists  \n   - Implement stub zone resolution (DNS)\n\n4. First Fix - LeaseStorage cleanup_expired bug:\n   - Location: `apps/yellow_dog_dhcpv4/lib/yellow_dog/dhcpv4/lease_storage.ex`\n   - Bug: Code piped `Enum.each` (returns `:ok`) into `length()` causing badarg\n   - Fix: Store filtered expired records in variable, then return length\n   - Committed: `77a8983`\n\n5. Second Task - Stub Zone Resolution:\n   - Read existing stub zone at `apps/yellow_dog_dns/lib/yellow_dog/dns/zone/stub.ex` - had TODO for resolution\n   - Read forward zone at `apps/yellow_dog_dns/lib/yellow_dog/dns/zone/forward.ex` as a model\n   - Implemented full stub zone resolution with:\n     - UDP socket for querying NS servers\n     - Round-robin NS server selection\n     - Timeout and retry handling\n     - Glue record management\n     - Async response handling\n\n6. Test Creation - Stub Zone Tests:\n   - Created `apps/yellow_dog_dns/test/yellow_dog/dns/zone/stub_test.exs`\n   - Encountered multiple errors that needed fixing:\n     a. `question` key should be `qdlist` in DNS.Message struct\n     b. `opcode: :query` should use `DNS.Message.OpCode.new(0)` - fixed by using `Header.new()`\n     c. Question type `:A` should be numeric value - created `type_to_number/1` helper\n     d. Registry cleanup issues - fixed setup to use `start_supervised`\n   - Final test result: 15 tests, 0 failures\n\nSummary:\n1. Primary Request and Intent:\n   The user invoked \"Loki Mode\" - an autonomous continuous improvement mode for the YellowDog project (an 11-app Elixir umbrella with DNS, mDNS, DHCPv4, DHCPv6 services). The system should:\n   - Read `.loki/CONTINUITY.md` to understand progress and identify next tasks\n   - Execute tasks autonomously without asking questions\n   - Run tests to verify changes\n   - Commit changes atomically\n   - Update continuity documentation\n   - Never stop - always find the next improvement\n\n2. Key Technical Concepts:\n   - Elixir/OTP umbrella project architecture\n   - GenServer pattern for DNS zone management\n   - Mnesia for lease storage persistence\n   - DNS protocol (RFC compliant) with ex_dns library\n   - Stub zones vs Forward zones in DNS\n   - UDP socket communication with async response handling\n   - Round-robin server selection with retry logic\n   - ExUnit testing with Registry supervision\n   - Token bucket rate limiting (previously implemented)\n\n3. Files and Code Sections:\n\n   - **`apps/yellow_dog_dhcpv4/lib/yellow_dog/dhcpv4/lease_storage.ex`**\n     - Bug fix for `cleanup_expired/0` function\n     - Original code piped `Enum.each` (returns `:ok`) into `length()` causing badarg error\n     - Fix: Store filtered records in variable before processing\n     ```elixir\n     def cleanup_expired do\n       now = System.system_time(:second)\n\n       transaction = fn ->\n         # Find all active leases that have expired\n         expired_records =\n           :mnesia.match_object(@table_name, lease_record(state: :active, _: :_), :read)\n           |> Enum.filter(fn record ->\n             lease_record(expires_at: expires_at) = record\n             expires_at <= now\n           end)\n\n         # Update each expired record\n         Enum.each(expired_records, fn record ->\n           updated_record =\n             lease_record(record,\n               state: :expired,\n               updated_at: now\n             )\n\n           :mnesia.write(@table_name, updated_record, :write)\n         end)\n\n         # Return count of expired records\n         length(expired_records)\n       end\n       # ... rest of function\n     end\n     ```\n\n   - **`apps/yellow_dog_dns/lib/yellow_dog/dns/zone/stub.ex`**\n     - Complete rewrite implementing stub zone DNS resolution\n     - Key features: NS record management, glue records, UDP forwarding, round-robin selection, timeout/retry\n     ```elixir\n     defmodule YellowDog.Dns.Zone.Stub do\n       use GenServer\n       @behaviour YellowDog.Dns.Zone.Behaviour\n\n       @default_timeout 5000\n       @default_retries 2\n       @default_port 53\n\n       defstruct [\n         :name, :view_name, :socket, :created_at,\n         ns_records: [], glue_records: %{},\n         timeout: @default_timeout, retries: @default_retries,\n         current_ns: 0, query_count: 0, success_count: 0,\n         error_count: 0, pending: %{}\n       ]\n\n       # Key functions implemented:\n       # - start_link/1, get_name/1, get_view/1, resolve/2, reload/2, stats/1\n       # - get_ns_records/1, add_glue_record/3\n       # - handle_info for {:udp, ...} and {:timeout, ...}\n       # - Private: parse_glue_records, get_available_ns_servers, select_ns_server, send_query\n     end\n     ```\n\n   - **`apps/yellow_dog_dns/test/yellow_dog/dns/zone/stub_test.exs`**\n     - Comprehensive test suite for stub zone (15 tests)\n     - Tests: start_link, get_name/get_view, get_ns_records, add_glue_record, resolve, reload, stats, timeout handling\n     ```elixir\n     defmodule YellowDog.Dns.Zone.StubTest do\n       use ExUnit.Case, async: false\n       alias YellowDog.Dns.Zone.Stub\n\n       setup do\n         {:ok, _registry} =\n           start_supervised({Registry, keys: :unique, name: YellowDog.Dns.ZoneRegistry})\n         %{registry: registry_name}\n       end\n\n       # Helper to create test queries\n       defp create_test_query(name, type) do\n         header = DNS.Message.Header.new()\n         type_num = type_to_number(type)\n         question = DNS.Message.Question.new(name, type_num, 1)\n         %DNS.Message{\n           header: %{header | id: :rand.uniform(65535)},\n           qdlist: [question]\n         }\n       end\n\n       defp type_to_number(:A), do: 1\n       # ... other type mappings\n     end\n     ```\n\n4. Errors and Fixes:\n\n   - **LeaseStorage cleanup_expired badarg error**:\n     - Error: `Enum.each` returns `:ok`, piping to `length()` causes badarg\n     - Fix: Store filtered list in variable, return its length separately\n\n   - **DNS.Message struct key error**:\n     - Error: `key :question not found` when creating DNS.Message\n     - Fix: Changed `question:` to `qdlist:` (correct field name)\n\n   - **OpCode struct error**:\n     - Error: `function :query.value/0 is undefined`\n     - Fix: Use `DNS.Message.Header.new()` instead of manually constructing header with `opcode: :query`\n\n   - **DNS Question type atom error**:\n     - Error: `Protocol.UndefinedError: protocol DNS.Parameter not implemented for type Atom` for `:A`\n     - Fix: Created `type_to_number/1` helper and used `DNS.Message.Question.new(name, type_num, 1)`\n\n   - **Registry cleanup causing noproc errors**:\n     - Error: Tests failing with `unknown registry` or `noproc` errors\n     - Fix: Changed setup to use `start_supervised`