{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-5-20251101","id":"msg_01AQ9APs5i2RhMBAy3FHHJdu","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Now I understand. The issue is that `:mnesia.clear_table/1` doesn't need to be wrapped in a transaction - it's already an atomic operation. Let me check the Mnesia documentation behavior.\n\nThe problem is that when `clear_all/0` is wrapped in `mnesia.transaction`, and `mnesia.clear_table/1` also does its own transaction, the nested transactions cause issues.\n\nThe fix is simple: don't wrap `clear_table` in a transaction since it's already transactional internally."}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2348,"cache_read_input_tokens":85641,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":2348,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":2,"service_tier":"standard"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"eb21cfce-0067-4926-ae35-eac907707d9d","uuid":"e5ed3321-27bd-4b5f-b4bc-a3ca0f474158"}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-5-20251101","id":"msg_01AQ9APs5i2RhMBAy3FHHJdu","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_014MMm8TRq9aDDKQCQwZPWAy","name":"Edit","input":{"replace_all":false,"file_path":"/home/gao/Workspace/gsmlg-dev/yellow-dog/apps/yellow_dog_dhcpv4/lib/yellow_dog/dhcpv4/lease_storage.ex","old_string":"  @spec clear_all() :: :ok\n  def clear_all do\n    transaction = fn ->\n      :mnesia.clear_table(@table_name)\n    end\n\n    case :mnesia.transaction(transaction) do\n      {:atomic, :ok} ->\n        :telemetry.execute(\n          [:yellow_dog, :dhcpv4, :lease_storage, :cleared],\n          %{count: 1},\n          %{}\n        )\n\n        :ok\n\n      {:aborted, reason} ->\n        :telemetry.execute(\n          [:yellow_dog, :dhcpv4, :lease_storage, :clear_failed],\n          %{count: 1},\n          %{reason: inspect(reason)}\n        )\n\n        {:error, reason}\n    end\n  end","new_string":"  @spec clear_all() :: :ok | {:error, term()}\n  def clear_all do\n    # Note: :mnesia.clear_table/1 is already atomic, don't wrap in transaction\n    # to avoid nested transaction issues\n    case :mnesia.clear_table(@table_name) do\n      {:atomic, :ok} ->\n        :telemetry.execute(\n          [:yellow_dog, :dhcpv4, :lease_storage, :cleared],\n          %{count: 1},\n          %{}\n        )\n\n        :ok\n\n      {:aborted, reason} ->\n        :telemetry.execute(\n          [:yellow_dog, :dhcpv4, :lease_storage, :clear_failed],\n          %{count: 1},\n          %{reason: inspect(reason)}\n        )\n\n        {:error, reason}\n    end\n  end"}}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2348,"cache_read_input_tokens":85641,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":2348,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":2,"service_tier":"standard"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"eb21cfce-0067-4926-ae35-e