{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-5-20251101","id":"msg_01GxH4YvZXoRCRoQzpo9uuQM","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"**★ Insight ─────────────────────────────────────**\nThe RecursionController uses a Registry (`YellowDog.Dns.RecursionRegistry`) for named process registration. When writing unit tests for GenServers that use via-tuples with Registry, we need to ensure the registry is started in `setup_all` before any tests run. This is a common pattern when testing distributed/named processes.\n**─────────────────────────────────────────────────**\n\nNow let me continue with the mDNS public API facade tests. First, let me check what the mDNS public API looks like:"}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1,"cache_creation_input_tokens":283,"cache_read_input_tokens":144126,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":283,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":1,"service_tier":"standard"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"84996b7b-e98e-4515-80e7-3bf6c146a135","uuid":"9508ffa9-6418-4003-ab05-3febec98f918"}
