low_dog_dhcpv6, etc.)\n   - GenServer patterns and testing\n   - DNS protocol handling (DNS.Message, DNS.Message.RCode, DNS.Message.Question)\n   - Registry-based process naming (via tuples)\n   - ExUnit testing with setup_all vs setup patterns\n   - Process trapping exits for error testing\n   - ETS tables for caching (MessageCache, NetworkMonitor)\n   - Token bucket rate limiting\n\n3. Files and Code Sections:\n   \n   - **apps/yellow_dog_dns/test/yellow_dog/dns/connection_process_test.exs** (CREATED)\n     - 41 comprehensive unit tests for DNS query orchestration\n     - Key pattern - building test DNS queries properly:\n     ```elixir\n     defp build_test_query(id \\\\ 12345, name \\\\ \"example.com\", type \\\\ :a) do\n       query = Message.new()\n       question = Question.new(name, type, :in)\n       header = %{query.header | id: id, qdcount: 1, rd: 1}\n       %{query | header: header, qdlist: [question]}\n     end\n     \n     # Helper to extract rcode value for comparison\n     defp rcode_value(%RCode{value: <<value::4>>}), do: value\n     defp rcode_value(other), do: other\n     ```\n     - Tests cover: start_link, submit_query, submit_raw_data, stats, connection_closed, timeout handling, resolution complete/error messages, phase updates, concurrent queries\n\n   - **apps/yellow_dog_dns/test/yellow_dog/dns/recursion_controller_test.exs** (CREATED)\n     - 16 unit tests for recursive DNS resolution controller\n     - Key pattern - starting Registry in setup_all:\n     ```elixir\n     setup_all do\n       case Registry.start_link(keys: :unique, name: YellowDog.Dns.RecursionRegistry) do\n         {:ok, _pid} -> :ok\n         {:error, {:already_started, _pid}} -> :ok\n       end\n       :ok\n     end\n     ```\n     - Tests cover: start_link, stats, format_error, UDP message handling, termination, concurrent usage, view name registration\n\n   - **apps/yellow_dog_mdns/test/yellow_dog/mdns_test.exs** (CREATED - IN PROGRESS)\n     - Tests for mDNS public API f