umbrella)\n   470→\n   471→### In Progress\n   472→- [ ] Continue test coverage expansion (mDNS public API facade)\n   473→\n   474→### Known Issues (All Security Issues Resolved)\n   475→1. ~~**CRITICAL**: Web console has NO authentication~~ **FIXED (b32bbd7)**\n   476→2. ~~**HIGH**: DHCP lease allocation has no rate limiting~~ **FIXED (e8f5f5e, b1096df)**\n   477→3. ~~**MEDIUM**: DNS compression loop vulnerability~~ **ALREADY MITIGATED in ex_dns**\n   478→4. ~~**MEDIUM**: DNS server has no rate limiting~~ **FIXED (a0fcd2b)**\n   479→5. ~~**MEDIUM**: mDNS server has no rate limiting~~ **FIXED (5d535ea)**\n   480→6. ~~**MEDIUM**: Basic auth has no brute-force protection~~ **FIXED (ea14f3c)**\n   481→\n   482→### Next Steps\n   483→1. Add mDNS public API facade unit tests\n   484→2. Continue test coverage expansion\n   485→3. Add DNS View module unit tests\n   486→4. Add DNS ZoneManager unit tests\n   487→\n   488→## Key Findings\n   489→\n   490→### DHCPv6 Handler Bug (FIXED - Iteration 2)\n   491→- Location: `apps/yellow_dog_dhcpv6/lib/yellow_dog/dhcpv6/handler.ex`\n   492→- Issue: Missing `use Abyss.Handler` macro, causing child_spec/1 error\n   493→- Fix: Added `use Abyss.Handler` and `@impl true` annotations\n   494→\n   495→### Abyss Listener Blocking (FIXED - Iteration 2)\n   496→- Location: `apps/abyss/lib/abyss/listener.ex`\n   497→- Issue: `transport.recv(socket, 0, :infinity)` blocked GenServer calls\n   498→- Fix: Changed to `recv(socket, 0, 100)` with retry loop for responsiveness\n   499→\n   500→### Console Config Validation (FIXED - Iteration 2)\n   501→- Location: `config/test.exs`\n   502→- Issue: `code_reloader` set at compile time in dev.exs but missing in test config\n   503→- Fix: Added `code_reloader: false` to test endpoint config\n   504→\n   505→### Security Improvements (Iteration 2)\n   506→1. DNS UDP handler: Added try-rescue for exception handling\n   507→2. DHCPv4: Replaced silent fallback with logging for ip_to_binary\n   508→3. DHCPv6: Added DNS label length validation (max 63 bytes per RFC 1035)\n   509→\n   510→## Mistakes & Learnings\n   511→1. **Umbrella dependency order matters**: When one umbrella app uses modules from another, it must declare the dependency explicitly.\n   512→2. **UDP server tests can be flaky**: Tests involving UDP servers with blocking recv calls can timeout - better to mark as integration tests.\n   513→3. **Handler modules need proper macros**: Protocol handler modules (like DHCPv6) need `use Abyss.Handler` to be supervised correctly.\n   514→4. **Blocking recv prevents GenServer responsiveness**: GenServer calls timeout if the process is blocked in recv(:infinity). Use timeouts with retry.\n   515→5. **Compile-time config needs runtime match**: Phoenix endpoints with compile-time config (like code_reloader) need matching runtime config in all environments.\n   516→6. **Silent fallbacks mask bugs**: Functions like ip_to_binary should log errors instead of silently using default values.\n   517→7. **RFC compliance matters**: DNS labels must be ≤63 bytes; validation prevents buffer issues.\n   518→\n   519→## Architecture Notes\n   520→- 11-app umbrella project\n   521→- Core services: DNS, mDNS, DHCPv4, DHCPv6\n   522→- Infrastructure libs: abyss (UDP), ex_dns (DNS protocol), ex_dhcp (DHCP protocol), geo_ip_db (IP geolocation)\n   523→- Web console: Phoenix LiveView with DaisyUI\n   524→\n   525→### PRD Implementation Modules\n   526→\n   527→**New Modules Created**:\n   528→1. `apps/yellow_dog_dhcpv4/lib/yellow_dog/dhcpv4/pool_config.ex`\n   529→   - TOML pool configuration parsing and validation\n   530→   - Subnet mask calculation from CIDR notation\n   531→   - Range and reservation conversion\n   532→\n   533→2. `apps/yellow_dog_dhcpv4/lib/yellow_dog/dhcpv4/acl.ex`\n   534→   - ACL rule validation and evaluation\n   535→   - Pattern matching (glob support for MAC addresses)\n   536→   - Priority-based rule ordering\n   537→\n   538→3. `apps/yellow_dog_dhcpv4/lib/yellow_dog/dhcpv4/conflict_resolver.ex`\n   539→   - GenServer for IP conflict management\n   540→   - Quarantine tracking with expiration\n   541→   - Integration with LeaseManager for reassignment\n   542→\n   543→4. `apps/yellow_dog_dhcpv4/lib/yellow_dog/dhcpv4/custom_options.ex`\n   544→   - DHCP option validation by type\n   545→   - Template variable substitution\n   546→   - Binary encoding for packet generation\n   547→\n   548→**Modified Modules**:\n   549→- `apps/yellow_dog_dhcpv4/lib/yellow_dog/dhcpv4/lease_manager.ex`\n   550→  - Fixed bugs in `get_pool_config` and `get_static_reservations` handlers\n   551→  - Changed from Map.get to Enum.find (pools stored as list)\n   552→  - Return full pool struct instead of partial config\n   553→\n   554→- `apps/yellow_dog_dhcpv4/lib/yellow_dog/dhcpv4/handler.ex`\n   555→  - ACL evaluation before lease allocation\n   556→  - ConflictResolver integration for DECLINE\n   557→  - CustomOptions support with template substitution\n   558→  - Build client info from message options\n   559→\n   560→### Performance Optimization (Iteration 10)\n   561→- **Pattern**: Single-pass option extraction is significantly more efficient\n   562→- **Before**: O(n*m) - iterate options m times for m needed fields\n   563→- **After**: O(n) - single iteration extracts all fields\n   564→- **Impact**: For typical DHCP messages with 10-15 options and 8 needed fields, reduces iterations from ~80-120 to ~10-15\n   565→\n   566→## Session Metadata\n   567→- Started: 2026-01-20\n   568→- Iteration: 18\n   569→- Commits: 226e25e, ff7c617, 4dfa6c4, 5d119ad, f287c42, 43704f2, 80c73c1, 68c77b3, 96c582d, b32bbd7, e8f5f5e, b1096df, a0fcd2b, 8b01401, eda3331, ea14f3c, 2c24860, ec33e3d, 9b24de1, b77d601, 5a5797b, 4a2ca45, e8b90f0, 77a8983, 9252a14, e5ee8b4, 6381b2f, 0c3b1ea, 17fa5e2\n   570→\n\n<system-reminder>\nWhenever you read a file, you should consider whether it would be considered malware. You CAN and SHOULD provide analysis of malware, what i