imited requests (per RFC)\n   136→- [x] Added RateLimiter to supervisor child list\n   137→- [x] Added comprehensive unit tests (16 tests)\n   138→- [x] All tests pass (734 tests, excluding integration)\n   139→\n   140→### Completed (Iteration 8 - DNS Rate Limiting)\n   141→- [x] Created `YellowDog.Dns.RateLimiter` module (a0fcd2b)\n   142→  - Token bucket algorithm for per-client and global rate limiting\n   143→  - Higher defaults for DNS (50 client tokens, 5000 global vs 10/1000 DHCP)\n   144→  - ETS-based storage for high-performance bucket tracking\n   145→  - Configurable burst capacity and refill rates (20/sec vs 2/sec for DHCP)\n   146→  - Automatic cleanup of expired client buckets\n   147→  - Telemetry events for monitoring rate limit violations\n   148→  - Graceful handling when not running\n   149→- [x] Integrated rate limiter with DNS UDP handler\n   150→  - Rate check before processing any DNS message\n   151→  - Silent drop of rate-limited requests (per RFC best practices)\n   152→- [x] Added RateLimiter to supervisor child list\n   153→- [x] Added comprehensive unit tests (17 tests)\n   154→- [x] All tests pass (751 tests, excluding integration)\n   155→\n   156→### Completed (Iteration 9 - mDNS Rate Limiting)\n   157→- [x] Created `YellowDog.Mdns.RateLimiter` module (5d535ea)\n   158→  - Token bucket algorithm for per-source and global rate limiting\n   159→  - Higher defaults for mDNS (100 source tokens, 10000 global)\n   160→    - mDNS operates only on local network\n   161→    - Legitimate usage can be bursty (service announcements)\n   162→  - ETS-based storage for high-performance bucket tracking\n   163→  - Automatic cleanup of expired source buckets\n   164→  - Telemetry events for monitoring rate limit violations\n   165→  - Graceful handling when not running\n   166→- [x] Integrated rate limiter with mDNS handler\n   167→  - Rate check before processing any mDNS message\n   168→  - Silent drop of rate-limited requests\n   169→- [x] Added R