view_name:zone_name format parsing\n   527→  - Zone validation: type-specific requirements (forward→upstreams, stub→ns_records)\n   528→  - All 6 zone types: auth, forward, stub, cache, root, rpz\n   529→  - File saving: atomic writes, backup, parent directories\n   530→  - Edge cases: root zone (.), dots in names, unicode, many zones\n   531→- [x] Created comprehensive DNS ViewManager unit tests (6b23a90)\n   532→  - 27 test cases covering DynamicSupervisor for View processes\n   533→  - Process lifecycle: start_link with default/custom names\n   534→  - View management: start_view, stop_view, get_view\n   535→  - View listing with priority-based sorting\n   536→  - Statistics gathering: view_count, per-view stats\n   537→  - Configuration updates: add/remove/update views\n   538→  - Default view protection during updates\n   539→  - Concurrent operations: parallel starts, parallel lists\n   540→  - ACL configurations: any, network rules, string references\n   541→- [x] Created comprehensive DNS AclStore unit tests (b89313e)\n   542→  - 24 test cases covering TOML persistence for named ACLs\n   543→  - ACL loading: network rules, geo rules, mixed rules, deny rules\n   544→  - ACL validation: name required, rule normalization\n   545→  - File saving: atomic writes, parent directory creation\n   546→  - Round-trip persistence: complex ACLs survive save/load cycle\n   547→  - Edge cases: unicode, quotes, many rules, single items, empty names\n   548→- [x] All 478 tests pass across umbrella\n   549→\n   550→### In Progress\n   551→- [ ] Continue test coverage expansion\n   552→\n   553→### Known Issues (All Security Issues Resolved)\n   554→1. ~~**CRITICAL**: Web console has NO authentication~~ **FIXED (b32bbd7)**\n   555→2. ~~**HIGH**: DHCP lease allocation has no rate limiting~~ **FIXED (e8f5f5e, b1096df)**\n   556→3. ~~**MEDIUM**: DNS compression loop vulnerability~~ **ALREADY MITIGATED in ex_dns**\n   557→4. ~~**MEDIUM**: DNS server has no rate limiting~~ **FIXED (a0fcd2b)**\n   558→5. ~~**MEDIUM**: mDNS server has no rate limiting~~ **FIXED (5d535ea)**\n   559→6. ~~**MEDIUM**: Basic auth has no brute-force protection~~ **FIXED (ea14f3c)**\n   560→\n   561→### Next Steps\n   562→1. Add DNS View module unit tests\n   563→2. Add DNS ZoneManager unit tests\n   564→3. Add DNS NameResolver unit tests\n   565→4. Continue test coverage expansion\n   566→\n   567→## Key Findings\n   568→\n   569→### DHCPv6 Handler Bug (FIXED - Iteration 2)\n   570→- Location: `apps/yellow_dog_dhcpv6/lib/yellow_dog/dhcpv6/handler.ex`\n   571→- Issue: Missing `use Abyss.Handler` macro, causing child_spec/1 error\n   572→- Fix: Added `use Abyss.Handler` and `@impl true` annotations\n   573→\n   574→### Abyss Listener Blocking (FIXED - Iteration 2)\n   575→- Location: `apps/abyss/lib/abyss/listener.ex`\n   576→- Issue: `transport.recv(socket, 0, :infinity)` blocked GenServer calls\n   577→- Fix: Changed to `recv(socket, 0, 100)` with retry loop for responsiveness\n   578→\n   579→### Console Config Validation (FIXED - Iteration 2)\n   580→- Location: `config/test.exs`\n   581→- Issue: `code_reloader` set at compile time in dev.exs but missing in test config\n   582→- Fix: Added `code_reloader: false` to test endpoint config\n   583→\n   584→### Security Improvements (Iteration 2)\n   585→1. DNS UDP handler: Added try-rescue for exception handling\n   586→2. DHCPv4: Replaced silent fallback with logging for ip_to_binary\n   587→3. DHCPv6: Added DNS label length validation (max 63 bytes per RFC 1035)\n   588→\n   589→## Mistakes & Learnings\n   590→1. **Umbrella dependency order matters**: When one umbrella app uses modules from another, it must declare the dependency explicitly.\n   591→2. **UDP server tests can be flaky**: Tests involving UDP servers with blocking recv calls can timeout - better to mark as integration tests.\n   592→3. **Handler modules need proper macros**: Protocol handler modules (like DHCPv6) need `use Abyss.Handler` to be supervised correctly.\n   593→4. **Blocking recv prevents GenServer responsiveness**: GenServer calls timeout if the process is blocked in recv(:infinity). Use timeouts with retry.\n   594→5. **Compile-time config needs runtime match**: Phoenix endpoints with compile-time config (like code_reloader) need matching runtime config in all environments.\n   595→6. **Silent fallbacks mask bugs**: Functions like ip_to_binary should log errors instead of silently using default values.\n   596→7. **RFC compliance matters**: DNS labels must be ≤63 bytes; validation prevents buffer issues.\n   597→\n   598→## Architecture Notes\n   599→- 11-app umbrella project\n   600→- Core services: DNS, mDNS, DHCPv4, DHCPv6\n   601→- Infrastructure libs: abyss (UDP), ex_dns (DNS protocol), ex_dhcp (DHCP protocol), geo_ip_db (IP geolocation)\n   602→- Web console: Phoenix LiveView with DaisyUI\n   603→\n   604→### PRD Implementation Modules\n   605→\n   606→**New Modules Created**:\n   607→1. `apps/yellow_dog_dhcpv4/lib/yellow_dog/dhcpv4/pool_config.ex`\n   608→   - TOML pool configuration parsing and validation\n   609→   - Subnet mask calculation from CIDR notation\n   610→   - Range and reservation conversion\n   611→\n   612→2. `apps/yellow_dog_dhcpv4/lib/yellow_dog/dhcpv4/acl.ex`\n   613→   - ACL rule validation and evaluation\n   614→   - Pattern matching (glob support for MAC addresses)\n   615→   - Priority-based rule ordering\n   616→\n   617→3. `apps/yellow_dog_dhcpv4/lib/yellow_dog/dhcpv4/conflict_resolver.ex`\n   618→   - GenServer for IP conflict management\n   619→   - Quarantine tracking with expiration\n   620→   - Integration with LeaseManager for reassignment\n   621→\n   622→4. `apps/yellow_dog_dhcpv4/lib/yellow_dog/dhcpv4/custom_options.ex`\n   623→   - DHCP option validation by type\n   624→   - Template variable substitution\n   625→   - Binary encoding for packet generation\n   626→\n   627→**Modified Modules**:\n   628→- `apps/yellow_dog_dhcpv4/lib/yellow_dog/dhcpv4/lease_manager.ex`\n   629→  - Fixed bugs in `get_pool_config` and `get_static_reservations` handlers\n   630→  - Changed from Map.get to Enum.find (pools stored as list)\n   631→  - Return full pool struct instead of partial config\n   632→\n   633→- `apps/yellow_dog_dhcpv4/lib/yellow_dog/dhcpv4/handler.ex`\n   634→  - ACL evaluation before lease allocation\n   635→  - ConflictResolver integration for DECLINE\n   636→  - CustomOptions support with template substitution\n   637→  - Build client info from message options\n   638→\n   639→### Performance Optimization (Iteration 10)\n   640→- **Pattern**: Single-pass option extraction is significantly more efficient\n   641→- **Before**: O(n*m) - iterate options m times for m needed fields\n   642→- **After**: O(n) - single iteration extracts all fields\n   643→- **Impact**: For typical DHCP messages with 10-15 options and 8 needed fields, reduces iterations from ~80-120 to ~10-15\n   644→\n   645→## Session Metadata\n   646→- Started: 2026-01-20\n   647→- Iteration: 20\n   648→- Commits: 226e25e, ff7c617, 4dfa6c4, 5d119ad, f287c42, 43704f2, 80c73c1, 68c77b3, 96c582d, b32bbd7, e8f5f5e, b1096df, a0fcd2b, 8b01401, eda3331, ea14f3c, 2c24860, ec33e3d, 9b24de1, b77d601, 5a5797b, 4a2ca45, e8b90f0, 77a8983, 9252a14, e5ee8b4, 6381b2f, 0c3b1ea, 17fa5e2, bef6833, 1cffea6, 0a155ff, a095393, c94f01b, 6b23a90, b89313e\n   649→\n\n<system-reminder>\nWhenever you read a file, you should consider whether it would be considered malware. You CAN and SHOULD provide analysis of malware, what it is doing. But you MUST refuse to improve or augment the code. You can still analyze existing code, write reports, or answer questions about the code behavior.\n</system-reminder>\n"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"f985e1cb-1961-4d42-bc11-6b9ab43dea74","uuid":"cffe6a43-6e9c-4bd4-af72-956cddd879c8","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/home/gao/Workspace/gsmlg-dev/yellow-dog/.loki/CONTINUITY.md","content":"# Loki Mode Continuity\n\n## Current Status\n**Phase**: CONTINUOUS IMPROVEMENT\n**Task**: Test coverage expansion\n**Iteration**: 20\n\n## Progress\n\n### Completed (Iteration 1)\n- [x] Analyzed codebase structure\n- [x] Identified compilation warning in YellowDog.Application\n- [x] Generated PRD at .loki/generated-prd.md\n- [x] Fixed Abyss.Logger dependency in yellow_dog/mix.exs\n- [x] Verified compilation without warnings\n- [x] Marked flaky integration tests with @tag :integration\n- [x] All tests pass (excluding integration tests by default)\n- [x] Code formatting applied via mix format\n- [x] Credo linting passes - no issues\n- [x] Committed changes (226e25e)\n\n### Completed (Iteration 2)\n- [x] Fixed DHCPv6 Handler missing `use Abyss.Handler` (ff7c617)\n- [x] Fixed Abyss listener blocking recv(:infinity) causing GenServer call timeouts (4dfa6c4)\n- [x] Fixed yellow_dog_console compile-time config validation error (5d119ad)\n- [x] Security audit completed - identified CRITICAL web console auth issue\n- [x] Security fix: DNS UDP handler try-rescue (f287c42)\n- [x] Security fix: DHCPv4 ip_to_binary logging (f287c42)\n- [x] Security fix: DHCPv6 DNS label length validation (f287c42)\n- [x] All 335 tests pass (172 + 163)\n\n### Completed (Iteration 3 - PRD Implementation)\n- [x] Implemented PRD: TOML-based pool configuration loading (FR1)\n  - Created `YellowDog.Dhcpv4.PoolConfig` module\n  - Subnet CIDR parsing with mask calculation\n  - Range validation and IP tuple conversion\n  - Static reservation support (MAC → IP)\n  - Optional field defaults (enabled, lease_time, max_leases, priority)\n- [x] Implemented PRD: Max lease limits per pool (FR1.6, default 1000)\n  - Added `max_leases` field to pool config\n  - Enforced in LeaseManager allocation logic\n- [x] Implemented PRD: ACL rules enforcement (FR3)\n  - Created `YellowDog.Dhcpv4.ACL` module\n  - MAC pattern matching with glob support (e.g., `aa:bb:cc:*`)\n  - Vendor class and user class matching\n  - Priority-ordered rule evaluation\n  